wn security vulnerabilities, so the dependency should be updated to a patched version. Once that security issue is resolved, the change should be in good shape.\n\n## 5325622630 pullfrog[bot]\n> ✅ No new issues found.\n\n**Reviewed changes** I reviewed commit `2fcf4157` against the full DevFn documentation-site diff.\n\n- **Finalized public URLs:** Set `https://devfn.com` as the canonical origin and served generated LLM resources under `/docs`.\n- **Shared site presentation:** Extracted the landing page into a reusable component and refined the search status message.\n- **Hardened content loading:** Parsed YAML frontmatter with `gray-matter`, removed fabricated asset timestamps, normalized control-file matching, and made initialization failures retryable.\n- **Strengthened validation:** Added shared runtime contract tests and a nonmutating generated-LLM artifact check, with a scoped resolver for the site's pinned DocsFn core.\n\nLocal builds and tests could not run because `npm ci` reports missing optional turbo platform packages in the root lockfile.\n\n<!--\nPullfrog review metadata. These findings were written against 2fcf4157;\nif commits have landed on codex/docs-devfn-20260926 since, treat every specific bug, file, or\nline callout as POTENTIALLY STALE and re-diff before acting on it.\n\n- Mode: IncrementalReview (delta against prior pullfrog review)\n- Files reviewed: 59\n- Commits reviewed: 4\n- Base: dev (7c6ec512)\n- Head: codex/docs-devfn-20260926 (2fcf4157)\n- Reviewed commits:\n  - 2fcf4157 — docs(devfn): finalize public URLs and shared site fixes\n  - 13f56183 — docs(devfn): correct lifecycle guarantees and shared loader behavior\n  - aabb7d6f — docs(devfn): fix site navigation and consumer guidance\n  - b84bae1b — docs(devfn): add DocsFn consumer site\n- Prior pullfrog review: 13f56183 (https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/212#pullrequestreview-5325500871)\n-->\n\n\n<!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ -->\n<sup><a href=\"https://pullfrog.