{"type":"message","id":"b7535ff0","parentId":"79d420ca","timestamp":"2026-10-06T11:26:52.926Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_9CSwmjvE6FmrXPELWXT7QsTb|fc_055fb762f51dfcfc016ac4dafbc59487d0815143d19c4edabf","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":" \n Common share-link patterns — one-time, time-bound, password-protected, IP-restricted.\n@@ -7751,7 +7759,7 @@\n \n # Tenant isolation\n \n-Source: https://filefn.superfunctions.dev/docs/recipes/tenant-isolation\n+Source: https://filefn.com/docs/recipes/tenant-isolation\n \n \n Per-tenant storage paths, quotas, grants, and authorization — the production isolation pattern.\n@@ -7891,7 +7899,7 @@\n \n # Video uploads\n \n-Source: https://filefn.superfunctions.dev/docs/recipes/video-uploads\n+Source: https://filefn.com/docs/recipes/video-uploads\n \n \n Large-file video uploads with multi-resolution transcoding, poster frames, and queued processing.\n@@ -7993,7 +8001,7 @@\n \n # Virus scanning\n \n-Source: https://filefn.superfunctions.dev/docs/recipes/virus-scanning\n+Source: https://filefn.com/docs/recipes/virus-scanning\n \n \n Plug ClamAV (or any AV provider) into the filefn processing pipeline as a custom processor.\n@@ -8113,7 +8121,7 @@\n \n # Reference\n \n-Source: https://filefn.superfunctions.dev/docs/reference\n+Source: https://filefn.com/docs/reference\n \n \n The canonical reference for filefn — every route, every error, every event, every schema, every config knob, the changelog.\n@@ -8142,7 +8150,7 @@\n \n # Changelog\n \n-Source: https://filefn.superfunctions.dev/docs/reference/changelog\n+Source: https://filefn.com/docs/reference/changelog\n \n \n Notable filefn releases and migration notes.\n@@ -8176,7 +8184,7 @@\n \n # Configuration\n \n-Source: https://filefn.superfunctions.dev/docs/reference/configuration\n+Source: https://filefn.com/docs/reference/configuration\n \n \n Every option in FileFnConfig — types, defaults, and effects.\n@@ -8190,7 +8198,7 @@\n \n | Field | Type | Effect |\n | --- | --- | --- |\n-| `db` | `Adapter` | The DB adapter (`@superfunctions/db`). |\n+| `database` | `Adapter` | The DB adapter (`@superfunctions/db`); `db` remains a deprecated alias. |\n | `storage` | `StorageAdapter` | The storage adapter (`@superfunctions/storage`). |\n \n ## Policies\n@@ -8227,7 +8235,8 @@\n | Field | Type | Default | Effect |\n | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n | `rateLimiter` | `RateLimiter` | undefined | Single global rate limiter. |\n-| `rateLimit.persistence` | `RateLimitPersistence` | undefined | Shared persistence (Redis/KV). |\n+| `stores` | `RuntimeStores` | undefined | Shared `atomicKv` / `kv` stores. |\n+| `rateLimit.mode` | `\"strict\" \\| \"best-effort\" \\| \"local\"` | inferred from stores | Strict requires CAS-capable `stores.atomicKv`; best-effort uses `stores.kv`; local keeps counters in-process. |\n | `rateLimit.algorithm` | `\"fixed-window\" | \"sliding-window\" | \"token-bucket\"` | `\"fixed-window\"` | Algorithm. |\n | `rateLimit.limits.uploadInit` | `{ windowSeconds, maxRequests }` | undefined | Per-route. |\n | `rateLimit.limits.uploadSign` | same | undefined | |\n@@ -8258,13 +8267,13 @@\n | Field | Type | Default | Effect |\n | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n | `namespace` | `string` | `\"filefn\"` | Table prefix. |\n-| `logger` | `Logger` | undefined | Pluggable structured logger. |\n+| `observability` | `ObservabilityInput<FileFnObservationEvent>` | undefined | Structured logger, events, metrics, traces and request observations. |\n \n ## Example: production config\n \n ```ts\n const fileFn = createFileFn({\n-  db: createPostgresAdapter({ pool }),\n+  database: createPostgresAdapter({ pool }),\n   storage: createS3Storage({ region, bucket, cdnPrefix }),\n   policies: createNucleusPolicies(),\n \n@@ -8278,10 +8287,11 @@\n \n   quota: storageQuotaProvider,\n   authorizer: composeAuthorizers([orgAdminCanRead, createDefaultAuthorizer({ db, namespace: \"filefn\" })]),\n-  logger: pinoLogger,\n+  observability: { logger: pinoLogger },\n+  stores: { atomicKv: redisAtomicStore },\n \n   rateLimit: {\n-    persistence: redisPersistence,\n+    mode: \"strict\",\n     algorithm: \"sliding-window\",\n     limits: {\n       uploadInit:        { windowSeconds: 60, maxRequests: 10 },\n@@ -8319,7 +8329,7 @@\n \n # Envelopes\n \n-Source: https://filefn.superfunctions.dev/docs/reference/envelopes\n+Source: https://filefn.com/docs/reference/envelopes\n \n \n The success and error wrapper every filefn route returns.\n@@ -8421,7 +8431,7 @@\n \n # Errors\n \n-Source: https://filefn.superfunctions.dev/docs/reference/errors\n+Source: https://filefn.com/docs/reference/errors\n \n \n Every filefn error code with its HTTP status, message, common causes, and fixes.\n@@ -8527,7 +8537,7 @@\n \n # Events\n \n-Source: https://filefn.superfunctions.dev/docs/reference/events\n+Source: https://filefn.com/docs/reference/events\n \n \n Every filefn event with its payload, when it fires, and what's redacted.\n@@ -8603,7 +8613,7 @@\n \n # Routes\n \n-Source: https://filefn.superfunctions.dev/docs/reference/routes\n+Source: https://filefn.com/docs/reference/routes\n \n \n Every HTTP route filefn exposes — methods, paths, request shapes, response shapes, error codes.\n@@ -8713,7 +8723,7 @@\n \n # Schema\n \n-Source: https://filefn.superfunctions.dev/docs/reference/schema\n+Source: https://filefn.com/docs/reference/schema\n \n \n Every filefn DB table — columns, types, indexes — and how to migrate them.\n@@ -8867,7 +8877,7 @@\n \n # SDKs\n \n-Source: https://filefn.superfunctions.dev/docs/sdk\n+Source: https://filefn.com/docs/sdk\n \n \n TypeScript server, browser client, Python kernel, native Swift package, viewer resolver, and WKWebView bridge — every filefn SDK speaks the same routes and envelopes.\n@@ -8903,7 +8913,7 @@\n \n # @filefn/client\n \n-Source: https://filefn.superfunctions.dev/docs/sdk/client\n+Source: https://filefn.com/docs/sdk/client\n \n \n The browser / Node / Bun / Deno client SDK — uploadFile, resumeUpload, resolveRenderable, OPFS offline, HEIC preprocessing.\n@@ -9129,7 +9139,7 @@\n \n # filefn (Python)\n \n-Source: https://filefn.superfunctions.dev/docs/sdk/python\n+Source: https://filefn.com/docs/sdk/python\n \n \n The Python kernel — create_file_fn, FileFnConfig, processors, providers.\n@@ -9286,7 +9296,7 @@\n \n # @filefn/server\n \n-Source: https://filefn.superfunctions.dev/docs/sdk/server\n+Source: https://filefn.com/docs/sdk/server\n \n \n The Node / Bun / Workers server kernel — createFileFn, FileProvider, Authorizer, QuotaProvider, and processor authoring.\n@@ -9312,6 +9322,7 @@\n interface FileFn extends FileProvider {\n   router: FileFnRouter;                                  // single Request → Response | null\n   events: FileFnEventEmitter;                            // typed event emitter\n+  readonly services: FileFnServices;                     // bound, authorized domain services\n   definePolicy(name: string, policy: Omit<Policy, \"name\">): void;\n   getSchema(): { version: number; schemas: TableSchema[] };\n }\n@@ -9321,14 +9332,15 @@\n \n | Field | Type | Default | Notes |\n | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n-| `db` | `Adapter` | required | `@superfunctions/db` `Adapter`. |\n+| `database` | `Adapter` | required | `@superfunctions/db` `Adapter`; FileFn applies its own schema. `db` remains a deprecated alias. |\n | `storage` | `StorageAdapter` | required | `@superfunctions/storage` `StorageAdapter`. |\n+| `stores` | `RuntimeStores` | undefined | Shared runtime stores, including `atomicKv` for strict rate limiting and `kv` for best-effort counters. |\n | `policies` | `Policy[]` | `[]` | Initial policies. Use `createNucleusPolicies()` for sane defaults. |\n | `auth` | `AuthConfig` | `{}` | `{ resolveSession, required }`. |\n | `quota` | `QuotaProvider` | undefined | Optional storage quota. |\n | `rateLimiter` | `RateLimiter` | undefined | Single global rate limiter. |\n-| `rateLimit` | `{ persistence?, algorithm?, limits? }` | undefined | Per-route rate limits. |\n-| `logger` | `Logger` | undefined | Pluggable structured logger. |\n+| `rateLimit` | `{ mode?, algorithm?, limits? }` | undefined | Per-route rate limits; mode is `\"strict\"`, `\"best-effort\"`, or `\"local\"`. |\n+| `observability` | `ObservabilityInput<FileFnObservationEvent>` | undefined | Shared logging, typed events, metrics, traces and request observations. |\n | `authorizer` | `Authorizer` | default | Permission resolution. |\n | `namespace` | `string` | `\"filefn\"` | Table prefix. |\n | `defaultChunkSizeBytes` | `number` | `5 MiB` | Multipart chunk floor. |\n@@ -9337,6 +9349,24 @@\n | `dedup` | `{ enabled: boolean }` | `{ enabled: false }` | Content-addressable storage. |\n | `processing` | `{ enabled, processors?, flowFn? }` | `{ enabled: false }` | Processing pipeline. |\n \n+## Migrating from 0.1.x\n+\n+Version 0.2.0 removes `FileFnConfig.logger` and `rateLimit.persistence`; there\n+are no compatibility aliases for these options.\n+\n+- Replace `logger` with `observability: { logger }`, using a logger compatible\n+  with `@superfunctions/observability`.\n+- Replace `rateLimit.persistence` with `stores.kv` and\n+  `rateLimit.mode: \"best-effort\"` when cross-replica limits may be approximate.\n+- For strict shared limits, provide a CAS-capable `stores.atomicKv` and set\n+  `rateLimit.mode: \"strict\"`. Missing atomic storage is rejected.\n+- For process-local counters, use `rateLimit.mode: \"local\"`.\n+\n+Without an explicit mode, FileFn selects strict when `stores.atomicKv` is\n+present, otherwise best-effort when `stores.kv` is present, otherwise local.\n+The separate pre-built `rateLimiter` option remains supported.\n+\n+\n ## `FileProvider`\n \n `FileFn` implements [`@superfunctions/files`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@superfunctions/files)' `FileProvider`. You can call it programmatically without going through HTTP:\n@@ -9354,6 +9384,32 @@\n ```\n \n `ctx` carries the principal — `{ principalId, tenantId, uploadSessionToken }`.\n+\n+## Bound domain services\n+\n+The public `FileFn.services` bundle is available in `@filefn/server` 0.2.0.\n+It contains `files`, `uploads`, `grants`, `shares`, `processing`, and `policies`.\n+These are the same instances used by the facade and router, bound to the same\n+schema, namespace, database, storage, policies, quota provider, and event emitter.\n+No separately constructed service or table access is needed.\n+\n+```ts\n+const { versions } = await fileFn.services.files.listVersions(fileId, ctx);\n+const grants = await fileFn.services.grants.listGrants(fileId, ctx);\n+const artifacts = await fileFn.services.processing.listArtifactsForFile(fileId, ctx);\n+await fileFn.services.processing.triggerProcessingForFile(fileId, ctx, versionId);\n+```\n+\n+All file operations still require the caller's domain principal/tenant context.\n+Grant management remains owner-only; share management and artifact access retain\n+their existing domain checks. The bound processing surface intentionally does\n+not expose `runProcessing` or a trigger accepting caller-supplied storage keys:\n+`triggerProcessingForFile` authorizes the file/version and resolves the input\n+from FileFn before scheduling work.\n+\n+`@filefn/admin` requires this declared server version. Its\n+`createFileFnDomainAdminService({ fileFn, context })` maps each active admin\n+actor/scope to FileFn's domain context rather than bypassing these checks.\n \n ## Routes\n \n@@ -9486,7 +9542,7 @@\n \n # Swift\n \n-Source: https://filefn.superfunctions.dev/docs/sdk/swift\n+Source: https://filefn.com/docs/sdk/swift\n \n \n The native Swift Package Manager target — FileFnClient, foreground / background uploaders, SwiftUI helpers, secret-store-backed token recovery.\n@@ -9681,7 +9737,7 @@\n \n # Swift bridge\n \n-Source: https://filefn.superfunctions.dev/docs/sdk/swift-bridge\n+Source: https://filefn.com/docs/sdk/swift-bridge\n \n \n Native-backed WKWebView bridge — FileFnWebViewBridgeHost on the Swift side, @filefn/swift-bridge on the JS side, with asset-handle uploads and bridge-scheme previews.\n@@ -9818,7 +9874,7 @@\n \n # @filefn/viewer\n \n-Source: https://filefn.superfunctions.dev/docs/sdk/viewer\n+Source: https://filefn.com/docs/sdk/viewer\n \n \n Framework-agnostic render-intent resolver utilities for filefn clients.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1791286012926}}
