ew-20260930/sequential-20261003T184612Z/PR-212/frozen-novel-human-source.patch","offset":301,"limit":300}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-6.1-sol","usage":{"input":5069,"output":381,"cacheRead":125952,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":314,"totalTokens":131402,"cost":{"input":0.010138,"output":0.0038100000000000005,"cacheRead":0.0125952,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.026543200000000003}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1791286037344,"responseId":"resp_055fb762f51dfcfc016ac4db17a40487d09600e6a9335aa8c1","rawStopReason":"completed","thinkingLevel":"high"}}
{"type":"message","id":"517887a5","parentId":"0c58987f","timestamp":"2026-10-06T11:27:39.374Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_0H5AMjTPliQOFnJ2wZWWIrC4|fc_055fb762f51dfcfc016ac4db2a1bb487d0b99eec743beba32b","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"index 000000000..2d8165378\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/devfn/docs/content/docs/reference/compose.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,6 @@\n+---\n+title: \"@devfn/compose\"\n+description: Source package guide for @devfn/compose.\n+---\n+\n+Requires Docker Compose 2.24.4 or newer. Starts only declared Compose services with `--no-deps` under a worktree-specific project name, replaces source mappings with loopback or explicitly public DevFn host-port mappings while retaining conventional container ports, and never removes persistent volumes during ordinary cleanup. Secret-bearing services disable Docker log persistence.\ndiff --git a/devfn/docs/content/docs/reference/config.md b/devfn/docs/content/docs/reference/config.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 000000000..27867cdf1\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/devfn/docs/content/docs/reference/config.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,6 @@\n+---\n+title: \"@devfn/config\"\n+description: Source package guide for @devfn/config.\n+---\n+\n+Validated DevFn project manifests and organization port-policy contracts. Every manifest can declare lifecycle commands and must be reviewed and explicitly trusted before the DevFn CLI loads its exact digest; executable manifests additionally must be self-contained.\ndiff --git a/devfn/docs/content/docs/reference/configuration.md b/devfn/docs/content/docs/reference/configuration.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 000000000..26da23585\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/devfn/docs/content/docs/reference/configuration.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,70 @@\n+---\n+title: Configuration contract\n+description: Manifest fields, ports, processes, services, profiles, and policy.\n+---\n+\n+DevFn discovers `devfn.config.ts`, `.js`, `.mjs`, `.cjs`, or `.json` while walking upward from the current directory. JavaScript-family manifests are executable code, require digest-bound trust, and must be self-contained (no imports or `require()`). JSON is data-only.\n+\n+## Top-level manifest\n+\n+| Field | Required | Meaning |\n+| --- | --- | --- |\n+| `version: 1` | yes | Manifest schema version. |\n+| `project.id` | yes | Stable semantic project identity. |\n+| `project.name` | no | Human display name. |\n+| `defaultProfile` | no | Profile selected when `--profile` is omitted. Without it, a `profiles.default` entry is required. |\n+| `runtimeDir` | no | Repository-relative generated-state root; defaults to `.devfn`. |\n+| `ports` | no | Named `PortSpec` map. |\n+| `processes` | no | Named native process map. |\n+| `services` | no | Named Docker Compose service map. |\n+| `profiles` | yes | Named selections of processes/services plus non-secret environment and proxy choice. |\n+| `hostnames` | no | Explicit local hostname routes to named ports. |\n+| `prerequisites` | no | Required command/version diagnostics, optionally profile-scoped. |\n+| `environmentOutputs` | no | Repository-relative dotenv or JSON runtime files and owner-only permission modes. |\n+| `policy` | no | Repository-relative organization policy JSON path. |\n+\n+Every repository-relative path rejects absolute paths, `..` escape, and runtime symlink escape. Validation resolves process/service dependencies, port references, profile selections, the default profile, and hostname targets/profile filters. It does not validate `prerequisites[].profiles` against known profiles; an unknown name silently skips that prerequisite in `doctor`. Check these filters explicitly. An explicitly configured but missing policy is an error; only the conventional unconfigured policy path is optional.\n+\n+## Ports\n+\n+A port can specify `protocol` (`tcp` or `udp`), `preferred`, `range: [start, end]`, `exact`, `ephemeral`, `exposure` (`loopback` or `public`), conventional container `internal` port, contiguous `block` name, and exported `env` key.\n+\n+- `exact: true` requires `preferred` and fails closed on collision.\n+- `ephemeral: true` cannot be combined with fixed preferences.\n+- Requirements sharing `block` receive a contiguous allocation.\n+- Public ports require `devfn up --allow-public`.\n+\n+## Native processes\n+\n+`adapter` is one of `command`, `npm`, `pnpm`, `turbo`, `wrangler`, `xcode`, or `extfn`. A process can specify `command`, package-manager `script`, repository-relative `cwd`, non-secret literal `env`, inherited `envAllowlist`, redacted `secretEnv`, named `ports`, `dependsOn`, `health`, `shutdownTimeoutMs`, and `exposure` (`local` or `public`).\n+\n+Turbo, Wrangler, and ExtFn resolve project-local binaries with offline npm execution; pnpm runs through Corepack so the repository's `packageManager` pin is honored. Adapters never download a missing tool during startup. `doctor` reports the missing prerequisite instead. Discovery marks Yarn and Bun as proposed and emits no guessed npm process; add an explicit command adapter after review.\n+\n+Local-process exposure verification requires `lsof` on macOS and Linux; Windows uses `netstat`. Run `devfn doctor` before startup to detect a missing listener-inspection tool.\n+\n+Sensitive-looking keys cannot be literal manifest values. They must be inherited by name in `envAllowlist` and repeated in `secretEnv`, which activates streaming redaction before logs are persisted. This is a key-name safeguard, not general secret detection; reviewers must inspect all other literal values. Public processes require `--allow-public`.\n+\n+## Compose services\n+\n+A service uses `adapter: \"compose\"`, Compose `service`, optional repository-relative `file`, project-name prefix, named host-port-to-container-port mappings, dependencies, health, `persistent`, non-secret `env`, `envAllowlist`, and `secretEnv`. DevFn always adds the worktree instance suffix to the Compose project name.\n+\n+DevFn writes a generated override with loopback host mappings unless the named port explicitly selects public exposure. It starts only the requested service with `--no-deps`. Services declaring `secretEnv` use Docker's `none` logging driver and therefore cannot use log-pattern health checks. Ordinary cleanup stops/removes only invocation-owned containers and never passes a volume-deletion flag.\n+\n+## Health checks\n+\n+- HTTP: `{ type: \"http\", port: \"app\", path: \"/health\", expectedStatus: 200, timeoutMs: 120000 }`\n+- TCP: `{ type: \"tcp\", port: \"postgres\" }`\n+- Command: `{ type: \"command\", command: [\"node\", \"scripts/ready.mjs\"] }`\n+- Log: `{ type: \"log\", pattern: \"ready on\" }`\n+\n+HTTP URLs are returned only for explicitly routed hostnames or ports named by HTTP health checks. Other services remain transport allocations visible through `devfn ports`; DevFn does not invent an HTTP URL for a database or arbitrary TCP listener.\n+\n+## Profiles and hostnames\n+\n+Profiles select named processes/services, add non-secret environment, and opt into the shared proxy with `proxy: true`. Dependencies are included transitively and started topologically. Cycles fail before mutation.\n+\n+A hostname maps a route name to `target`, optional `hostname` template, `tls` (`off` or `internal`), and optional `profiles` filter. Templates accept `{project}` and `{instance}`. Every resolved name must end in `.localhost`.\n+\n+## Organization policy\n+\n+`devfn.policy.json` supports `fallbackRange`, `hostnameSuffix`, and entries with `name`, exactly one of `port`/`range`, `kind` (`protected`, `preferred`, or `excluded`), optional `project`, and `description`. `devfn ports report` combines the policy with the entire machine registry into Markdown; it is not limited to the current project or profile. `--output` must remain inside the repository.\ndiff --git a/devfn/docs/content/docs/reference/core.md b/devfn/docs/content/docs/reference/core.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 000000000..f777f4bc7\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/devfn/docs/content/docs/reference/core.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,6 @@\n+---\n+title: \"@devfn/core\"\n+description: Source package guide for @devfn/core.\n+---\n+\n+Builds dependency-ordered lifecycle plans, reserves ports before mutation, starts Compose and native resources, verifies readiness, registers shared proxy routes, emits machine-readable receipts, and rolls back only resources created by the failing invocation.\ndiff --git a/devfn/docs/content/docs/reference/index.md b/devfn/docs/content/docs/reference/index.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 000000000..30947bb0e\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/devfn/docs/content/docs/reference/index.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,14 @@\n+---\n+title: Reference\n+description: DevFn configuration, security, migration, and package guides.\n+---\n+\n+The reference pages mirror existing source guides:\n+\n+- [Configuration contract](/docs/reference/configuration)\n+- [Security contract](/docs/reference/security)\n+- [Migration guide](/docs/reference/migration)\n+- [CLI](/docs/reference/cli), [core](/docs/reference/core), [config](/docs/reference/config)\n+- [Ports](/docs/reference/ports), [processes](/docs/reference/processes), [Compose](/docs/reference/compose), [proxy](/docs/reference/proxy), [testing](/docs/reference/testing)\n+\n+Keep source and site copies aligned when changing a public contract.\ndiff --git a/devfn/docs/content/docs/reference/meta.json b/devfn/docs/content/docs/reference/meta.json\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 000000000..6b6984e1c\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/devfn/docs/content/docs/reference/meta.json\n@@ -0,0 +1,4 @@\n+{\n+  \"title\": \"Reference\",\n+  \"pages\": [\"index\", \"configuration\", \"security\", \"migration\", \"cli\", \"core\", \"config\", \"ports\", \"processes\", \"compose\", \"proxy\", \"testing\"]\n+}\ndiff --git a/devfn/docs/content/docs/reference/migration.md b/devfn/docs/content/docs/reference/migration.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 000000000..a08facb4e\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/devfn/docs/content/docs/reference/migration.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,16 @@\n+---\n+title: Migration guide\n+description: Adopt DevFn without losing existing scripts, outputs, or Compose data.\n+---\n+\n+1. Preserve all existing scripts and Compose data.\n+2. Run `devfn init`, inspect confirmed versus proposed detections, then rerun with `--yes` only when the preview is truthful.\n+3. Edit the manifest so every command, dependency, port, profile, and health check is explicit.\n+4. Run `devfn doctor --trust`; address missing runtimes and exact-port conflicts.\n+5. Before the first start, back up every pre-existing file targeted by `environmentOutputs[].path`; DevFn overwrites configured outputs and cannot restore prior contents.\n+6. Before the first start, inspect the resolved Compose configuration and verify that each database mounts the intended existing volume. DevFn adds a worktree-specific project suffix, so an ordinary project-scoped named volume may resolve to a different, empty volume. Back up existing database contents and any data stored only in container writable layers; `down` removes DevFn-created containers.\n+7. Start with a minimal profile and compare it with the existing manual startup flow.\n+8. Add full, OAuth, test, or docs profiles incrementally. Public tunnels must remain explicit.\n+9. Verify `devfn down` preserves databases and volumes before adopting it as the daily command.\n+\n+Rollback by running `devfn down`, then inspect `runtimeDir` and every `environmentOutputs[].path` in the manifest before removing generated files. The default generated location is `.devfn/`, but custom paths may live elsewhere. Preserve any target that existed before DevFn adoption; cleanup does not know whether a configured output replaced user-owned content. Finally remove the DevFn manifest and continue using the preserved original scripts. Docker volumes and source configuration are not deleted.\ndiff --git a/devfn/docs/content/docs/reference/ports.md b/devfn/docs/content/docs/reference/ports.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 000000000..789ddb854\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/devfn/docs/content/docs/reference/ports.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,6 @@\n+---\n+title: \"@devfn/ports\"\n+description: Source package guide for @devfn/ports.\n+---\n+\n+Machine-local, lock-protected port leases with worktree instance identity, exact/preferred/range/ephemeral allocation, stale reconciliation, listener discovery, Docker mapping discovery, and generated inventory reports. Reports enumerate the complete machine registry, including other projects and profiles, and are not a current-selection view.\ndiff --git a/devfn/docs/content/docs/reference/processes.md b/devfn/docs/content/docs/reference/processes.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 000000000..ed28b7302\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/devfn/docs/content/docs/reference/processes.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,6 @@\n+---\n+title: \"@devfn/processes\"\n+description: Source package guide for @devfn/processes.\n+---\n+\n+Native process groups, durable logs, HTTP/TCP/command/log readiness, PID-birth ownership checks, and graceful termination. It is deliberately browser- and artifact-model-neutral so ProbeFn can adopt it later without depending on DevFn orchestration.\ndiff --git a/devfn/docs/content/docs/reference/proxy.md b/devfn/docs/content/docs/reference/proxy.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 000000000..fa250941d\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/devfn/docs/content/docs/reference/proxy.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,6 @@\n+---\n+title: \"@devfn/proxy\"\n+description: Source package guide for @devfn/proxy.\n+---\n+\n+Maintains one lock-protected, DevFn-owned Caddy route registry. Generated configurations contain concrete `.localhost` routes and loopback targets only, are validated before reload, and never include a catch-all. If another Caddy owns the admin endpoint, DevFn refuses to replace its configuration.\ndiff --git a/devfn/docs/content/docs/reference/security.md b/devfn/docs/content/docs/reference/security.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 000000000..41647948d\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/devfn/docs/content/docs/reference/security.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,14 @@\n+---\n+title: Security contract\n+description: Manifest trust, secret handling, local exposure, and ownership.\n+---\n+\n+- Every DevFn manifest can declare lifecycle commands, so the CLI refuses to load JSON, TypeScript, or JavaScript until the user records trust for its exact digest with `--trust`. JSON is parsed directly from the verified bytes; executable manifests run from a private copy of those same bytes and must be self-contained, with imports and `require()` rejected so dependency files cannot bypass the digest boundary.\n+- Runtime children inherit a small base environment plus explicit `envAllowlist` entries. Sensitive-looking keys must also be listed in `secretEnv`; a detached wrapper redacts those effective values before native-process logs are persisted. Literal values are rejected only when their key looks sensitive, so review every manifest literal. Compose logging is disabled for services with `secretEnv` because Docker otherwise retains historical unredacted logs. Inherited `secretEnv` values are not persisted in the registry or lifecycle receipt. Managed-process command arguments are serialized verbatim in receipts, so never embed credentials in command arguments; supply them through the explicitly allowed secret environment instead.\n+- Generated environment and state files use owner-only modes (default `0600`); their directories use `0700`. Existing files are explicitly re-permissioned after each write.\n+- Local ports and proxy targets bind to loopback unless a manifest explicitly selects public exposure. Profiles containing public processes or ports require the separate `--allow-public` confirmation on every start. A public Cloudflare tunnel must never be inferred.\n+- Repository-relative process, Compose, runtime, policy, and output paths are validated against lexical and symlink path escape.\n+- PID ownership uses a birth signature where the host exposes one. DevFn refuses to stop a reused PID.\n+- `down` stops only the exact worktree instance. Ordinary shutdown removes no persistent Docker volumes.\n+- Project hostnames must be concrete `.localhost` names. DevFn manages only a Caddy process it started itself and refuses to overwrite an unrelated Caddy admin endpoint.\n+- Volume deletion, database reset, public tunnels, and other destructive operations are outside ordinary lifecycle commands and require separate explicit tooling and confirmation.\ndiff --git a/devfn/docs/content/docs/reference/testing.md b/devfn/docs/content/docs/reference/testing.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 000000000..ac3113334\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/devfn/docs/content/docs/reference/testing.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,6 @@\n+---\n+title: \"@devfn/testing\"\n+description: Source package guide for @devfn/testing.\n+---\n+\n+Deterministic fixture manifests, temporary projects, and fake listeners for allocator, lifecycle, crash-recovery, and CLI contract tests.\ndiff --git a/devfn/docs/content/docs/security.md b/devfn/docs/content/docs/security.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 000000000..70947b8b5\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/devfn/docs/content/docs/security.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,10 @@\n+---\n+title: Trust and secret handling\n+description: Review manifests, isolate secrets, and confirm public exposure.\n+---\n+\n+Every manifest can declare lifecycle commands. DevFn requires explicit trust for its exact digest before first load and after edits, including JSON manifests. Executable manifests run from a private verified copy and cannot import other files, closing a dependency escape around the digest check.\n+\n+Runtime children inherit a small base environment plus named `envAllowlist` entries. Sensitive-looking names must also appear in `secretEnv` so effective values are redacted before native logs persist. The literal-key safeguard is not full secret detection; inspect all manifest literals. Compose services with `secretEnv` use Docker's `none` logging driver. Runtime directories and files default to owner-only modes.\n+\n+Ports and proxy targets bind to loopback unless the manifest explicitly selects public exposure; `--allow-public` is an additional confirmation on every start. DevFn does not infer a public tunnel. `down` stops only owned instance resources and does not delete persistent volumes. Read the [full security contract](/docs/reference/security) before using DevFn with sensitive data.\ndiff --git a/devfn/docs/content/pages/.gitkeep b/devfn/docs/content/pages/.gitkeep\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 000000000..e69de29bb\ndiff --git a/devfn/docs/docsfn.config.ts b/devfn/docs/docsfn.config.ts\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 000000000..bfb1b33b3\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/devfn/docs/docsfn.config.ts\n@@ -0,0 +1,36 @@\n+import type { DocsConfig } from \"@docsfn/core\";\n+\n+const config: DocsConfig = {\n+  schemaVersion: 1,\n+  site: {\n+    title: \"DevFn\",\n+    description: \"Trusted local profiles, process and Compose lifecycle, port leases, readiness, and localhost routes.\",\n+    basePath: \"/docs\",\n+    editLink: { pattern: \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/edit/dev/devfn/docs/{path}\" },\n+  },\n+  compat: { preset: \"none\" },\n+  content: {\n+    root: \".\",\n+    docsDir: \"content/docs\",\n+    pagesDir: \"content/pages\",\n+    blogDir: \"content/blog\",\n+    apiDir: \"content/api\",\n+    assetsDir: \"static\",\n+    metaFileName: \"meta.json\",\n+  },\n+  navigation: {\n+    topNav: [\n+      { label: \"Docs\", href: \"/docs\" },\n+      { label: \"Packages\", href: \"/docs/reference\" },\n+      { label: \"GitHub\", href: \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/tree/dev/devfn\", external: true },\n+    ],\n+    sidebars: {\n+      docs: { title: \"Documentation\", root: true, include: [\"docs/**\"] },\n+    },\n+  },\n+  search: { enabled: true, scopes: [\"docs\"], bodyIndexing: \"summary\" },\n+  auth: { enabled: false, mode: \"public\" },\n+  analytics: { enabled: false, provider: \"watchfn\", respectDnt: true },\n+};\n+\n+export default config;\ndiff --git a/devfn/docs/package.json b/devfn/docs/package.json\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 000000000..a5682edee\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/devfn/docs/package.json\n@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@\n+{\n+  \"name\": \"@devfn/docs\",\n+  \"version\": \"0.0.1\",\n\n[1143 more lines in file. Use offset=601 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1791286059374}}
{"type":"message","id":"ace60d12","parentId":"517887a5","timestamp":"2026-10-06T11:27:42.563Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_iy2tmIpEBS4KdctoeFzskQRE|fc_055fb762f51dfcfc016ac4db2d8b9887d08287c4a2bc3c5c33","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/audits/sf-docs-review-20260930/sequential-20261003T184612Z/PR-212/frozen-novel-human-source.patch","offset":601,"limit":300}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-6.1-sol","usage":{"input":5201,"output":65,"cacheRead":130816,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":136082,"cost":{"input":0.010402,"output":0.0006500000000000001,"cacheRead":0.0130816,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.024133599999999998}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1791286059381,"responseId":"resp_055fb762f51dfcfc016ac4db2be85887d085c4ba6de736e52e","rawStopReason":"completed","thinkingLevel":"high"}}
{"type":"message","id":"52dcc83d","parentId":"ace60d12","timestamp":"2026-10-06T11:27:42.565Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_iy2tmIpEBS4KdctoeFzskQRE|fc_055fb762f51dfcfc016ac4db2d8b9887d08287c4a2bc3c5c33","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"+  \"private\": true,\n+  \"type\": \"module\",\n+  \"scripts\": {\n+    \"dev\": \"vite dev --port 6017\",\n+    \"build\": \"vite build\",\n+    \"preview\": \"vite preview --port 6017\",\n+    \"test\": \"npm run check:llms && vitest run --config ../../scripts/docs-site/vitest.config.ts\",\n+    \"generate:llms\": \"node scripts/generate-llms.mjs\",\n+    \"prebuild\": \"npm run generate:llms\",\n+    \"check:llms\": \"node scripts/generate-llms.mjs --check\"\n+  },\n+  \"dependencies\": {\n+    \"@21n/fonts\": \"^1.0.1\",\n+    \"@docsfn/core\": \"0.0.5\",\n+    \"@docsfn/provider-fs\": \"0.0.2\",\n+    \"@docsfn/svelte\": \"0.0.3\",\n+    \"@docsfn/sveltekit\": \"0.0.2\",\n+    \"gray-matter\": \"^4.0.3\"\n+  },\n+  \"devDependencies\": {\n+    \"@docsfn/cli\": \"0.0.2\",\n+    \"@sveltejs/adapter-auto\": \"^3.0.0\",\n+    \"@sveltejs/adapter-cloudflare\": \"^7.0.0\",\n+    \"@sveltejs/kit\": \"^2.0.0\",\n+    \"@sveltejs/vite-plugin-svelte\": \"^5.1.1\",\n+    \"@tailwindcss/vite\": \"^4.0.0\",\n+    \"@types/node\": \"^20.0.0\",\n+    \"svelte\": \"^5.55.7\",\n+    \"tailwindcss\": \"^4.0.0\",\n+    \"typescript\": \"^5.0.0\",\n+    \"vite\": \"^6.4.3\",\n+    \"vitest\": \"^3.2.4\"\n+  }\n+}\ndiff --git a/devfn/docs/scripts/generate-llms.mjs b/devfn/docs/scripts/generate-llms.mjs\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 000000000..62bff8f82\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/devfn/docs/scripts/generate-llms.mjs\n@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@\n+#!/usr/bin/env node\n+import { dirname, resolve } from \"node:path\";\n+import { fileURLToPath } from \"node:url\";\n+import { buildLlmsTxtArtifacts, buildManifest, loadDocsConfig } from \"@docsfn/core\";\n+import { FsContentProvider } from \"@docsfn/provider-fs\";\n+import { buildLlmsSiteArtifacts, withSourceLinks, writeLlmsArtifacts } from \"../../../scripts/docs-site/llms.mjs\";\n+\n+const cwd = resolve(dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), \"..\");\n+const deploymentOrigin = process.env.CLOUDFLARE_DOCS_DEPLOY === \"1\"\n+  ? process.env.CLOUDFLARE_DOCS_ASSETS_ORIGIN\n+  : undefined;\n+const { artifacts, manifest, canonicalUrl } = await buildLlmsSiteArtifacts(cwd, {\n+  buildLlmsTxtArtifacts, buildManifest, loadDocsConfig, FsContentProvider,\n+}, { canonicalUrl: deploymentOrigin });\n+artifacts.llmsTxt = withSourceLinks(artifacts.llmsTxt, manifest, \"devfn\", canonicalUrl);\n+artifacts.llmsFullTxt = withSourceLinks(artifacts.llmsFullTxt, manifest, \"devfn\", canonicalUrl);\n+const generatedFooter = \"For programmatic access, prefer the MCP server\\nor the structured manifest emitted alongside this file.\";\n+if (!artifacts.llmsFullTxt.includes(generatedFooter)) {\n+  throw new Error(\"Unexpected DocsFn llms-full footer; review the generated artifact before publishing\");\n+}\n+artifacts.llmsFullTxt = artifacts.llmsFullTxt.replace(generatedFooter, \"For a page index, see /docs/llms.txt.\");\n+writeLlmsArtifacts(resolve(cwd, \"static\"), artifacts);\ndiff --git a/devfn/docs/src/app.css b/devfn/docs/src/app.css\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 000000000..e1f0cfe06\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/devfn/docs/src/app.css\n@@ -0,0 +1,81 @@\n+@import \"@21n/fonts/styles.css\";\n+@import \"tailwindcss\";\n+@import \"@docsfn/svelte/theme.css\";\n+\n+/* Twenty One Native — same stack as @superfunctions/docs-theme / other monorepo docs */\n+:root {\n+  --docsfn-font-sans: \"Twenty One Native\", system-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\",\n+    Roboto, sans-serif;\n+  /* Tailwind v4 sets html { font-family: var(--default-font-family) } from --font-sans; align it */\n+  --font-sans: var(--docsfn-font-sans);\n+  /* Component theme uses --docsfn-color-* (see @docsfn/svelte theme.css), not --docsfn-primary */\n+  --docsfn-color-primary: hsl(154, 33%, 24%);\n+  --docsfn-color-primary-hover: hsl(154, 33%, 20%);\n+  --docsfn-color-accent-soft: hsl(154 33% 24% / 0.12);\n+  /*\n+   * TopBar is outside DocsLayout but uses position:sticky in theme.css.\n+   * Set this to roughly the rendered top bar height so the docs sidebar/TOC stick below it.\n+   */\n+  --docsfn-sticky-top-offset: 4rem;\n+\n+  /* Whole docs chrome (left sidebar + article + right TOC) max width; centers as a group */\n+  --docsfn-docs-shell-max-width: min(100rem, 100%);\n+\n+  /* Article column max inside the middle grid cell; justify-self:center centers it when capped */\n+  --docsfn-main-column-max-width: 48rem;\n+\n+  /* Sidebar column + full-bleed gutter to the left when the docs shell is centered */\n+  --docsfn-sidebar-panel-bg: #f4f4f5;\n+}\n+\n+@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {\n+  :root {\n+    --docsfn-sidebar-panel-bg: #232326;\n+    --docsfn-color-primary: hsl(155, 39%, 58%);\n+    --docsfn-color-primary-hover: hsl(155, 39%, 54%);\n+    --docsfn-color-accent-soft: hsl(155 39% 58% / 0.12);\n+  }\n+}\n+\n+/*\n+ * Tailwind @layer base wins over unscoped rules in the same file order for html — but unlayered\n+ * rules beat @layer. Force the document font so we are not stuck on ui-sans-serif / system-ui.\n+ */\n+html,\n+body {\n+  font-family: var(--docsfn-font-sans);\n+}\n+\n+/* ─── Site-specific layout (see @docsfn/svelte theme.css for defaults) ───── */\n+\n+/* Homepage / blog: keep top bar content centered with a comfortable max width */\n+.docsfn-topbar-container {\n+  max-width: var(--fd-layout-width, 1600px);\n+  margin-inline: auto;\n+  padding-inline: 1rem;\n+  box-sizing: border-box;\n+}\n+\n+/*\n+ * Docs routes: TopBar inner width matches the docs shell so nav lines up with the article column.\n+ * Same max-width as --docsfn-docs-shell-max-width + asymmetric padding = sidebar + main padding.\n+ */\n+@media (min-width: 1024px) {\n+  .docsfn-site-root.docsfn-docs-chrome .docsfn-topbar-container {\n+    max-width: var(--docsfn-docs-shell-max-width, none);\n+    margin-inline: auto;\n+    width: 100%;\n+    padding-left: calc(var(--docsfn-sidebar-width) + var(--docsfn-main-padding-inline));\n+    padding-right: var(--docsfn-main-padding-inline);\n+    box-sizing: border-box;\n+  }\n+}\n+\n+/* The published theme hides this column on mobile; an open drawer must override it. */\n+@media (max-width: 1023px) {\n+  .docsfn-site-root .docsfn-sidebar-col.docsfn-sidebar-col--open {\n+    display: block;\n+    top: var(--docsfn-sticky-top-offset);\n+    height: calc(100dvh - var(--docsfn-sticky-top-offset));\n+  }\n+}\ndiff --git a/devfn/docs/src/app.html b/devfn/docs/src/app.html\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 000000000..adf8bd873\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/devfn/docs/src/app.html\n@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@\n+<!doctype html>\n+<html lang=\"en\">\n+  <head>\n+    <meta charset=\"utf-8\" />\n+    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\" />\n+    %sveltekit.head%\n+  </head>\n+  <body data-sveltekit-preload-data=\"hover\">\n+    <div style=\"display: contents\">%sveltekit.body%</div>\n+  </body>\n+</html>\ndiff --git a/devfn/docs/src/lib/components/DocsSiteSearch.svelte b/devfn/docs/src/lib/components/DocsSiteSearch.svelte\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 000000000..ea239ce32\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/devfn/docs/src/lib/components/DocsSiteSearch.svelte\n@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@\n+<script lang=\"ts\">\n+  import Search from \"@site/docs-search\";\n+</script>\n+\n+<Search />\ndiff --git a/devfn/docs/src/lib/server/docs-site-source.ts b/devfn/docs/src/lib/server/docs-site-source.ts\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 000000000..c939aa36f\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/devfn/docs/src/lib/server/docs-site-source.ts\n@@ -0,0 +1,14 @@\n+import docsConfig from \"../../../docsfn.config\";\n+import { createDocsSiteRuntime } from \"../../../../../scripts/docs-site/runtime\";\n+\n+const content = import.meta.glob(\"../../../content/**/*\", {\n+  query: \"?raw\", import: \"default\", eager: true,\n+}) as Record<string, string>;\n+const 