{"type":"message","id":"62b62790","parentId":"08fd923e","timestamp":"2026-10-06T11:28:51.912Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_tcQXFQZGBpqcTmjze7q2ynXT|fc_055fb762f51dfcfc016ac4db72c29c87d0a33265c919f086e9","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"+- Local ports and proxy targets bind to loopback unless a manifest explicitly selects public exposure. Profiles containing public processes or ports require the separate `--allow-public` confirmation on every start. A public Cloudflare tunnel must never be inferred.\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>\n\n✅ Addressed in [`13f5618`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/13f561830279b4c40c8d095f2fdd38ff4c719bfa)\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNnc1 resolved=True devfn/docs/src/routes/+layout.server.ts\n<!-- cubic:v=bd00d907-64bf-41ee-8301-03486b6b0eaa -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=ce14b52f-6485-5594-8298-c25e4d334624 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":9} -->\nP2: Returning the full `source` sends every documentation page and the search artifact in the layout payload, even on routes that only need the site configuration. Return only client-needed layout fields and keep manifest/search processing server-side; the search artifact is already fetched separately.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At devfn/docs/src/routes/+layout.server.ts, line 6:\n\n<comment>Returning the full `source` sends every documentation page and the search artifact in the layout payload, even on routes that only need the site configuration. Return only client-needed layout fields and keep manifest/search processing server-side; the search artifact is already fetched separately.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -0,0 +1,8 @@\n+\n+export const load: LayoutServerLoad = async () => {\n+  return {\n+    source: await loadDocsSiteSource(),\n+  };\n+};\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>\n\n✅ Addressed in [`aabb7d6`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/aabb7d6f0d3147d010d061f4a461ff1ba6d059a8)\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNnc4 resolved=True devfn/docs/static/llms.txt\n<!-- cubic:v=5638b8b1-1b08-4013-bf6f-aa991a899023 -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=ce14b52f-6485-5594-8298-c25e4d334624 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":6} -->\nP3: The generated `llms.txt` links are origin-relative (`/docs/configuration`) because `site.canonicalUrl` is not set in `devfn/docs/docsfn.config.ts` — unlike authfn's docs site, which emits absolute URLs. Once committed and fetched by LLM clients, these paths have no resolvable host. Set `canonicalUrl` in the site config and regenerate the artifacts (via `npm --workspace @devfn/docs run generate:llms`), or hold off committing llms.txt until the public host is assigned.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At devfn/docs/static/llms.txt, line 7:\n\n<comment>The generated `llms.txt` links are origin-relative (`/docs/configuration`) because `site.canonicalUrl` is not set in `devfn/docs/docsfn.config.ts` — unlike authfn's docs site, which emits absolute URLs. Once committed and fetched by LLM clients, these paths have no resolvable host. Set `canonicalUrl` in the site config and regenerate the artifacts (via `npm --workspace @devfn/docs run generate:llms`), or hold off committing llms.txt until the public host is assigned.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@\n+\n+## Documentation\n+\n+- [Configuration](/docs/configuration) — Declare project identity, ports, processes, Compose services, and profiles.\n+- [Getting started](/docs/getting-started) — Initialize, trust, inspect, and start a local profile.\n+- [DevFn](/docs) — Trusted lifecycle orchestration for local development.\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>\n\n✅ Addressed in [`2fcf415`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/2fcf4157333b08d1c68a79cefb3a667bbfe642cc)\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNnc8 resolved=True devfn/docs/src/routes/docs/[...slug]/+page.server.ts\n<!-- cubic:v=555d6181-0d4c-4b46-ac96-08acaf7504a6 -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=ce14b52f-6485-5594-8298-c25e4d334624 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":6} -->\nP3: This API branch hardcodes `sidebarId: \"api\"`, but devfn's docsfn.config.ts only defines the `docs` sidebar, so `manifest.sidebars[\"api\"]` is undefined and API pages would render without the sidebar. Either add an `api` sidebar to docsfn.config.ts (as authfn/docs does) or drop the unused API branch.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At devfn/docs/src/routes/docs/[...slug]/+page.server.ts, line 65:\n\n<comment>This API branch hardcodes `sidebarId: \"api\"`, but devfn's docsfn.config.ts only defines the `docs` sidebar, so `manifest.sidebars[\"api\"]` is undefined and API pages would render without the sidebar. Either add an `api` sidebar to docsfn.config.ts (as authfn/docs does) or drop the unused API branch.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -0,0 +1,120 @@\n+        typeof api.frontmatter.description === \"string\" ? api.frontmatter.description : undefined,\n+      canonicalPath: route,\n+      canonicalUrl: buildCanonicalUrl(source.canonicalUrl, route),\n+      sidebarId: \"api\",\n+      headings: [],\n+      breadcrumbs: [\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>\n\n✅ Addressed in [`13f5618`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/13f561830279b4c40c8d095f2fdd38ff4c719bfa)\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNp6K resolved=True devfn/docs/package.json\n**Security issue**  \n🛑 Blocker — must fix before merge\n\n**Known vulnerabilities in svelte@5.0.0**\n\nOSV.dev reports 6 known vulnerabilities affecting `svelte@5.0.0`, introduced by this PR:\n\n- [GHSA-crpf-4hrx-3jrp](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-27125) **moderate**: Svelte SSR attribute spreading includes inherited properties from prototype chain — fixed in 5.51.5\n- [GHSA-f7gr-6p89-r883](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-27121) **moderate**: Svelte affected by cross-site scripting via spread attributes in Svelte SSR — fixed in 5.51.5\n- [GHSA-m56q-vw4c-c2cp](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-27122) **moderate**: Svelte SSR does not validate dynamic element tag names in `<svelte:element>` — fixed in 5.51.5\n\n…and 3 more — see the OSV links above.\n\nUpgrade to 5.51.5 or later.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn devfn/docs/package.json, upgrade the dependency svelte from 5.0.0 to a non-vulnerable version (5.51.5, 5.53.5, 5.55.7). Update any associated lockfile entries.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n> Not useful? Reply `@mira-rhombus reject` to dismiss this suggestion.\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNp6O resolved=True devfn/docs/src/lib/server/docs-site-source.ts\n**Refactor suggestion**  \n⚠️ Warning\n\n**Missing test coverage**\n\nThe PR introduces non-trivial logic across the new site — the bundled content provider, the hand-rolled `parseFrontmatter`, per-collection entry filtering, compiled-cache keying/lookup, and the route-resolution helpers in `docs/[...slug]/+page.server.ts` — but ships no test files, and the package's `test` script is `vitest run --passWithNoTests`, so zero assertions guard this code. At minimum, cover `parseFrontmatter` edge cases (missing closing fence, CRLF input, quoted values) and the collection filtering rules.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn the devfn/docs package, add a Vitest suite (for example src/lib/server/docs-site-source.test.ts and a companion file for src/routes/docs/[...slug]/+page.server.ts) covering parseFrontmatter edge cases (missing closing fence, CRLF frontmatter, quoted/unquoted values, boolean coercion), collectEntriesForCollection filtering (.gitkeep, meta.json, per-collection extensions), getCompiledArtifactOrThrow missing-key errors, and the route helpers buildCanonicalUrl, isRouteNotFoundError, and hasNestedDocsRoutes; wire the tests so `npm test` actually executes them instead of relying on --passWithNoTests.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n> Not useful? Reply `@mira-rhombus reject` to dismiss this suggestion.\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNp6R resolved=True devfn/docs/src/routes/docs/[...slug]/+page.server.ts\n**Error Handling**  \n⚠️ Warning\n\n**Type guard claims message without checking it**\n\nThe predicate type `input is { message: string }` promises a string `message`, but the check only inspects `code`. Any `DOCS_ROUTE_NOT_FOUND`-coded object whose `message` is missing or non-string passes the guard, and the catch block below then forwards a non-string to SvelteKit's `error(404, routeError.message)`. Verify `message` as part of the predicate.\n\n```suggestion\nfunction isRouteNotFoundError(input: unknown): input is { message: string } {\n  return (\n    typeof input === \"object\" &&\n    input !== null &&\n    \"code\" in input &&\n    String((input as { code: unknown }).code) === \"DOCS_ROUTE_NOT_FOUND\" &&\n    \"message\" in input &&\n    typeof (input as { message: unknown }).message === \"string\"\n  );\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn devfn/docs/src/routes/docs/[...slug]/+page.server.ts, update the isRouteNotFoundError guard (lines 22-30) to also verify that `message` exists and is a string before narrowing to { message: string } — e.g. add `\"message\" in input && typeof (input as { message: unknown }).message === \"string\"` — so error(404, routeError.message) never receives an undefined or non-string message.\n\nApply this code change:\n\nfunction isRouteNotFoundError(input: unknown): input is { message: string } {\n  return (\n    typeof input === \"object\" &&\n    input !== null &&\n    \"code\" in input &&\n    String((input as { code: unknown }).code) === \"DOCS_ROUTE_NOT_FOUND\" &&\n    \"message\" in input &&\n    typeof (input as { message: unknown }).message === \"string\"\n  );\n}\n```\n\n</details>\n\n> Not useful? Reply `@mira-rhombus reject` to dismiss this suggestion.\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNtlZ resolved=True devfn/docs/content/docs/getting-started.md\nOn a fresh project, this `init` call only prints a preview; it does not create `devfn.config.ts`, so the following `doctor --trust` fails with no manifest. Please show the required review-and-rerun step with `init --yes` before `doctor`, and align the CLI reference example.\n\n<details><summary>Technical details</summary>\n\n````markdown\n# Fresh-start command sequence does not create a manifest\n\n\n[431 more lines in file. Use offset=411 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1791286131912}}
