lifications,14 novel paths reviewed in the complete280-line producer-final novel patch (reads1–160/161–280). Frozen novel1742-line input was now visibly read completely in six bounded reads1–300/301–600/601–900/901–1200/1201–1500/1501–1742. This is post-use review and does not retroactively validate earlier truncated four-chunk claims or historical pre-use timing. Previously reviewed shared sources remain provenance reuse, not fresh whole5173/15242-line patch reading.\n\nReviewed all706 lines of the35-map readable lock comparison. Capture proves precisely these keys differ from42a; unrelated29 prerequisite maps and all other map values remain exact. Physical ordinary npm-ci passes with unchanged afe2b9c7db618ffbbb5c932a75baa5d404bf67689fcc31cfba3922546428938b. Real declared SearchFn peers/public exports, Vite6.4.3/plugin5 and Vitest^3.2.4/3.x policy retained; no broad normalization/peer bypass/metadata-only installation acceptance.\n\nNative generated amendment1744 lines reviewed through1–446/447–746/747–1096/1097–1446/1447–1744 (initial450 request truncated at446; continuation closes the gap). AuthFn index origin and five AI source changes follow executing config/native source. FileFn index/source header origin changes plus corpus repairs reproduce already reviewed42a database/stores/modes/observability/services source; no invented persistence aliases or caller-supplied processing-key access. Native nonwriting checks and HTTP exact bytes validate outputs, not manual generated edits. Unchanged DevFn generated bytes reuse frozen artifacts. No broad homepage-text rewriting or live hosting claim.\n\n## Coupled contracts\n\n- Unknown package input is shape-validated before export: malformed/nonconsumer cases retain the actual DevFn workspace hint, not TypeError; valid package admitted.\n- First-colon provider IDs/absolutePath, flat versus index sibling links and Unicode identity; full content remains server-owned; projected docs/API/sidebar/Blog surfaces and native /docs/blog/RSS/draft404 retained.\n- Consumer-resolved public exports/Kit/parser/search peers in six actual contexts, no parent application dependency borrowing or universal externalization.\n- Config and actual CLI select PUBLIC_ORIGIN only for DEPLOY=1; assets origin is not canonical fallback. Normal AuthFn/FileFn defaults .com; normal DevFn source-link fallback retained. buildLlmsSiteArtifacts canonical option AND returned canonical value retained.\n- Native search/TopBar/mobile drawer, single route/error titles, observer height/disconnect and reduced-motion positives preserved. Exposure hit testing uses an ordinary click at a verified backdrop point, not force/synthetic dispatch.\n- DevFn trust/secretEnv, init preview then --yes, machine state versus runtimeDir, prerequisite-profile limitation, existing-output backups and Compose volume/writable-layer warnings unchanged. No lifecycle/Docker/backend reimplementation.\n\n## Verification and limits\n\nLatest producer212-final receipts: six pristine builds, six46-Vitest+2-Node suites, six full tsc checks, six separate-process actual Vite search200/docs200/error404/single titles, six native preview LLM MIME/exact-byte checks, two hydrated DevFn search/focus/mobile/title browser checks; actual native CLI validation. Six executing SDK-config/CLI origin matrices cover assets-only/public/deployment-off with twelve static preimages restored byte/mode exact. OfflineCF dry-run passes; emitted Worker public-origin literals archived. Not local Worker execution or live upload proof.\n\nSix root and three genuine standalone physical closures previously zero failures with declarations/install unchanged. Root normal npm10-ci and genuine DevFn npm11 install have scripts enabled; AuthFn/FileFn standalone owners are retained independent installations, not fresh reinstalls. Exactly existing three contexts; no fourth/root/cleanup. Controlled28 inputs/context and observers must remain absent at promotion.\n\nRetain initial FileFn stale full corpus, invalid standalone target assumption, HMR collisions, center-click interception, multi-owner effect_orphan, obsolete AuthFn AI references, assets-only producer negative and capture typo. Scoped later passes do not erase these failures. No fresh PostgreSQL proof; native SQL skips remain. No full Bun authentication, backend durability/security-wide scan, native platform, OS IME/observer lifecycle, registry release or live Cloudflare/domain/secret changes.\n\nAll31 frozen thread bodies visibly read in bounded1–210/211–410/411–841 reads. Final dispositions1Fixed29Stale1Invalid; primary1Fixed6Stale1Invalid. Additional coordinated local families are assessed separately, not added to thread counts. Frozen JavaScript owner diagnostics superseded by reviewed42a/native contracts; Sonar canonical helper concerns corrected, async Promise/interface and static-title requests disproved, unused-loader hunk superseded. Hosted frozen failures remain historical, new-head gates unassessed.\n\n## Gate\n\nLocal source/acceptance review admits guarded promotion only after revalidating exact canonical source/modes, all current receipts, protected settings, independent standalone agreement, absent temporary inputs, clean frozen T, pinned ledger and exact remote identity. Ordinary uncommitted ancestry merge to reviewed42a plus exact canonical staged-tree equality required before one normal commit/push. No thread mutations, risk acceptance, CI polling or stopped-PR revisit.\n"}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-6.1-sol","usage":{"input":247,"output":1569,"cacheRead":176128,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":173,"totalTokens":177944,"cost":{"input":0.000494,"output":0.015690000000000003,"cacheRead":0.0176128,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0337968}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1791286199330,"responseId":"resp_055fb762f51dfcfc016ac4dbb7e15087d0b9e3e7a669452b67","rawStopReason":"completed","thinkingLevel":"high"}}
