{"type":"message","id":"1edbb265","parentId":"d259a6cf","timestamp":"2026-10-06T11:45:48.933Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_tXeJNthQnEh7EJAHoxcxWbOf|fc_055fb762f51dfcfc016ac4df6b7b8087d0abc099e5664d4085","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNogg extfn/docs/content/docs/reference/consumer-host-abstraction.md\n<!-- cubic:v=af5a2818-0cac-42a2-b3ea-497acfcbff8e -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=89d77ea6-21bc-5bb6-986a-2332a2024346 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":10} -->\nP2: `runtime.address.context` is a context kind, not the current URL path, so this adapter returns incorrect route state for shared navigation. Return `globalThis.location?.pathname ?? \"\"` and update the mirrored guide and generated LLM artifact.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At extfn/docs/content/docs/reference/consumer-host-abstraction.md, line 96:\n\n<comment>`runtime.address.context` is a context kind, not the current URL path, so this adapter returns incorrect route state for shared navigation. Return `globalThis.location?.pathname ?? \"\"` and update the mirrored guide and generated LLM artifact.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -0,0 +1,153 @@\n+      await runtime.browser.call(\"tabs.create\", { url });\n+    },\n+    currentPath() {\n+      return runtime.address.context;\n+    },\n+  },\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNogi extfn/docs/src/lib/server/docs-site-source.ts\n<!-- cubic:v=2568cae0-99c9-4d90-89c3-db47ded3eb63 -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=89d77ea6-21bc-5bb6-986a-2332a2024346 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":9} -->\nP2: Normalize a leading BOM and CRLF line endings before detecting frontmatter; otherwise affected pages render their metadata as body text and fall back to filename-derived titles.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At extfn/docs/src/lib/server/docs-site-source.ts, line 447:\n\n<comment>Normalize a leading BOM and CRLF line endings before detecting frontmatter; otherwise affected pages render their metadata as body text and fall back to filename-derived titles.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -0,0 +1,501 @@\n+  body: string;\n+  frontmatter: Record<string, unknown>;\n+} {\n+  if (!source.startsWith(\"---\\n\")) {\n+    return { body: source, frontmatter: {} };\n+  }\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNogn extfn/docs/src/lib/server/docs-site-source.ts\n<!-- cubic:v=004ae9b0-d32e-441b-9708-e35300429565 -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=89d77ea6-21bc-5bb6-986a-2332a2024346 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":8} -->\nP3: This site does not use the post compiler or the cache-summary/search-runtime helpers, so these exported paths are dead code in the consumer app. Remove the unused helpers and post cache, or add the routes/tests that consume them to avoid carrying an unreachable generalized scaffold.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At extfn/docs/src/lib/server/docs-site-source.ts, line 241:\n\n<comment>This site does not use the post compiler or the cache-summary/search-runtime helpers, so these exported paths are dead code in the consumer app. Remove the unused helpers and post cache, or add the routes/tests that consume them to avoid carrying an unreachable generalized scaffold.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -0,0 +1,501 @@\n+  });\n+}\n+\n+export async function getCompiledDocsPost(postId: string): Promise<CompiledContentArtifact> {\n+  const state = await loadDocsSiteServerState();\n+  return getCompiledArtifactOrThrow({\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNzqx scripts/docs-site/runtime.ts\n<!-- cubic:v=28db2e6a-2b9a-4df3-9915-24b920947e35 -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=062ac4fa-f9cd-5b7a-bd4b-d89f86693fc7 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":7} -->\nP1: This Node-only import breaks the documented Cloudflare opt-in unless every deployment enables `nodejs_compat`. Replace the path dependency with edge-safe POSIX path helpers, or make the Cloudflare configuration explicitly and verifiably enable the required compatibility flag.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At scripts/docs-site/runtime.ts, line 1:\n\n<comment>This Node-only import breaks the documented Cloudflare opt-in unless every deployment enables `nodejs_compat`. Replace the path dependency with edge-safe POSIX path helpers, or make the Cloudflare configuration explicitly and verifiably enable the required compatibility flag.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -0,0 +1,537 @@\n+import { basename, extname } from \"node:path\";\n+import {\n+  assertValidSourceEntries,\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNz7d extfn/docs/content/docs/reference/consumer-host-abstraction.md\n**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Return the actual pathname from the extension host**\n\nWhen shared components use `currentPath()` for routing or active-navigation state, this adapter returns an ExtFn context identifier such as `\"popup\"` or `\"content\"`, not the URL pathname returned by the SvelteKit implementation above. This makes the two implementations of `NavigationHost` observably incompatible; read the extension page's actual pathname (or explicitly redefine the interface around context identifiers) instead.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mPpj0 extfn/docs/svelte.config.js\n<!-- cubic:v=9c522afc-2e6e-450e-96f8-453fb7748a37 -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=804fce71-3bb1-546d-b7cc-49349a868699 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":8} -->\nP3: This `@site/docs-search` alias duplicates the exact same mapping already defined in `extfn/docs/vite.config.ts` (`resolve.alias` with `find: \"@site/docs-search\"` → `path.resolve(dirname, \"../../scripts/docs-site/Search.svelte\")`). Both feed the same Vite resolve pipeline, so the `kit.alias` entry is redundant, and the two definitions already use different path forms (relative string vs `path.resolve`) that can drift. The sibling sites (`authfn/docs`, `filefn/docs`) keep all `@site/*` aliases solely in `vite.config.ts` and use no `kit.alias`. Keep exactly one definition.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At extfn/docs/svelte.config.js, line 17:\n\n<comment>This `@site/docs-search` alias duplicates the exact same mapping already defined in `extfn/docs/vite.config.ts` (`resolve.alias` with `find: \"@site/docs-search\"` → `path.resolve(dirname, \"../../scripts/docs-site/Search.svelte\")`). Both feed the same Vite resolve pipeline, so the `kit.alias` entry is redundant, and the two definitions already use different path forms (relative string vs `path.resolve`) that can drift. The sibling sites (`authfn/docs`, `filefn/docs`) keep all `@site/*` aliases solely in `vite.config.ts` and use no `kit.alias`. Keep exactly one definition.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -14,6 +14,7 @@ const config = {\n   preprocess: vitePreprocess({ script: true }),\n   kit: {\n     adapter,\n+    alias: { \"@site/docs-search\": \"../../scripts/docs-site/Search.svelte\" },\n     appDir: docsDeploy ? \"docs/_app\" : \"_app\",\n     paths: {\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mPs38 scripts/docs-site/layout.ts\n## Superfluous trailing arguments\n\n<p>Superfluous argument passed to <a class=\"Link\" href=\"/21nCo/super-functions/blob/fec011e7c940d9ddc09b282f33007d9c3ec1aca9/scripts/verify-uifn-react-18-runtime.mjs#L49-L49\">default constructor of anonymous class</a>.</p>\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mP3IH extfn/docs/docsfn.config.ts\n**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Register ExtFn in the docs deployment pipeline**\n\nThe new site advertises this production canonical URL, but the repository's only docs deployment path does not know about ExtFn: `scripts/cloudflare-docs/config.mjs` has no `extfn` product, and `.github/workflows/superfunctions-docs-cloudflare-deploy.yml` neither watches `extfn/docs/**` nor offers ExtFn as a deploy target. Consequently, future ExtFn-only changes will not trigger a deployment, and neither manual nor tagged deployments can create the Worker/route for `extfn.com/docs`; add ExtFn to the product registry, selection logic, and workflow inputs/paths before publishing this URL.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6nFwIM scripts/cloudflare-docs/config.mjs\n**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Add ExtFn to the route-sync workflow**\n\nFresh evidence after the earlier deployment finding is that `.github/workflows/superfunctions-docs-cloudflare-routes.yml` still omits `extfn` from its product choices and does not expose `CLOUDFLARE_ZONE_ID_EXTFN_COM`. The deploy workflow can publish the Worker, but an operator cannot select ExtFn to attach its newly registered `extfn.com/docs*` route without choosing `all` and resynchronizing every product; add ExtFn to this separate route-provisioning workflow as well.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6nF0_U .github/workflows/superfunctions-docs-cloudflare-deploy.yml\n<!-- cubic:v=a8c432a7-0731-4521-ad33-711fbf708c46 -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=e3600364-f803-5837-8cd7-4222d9e23753 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":7} -->\nP2: Enabling extfn deploys here is not matched by the routes workflow: `superfunctions-docs-cloudflare-routes.yml` still offers only datafn/filefn/searchfn/authfn in its product choices and defines no `CLOUDFLARE_ZONE_ID_EXTFN_COM`/`CLOUDFLARE_ZONE_ID_EXTFN_DEV` vars, while `scripts/cloudflare-docs/config.mjs` registers extfn with zoneName `extfn.com` and hosts `dev.extfn.com`/`extfn.com`. `deploy.mjs` only runs `wrangler deploy` and never syncs routes, so these newly deployable extfn workers have no Cloudflare route pointing `extfn.com/docs` (or `dev.extfn.com/docs`) at them; the SvelteKit site also hardcodes its assets origin to those custom domains, so unreachable custom-domain routes break the deployed site. Update the routes workflow (add `extfn` option and the extfn.com zone-ID env vars) to match.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At .github/workflows/superfunctions-docs-cloudflare-deploy.yml, line 18:\n\n<comment>Enabling extfn deploys here is not matched by the routes workflow: `superfunctions-docs-cloudflare-routes.yml` still offers only datafn/filefn/searchfn/authfn in its product choices and defines no `CLOUDFLARE_ZONE_ID_EXTFN_COM`/`CLOUDFLARE_ZONE_ID_EXTFN_DEV` vars, while `scripts/cloudflare-docs/config.mjs` registers extfn with zoneName `extfn.com` and hosts `dev.extfn.com`/`extfn.com`. `deploy.mjs` only runs `wrangler deploy` and never syncs routes, so these newly deployable extfn workers have no Cloudflare route pointing `extfn.com/docs` (or `dev.extfn.com/docs`) at them; the SvelteKit site also hardcodes its assets origin to those custom domains, so unreachable custom-domain routes break the deployed site. Update the routes workflow (add `extfn` option and the extfn.com zone-ID env vars) to match.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -10,21 +10,25 @@ on:\n       - superfunctions-docs-searchfn-live-*\n       - superfunctions-docs-authfn-live-*\n       - superfunctions-datafn-docs-live-*\n+      - superfunctions-extfn-docs-live-*\n       - superfunctions-filefn-docs-live-*\n       - superfunctions-searchfn-docs-live-*\n\n[646 more lines in file. Use offset=181 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1791287148933}}
