y-wide clearance excluded.\n\n## Key Decisions\n- **#212 closed, #213 distinct round**: #212 publication consumed; recurring authorization allows next PR, not another #212 feedback cycle.\n- **Publication ≠ merge**: matching immediate heads and local passes do not establish hosted-green readiness.\n- **42a prerequisite authority**: preserve reviewed DB0.3/SecFn0.0.3 owners; frozenAPIbase7c6 discrepancies retained. Read #213 preparation SHA before assuming same current base.\n- **Architecture counters persist**: recurring206/207provider/payload/consumer-owner families are not reset for ExtFn.\n- **Faithful negatives ≠ native acceptance**: borrowed tooling is audit-only; #213 candidate installations still contain #212 bytes and provide no #213 consumer proof.\n- **Selective reuse with supplements**: immutable original plans, exact reviewed provenance, explicit later source/generated supplements; no unrelated product feature transfer.\n- **Tree/mode truth**: exact `ls-tree` membership, blob bytes and120000linktext; literal pathspecs for guarded Git source operations.\n- **Three genuine contexts only**: preserve existing contexts/locks/outputs; do not create a fourth for ExtFn or copy parent application dependencies.\n- **Fixture exclusion by identity**: preserve historical type fixtures and legitimate tracked `__tests__`/`__init__.py`; exact membership guards replace broad `__` filters.\n- **Consumer process ownership**: single-owner Node/Vite process; earlier multi-owner `effect_orphan` remains recorded harness failure.\n- **Real mobile hit testing**: exposed backdrop point verified with`elementFromPoint`, ordinary unforced click; no syntheticdispatch/app change for faulty center oracle.\n- **Executing public-origin ownership**: PUBLICorigin only in deployment, never assetsfallback; test actual config/CLI receivers, not only wrappers.\n- **No cleanup/root/stoppedPR revisit**: installed/history/protected artifacts and bounded publication allowance remain intact.\n- **R