}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-6.1-sol","usage":{"input":12338,"output":427,"cacheRead":91008,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":193,"totalTokens":103773,"cost":{"input":0.024676,"output":0.00427,"cacheRead":0.009100800000000001,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0380468}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1791330790878,"responseId":"resp_055fb762f51dfcfc016ac589e7481887d0a2d82a313fc6d7ff","rawStopReason":"completed","thinkingLevel":"high"}}
{"type":"message","id":"2743ef67","parentId":"38883773","timestamp":"2026-10-06T23:53:22.063Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_d9BC3Bv3IZ3kBkG8bR8n0iqA|fc_055fb762f51dfcfc016ac589f1ed5887d08c5d320afe1d14ec","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\nPreserve unrelated dirty work and exclude unrelated untracked and `.conduct/` artifacts. Do not expand into repository-wide cleanup or redesign. If a complete repair requires expanded authority or an unavailable dependency, explain the remaining defect and classify it as blocked rather than presenting a symptom patch as complete.\n\n## 8. Verify behavior and review the fix batch\n\nFor each root cause, demonstrate the previously failing behavior and its corrected outcome with focused regression coverage where practical. Confirm the test would fail on the old behavior, by running it against the old code when safe or by explaining the distinguishing assertion. Do not claim a reproduced failure when it was only reasoned through.\n\nUse evidence appropriate to the contract. Verify consumer-visible outcomes at the relevant boundaries: serialized artifacts, cleanup recovery, supported package entrypoints, or export/replay. Exercise combinations and composition where failures arise from interacting inputs; use property-based or generated cases when justified, without requiring them for every small fix. A regression matrix must test the stated invariant, not merely enumerate examples from bot comments.\n\nUse evidence appropriate to the contract:\n\n- For SQL, claims, locks, and transactions, prove resulting state and relevant concurrency behavior using a real disposable database when feasible. SQL-text assertions alone do not establish correctness.\n- For retry/recovery, cover the relevant interrupted state and the evidence needed to declare success.\n- For configuration propagation, verify both the executing component's configuration and required secret wiring without deploying.\n- Tests that mutate fixtures must restore prior values and row existence or use isolated disposable fixtures.\n\nFor operating-system lifecycle, process ownership, cleanup, or resource-release findings, the acceptance oracle must inspect the external OS-visible state. Do not prove absence of processes with the same liveness helper being changed. When the defect depends on PID 1, signals, reparenting, process groups, namespaces, or platform cleanup, reproduce that environment faithfully and prove the old head fails the distinguishing assertion before accepting a repair.\n\nIf behavioral verification is unavailable, report the gap explicitly. Test counts, mocks that mirror the implementation, and typechecks are not substitutes for proof of the failing behavior.\n\nAfter editing, review the entire fix diff together with its callers and affected contract before staging. Check for missed sibling paths, newly broken consumers, error/cleanup regressions, and interactions between fixes. Re-run checks when justified by subsequent changes or unresolved concerns. Complete local repair and verification within this single pre-push batch.\n\nRun focused tests first, then proportionate typecheck, lint, test, and build gates. Distinguish change-caused failures, baseline/environment limits, local proof, and external state.\n\nDo not wait for external CI in this skill. The required pre-edit current-head check snapshot is part of finding collection; after the push, one immediate check snapshot is allowed only for reporting. No polling. Skipped, failed, or absent reviewers do not prove coverage.\n\n## 9. Commit and push the fixes exactly once\n\nInvoking this skill authorizes one reviewed commit and one normal push of the fixes produced by this round to the PR head branch. Do not leave completed fixes only in the local worktree. If the fetched snapshot contains no actionable findings and no changes were made, do not create an empty commit or push.\n\nBefore committing:\n\n1. review the exact staged allowlist\n2. run `git diff --cached --check`\n3. confirm unrelated artifacts are excluded\n4. confirm the root-cause ledger identifies evidence for every claimed fix and lists remaining valid defects\n5. confirm no reset trigger remains unaddressed and no claimed complete repair leaves a known affected path deferred\n\nCreate exactly one commit for the reviewed fix batch and push it once to the PR head branch. Do not force-push. Verify the local, remote, and PR head SHAs once after pushing.\n\nDo not refetch review feedback after the push. Do not wait for the pushed commit to receive new reviews.\n\n## 10. Reconcile the queue\n\nSeparate remaining code defects from open GitHub thread and failed-check counts. Report how many snapshot threads and check diagnostics are fixed/already fixed, still valid, blocked, or unassessed, distinguishing surface counts from deduplicated root causes.\n\nThis skill does not by itself authorize posting replies, resolving threads, or dismissing reviews. If separately authorized by the user, resolve only snapshot threads whose full concern is covered by current-code evidence and the verified PR head; use captured IDs and mutation responses without refetching feedback. Never resolve a valid blocked finding or dismiss a review merely to reduce the count. Otherwise report fixed threads as eligible for resolution while leaving their GitHub state unchanged.\n\n## 11. Report and terminate\n\nReport with these explicit buckets:\n\n- `Fixed`\n- `Skipped (Already Fixed / Stale)`\n- `Not Attempted`\n- `Verification`\n- `Invalid / Accepted Risk` when applicable\n- `Convergence`: valid blocking root causes before/after, newly discovered defects, fix-induced regressions, recurring families, oldest deferred blockers and verification gaps. Distinguish assessed from unassessed items. Use improving, stalled, regressing or unknown with evidence; more tests, commits or resolved threads alone do not establish progress.\n- `Convergence gate`: ledger path, stable family IDs, failed-round counts, mode (`routine`, `architecture_reset_required`, or `architecture_reset`), and the assessment fields used to open any reset gate.\n\nFor each fixed root cause, summarize affected paths and behavioral evidence. Include unverified contracts and valid blocked defects; a completed round does not establish merge readiness.\n\nInclude the exact pushed commit SHA and PR URL. If no changes were needed, say explicitly that no commit or push was created. State failed, pending, or unverified CI and reviewer checks without waiting for them. A local fix does not establish that a hosted quality gate has passed.\n\nEnd with a clear termination statement such as:\n\n> One review round is complete. No post-push refetch or additional review loop was performed.\n\nThen stop.\n\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1791330802063}}
{"type":"message","id":"2e4a7b4d","parentId":"2743ef67","timestamp":"2026-10-06T23:53:22.063Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_QRnaUGxZCoRtsXt9sZjHZ6Np|fc_055fb762f51dfcfc016ac589f1ed6c87d0b83698d6d617b591","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { error } from \"@sveltejs/kit\";\nimport {\n  getTopNavigation,\n  type CompiledContentArtifact,\n  type Sidebar,\n} from \"@docsfn/core\";\nimport {\n  resolveDocsPageSurface,\n  resolveDocsRouteDataOrThrow,\n  type SvelteDocsPageSurface,\n} from \"@docsfn/sveltekit\";\nimport type { DocsSiteSource } from \"./runtime\";\n\ninterface DocsPageOptions {\n  apiBreadcrumbLabel?: string;\n  apiBreadcrumbHref?: string;\n  fallbackSidebarId?: string;\n}\n\nfunction buildCanonicalUrl(canonicalBase: string | undefined, path: string): string {\n  if (!canonicalBase) return path;\n  let end = canonicalBase.length;\n  while (end > 0 && canonicalBase[end - 1] === \"/\") end -= 1;\n  const origin = canonicalBase.slice(0, end);\n  const pathname = path.startsWith(\"/\") ? path : \"/\" + path;\n  return origin + pathname;\n}\n\nfunction isRouteNotFoundError(input: unknown): input is { message: string } {\n  return (\n    typeof input === \"object\" && input !== null &&\n    \"code\" in input && input.code === \"DOCS_ROUTE_NOT_FOUND\" &&\n    \"message\" in input && typeof input.message === \"string\"\n  );\n}\n\nfunction hasNestedDocsRoutes(routes: Record<string, string>, route: string): boolean {\n  return Object.keys(routes).some((candidate) => candidate.startsWith(`${route}/`));\n}\n\nexport async function loadDocsPage(input: {\n  slug: string | undefined;\n  source: DocsSiteSource;\n  getCompiledDocsPage: (id: string) => Promise<CompiledContentArtifact>;\n  resolveMarkdownRelativeLinks: (input: {\n    compiled: CompiledContentArtifact;\n    route: string;\n    sourcePath: string;\n    isIndexRoute: boolean;\n  }) => CompiledContentArtifact;\n  options?: DocsPageOptions;\n}) {\n  const { slug, source, getCompiledDocsPage, resolveMarkdownRelativeLinks, options = {} } = input;\n  let routeEntry;\n  try {\n    routeEntry = resolveDocsRouteDataOrThrow(slug, source.manifest, { basePath: \"/docs\" });\n  } catch (routeError) {\n    if (isRouteNotFoundError(routeError)) throw error(404, routeError.message);\n    throw routeError;\n  }\n\n  if (routeEntry.kind === \"post\") {\n    throw error(404, `unsupported docs route kind: ${routeEntry.kind}`);\n  }\n\n  let surface: SvelteDocsPageSurface;\n  if (routeEntry.kind === \"api\") {\n    const api = routeEntry.api;\n    const route = routeEntry.route;\n    surface = {\n      route,\n      title: api.title,\n      description: typeof api.frontmatter.description === \"string\" ? api.frontmatter.description : undefined,\n      canonicalPath: route,\n      canonicalUrl: buildCanonicalUrl(source.canonicalUrl, route),\n      sidebarId: \"api\",\n      headings: [],\n      breadcrumbs: [\n        { label: \"Docs\", href: \"/docs\" },\n        { label: options.apiBreadcrumbLabel ?? \"API Reference\", href: options.apiBreadcrumbHref ?? \"/docs/api\" },\n        { label: api.title, href: route },\n      ],\n      pagination: {},\n      topNav: getTopNavigation(source.manifest),\n      versions: source.manifest.versions,\n    };\n  } else {\n    surface = resolveDocsPageSurface({\n      manifest: source.manifest,\n      route: routeEntry.route,\n      page: routeEntry.page,\n      options: {\n        basePath: \"/docs\",\n        homeHref: \"/docs\",\n        canonicalUrl: source.canonicalUrl,\n        versionMode: \"path-prefix\",\n      },\n    });\n  }\n\n  const sidebarId = surface.sidebarId ?? \"default\";\n  const sidebar: Sidebar | undefined = source.manifest.sidebars[sidebarId] ??\n    (options.fallbackSidebarId ? source.manifest.sidebars[options.fallbackSidebarId] : undefined);\n  const compiled = routeEntry.kind === \"page\"\n    ? resolveMarkdownRelativeLinks({\n        compiled: await getCompiledDocsPage(routeEntry.page.id),\n        route: routeEntry.route,\n        sourcePath: routeEntry.page.id.slice(routeEntry.page.id.indexOf(\":\") + 1),\n        isIndexRoute: hasNestedDocsRoutes(source.manifest.routes, routeEntry.route),\n      })\n    : undefined;\n\n  return {\n    routeEntry: routeEntry.kind === \"page\" ? { kind: \"page\" as const } : routeEntry,\n    surface,\n    sidebar,\n    compiled,\n    searchDocumentCount: Array.isArray(source.searchArtifact.documents) ? source.searchArtifact.documents.length : 0,\n    searchScopes: Array.isArray(source.searchArtifact.scopes) ? source.searchArtifact.scopes.join(\", \") : \"none\",\n    siteTitle: source.siteTitle,\n    compatPreset: source.compatPreset,\n  };\n}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1791330802063}}
{"type":"message","id":"be53bcfc","parentId":"2e4a7b4d","timestamp":"2026-10-06T23:53:22.064Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_CNnGR3YAU7SzvsJLsFYmaJPJ|fc_055fb762f51dfcfc016ac589f1ed7487d0bbb2a51a10f35486","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { basename, extname } from \"node:path\";\nimport matter from \"gray-matter\";\nimport {\n  assertValidSourceEntries,\n  buildManifest,\n  buildSearchIndex,\n  compileSvelteContent,\n  createDiagnostic,\n  createDocsError,\n  createSourceEntryId,\n  createDocsSearchRuntime,\n  normalizeProviderPath,\n  toLegacyRawEntries,\n  type CompiledContentArtifact,\n  type DocsCollection,\n  type DocsCompatPreset,\n  type DocsConfig,\n  type DocsContentProvider,\n  type DocsManifest,\n  type DocsSearchArtifact,\n  type DocsSearchRuntime,\n  type DocsSourceEntry,\n} from \"@docsfn/core\";\n\nexport interface DocsSiteSource {\n  siteRoot: string;\n  manifest: DocsManifest;\n  searchArtifact: DocsSearchArtifact;\n  siteTitle: string;\n  canonicalUrl?: string;\n  compatPreset: DocsCompatPreset;\n  config: DocsConfig;\n}\n\nexport interface DocsSiteCompiledCacheSummary {\n  framework: \"svelte\";\n  compatPreset: DocsCompatPreset;\n  pageKeys: string[];\n  postKeys: string[];\n}\n\ninterface DocsSiteCompiledContentCache {\n  framework: \"svelte\";\n  compatPreset: DocsCompatPreset;\n  pages: Map<string, CompiledContentArtifact>;\n  posts: Map<string, CompiledContentArtifact>;\n  pageKeysById: Record<string, string>;\n  postKeysById: Record<string, string>;\n}\n\ninterface DocsSiteServerState {\n  source: DocsSiteSource;\n  compiledCache: DocsSiteCompiledContentCache;\n}\n\nfunction createCompiledCacheKey(input: {\n  kind: \"page\" | \"post\";\n  id: string;\n  framework: \"svelte\";\n  compatPreset: DocsCompatPreset;\n}): string {\n  return [input.kind, input.id, input.framework, input.compatPreset].join(\"|\");\n}\n\nfunction sortById<T extends { id: string }>(items: T[]): T[] {\n  return [...items].sort((left, right) =>\n    left.id.localeCompare(right.id, \"en\", {\n      sensitivity: \"variant\",\n      numeric: true,\n    }),\n  );\n}\n\nfunction createCompiledCache(input: {\n  manifest: DocsManifest;\n  compatPreset: DocsCompatPreset;\n}): DocsSiteCompiledContentCache {\n  const framework = \"svelte\" as const;\n  const pages = new Map<string, CompiledContentArtifact>();\n  const posts = new Map<string, CompiledContentArtifact>();\n  const pageKeysById: Record<string, string> = {};\n  const postKeysById: Record<string, string> = {};\n\n  for (const page of sortById(Object.values(input.manifest.pages))) {\n    const key = createCompiledCacheKey({\n      kind: \"page\",\n      id: page.id,\n      framework,\n      compatPreset: input.compatPreset,\n    });\n    pageKeysById[page.id] = key;\n    pages.set(\n      key,\n      compileSvelteContent({\n        source: page.body,\n        sourcePath: page.id,\n        compatPreset: input.compatPreset,\n      }),\n    );\n  }\n\n  for (const post of sortById(Object.values(input.manifest.posts))) {\n    const key = createCompiledCacheKey({\n      kind: \"post\",\n      id: post.id,\n      framework,\n      compatPreset: input.compatPreset,\n    });\n    postKeysById[post.id] = key;\n    posts.set(\n      key,\n      compileSvelteContent({\n        source: post.body,\n        sourcePath: post.id,\n        compatPreset: input.compatPreset,\n      }),\n    );\n  }\n\n  return {\n    framework,\n    compatPreset: input.compatPreset,\n    pages,\n    posts,\n    pageKeysById,\n    postKeysById,\n  };\n}\n\nfunction getCompiledArtifactOrThrow(input: {\n  kind: \"page\" | \"post\";\n  id: string;\n  cache: DocsSiteCompiledContentCache;\n}): CompiledContentArtifact {\n  const keysById =\n    input.kind === \"page\" ? input.cache.pageKeysById : input.cache.postKeysById;\n  const entries = input.kind === \"page\" ? input.cache.pages : input.cache.posts;\n  const key = keysById[input.id];\n\n  if (!key) {\n    throw createDocsError({\n      code: \"DOCS_ARTIFACT_INVALID\",\n      message: `compiled ${input.kind} cache key is missing for ${input.id}`,\n      diagnostics: [\n        createDiagnostic({\n          code: \"DOCS_ARTIFACT_INVALID\",\n          message: `compiled ${input.kind} cache key is missing for ${input.id}`,\n          details: {\n            kind: input.kind,\n            id: input.id,\n          },\n        }),\n      ],\n    });\n  }\n\n  const compiled = entries.get(key);\n  if (!compiled) {\n    throw createDocsError({\n      code: \"DOCS_ARTIFACT_INVALID\",\n      message: `compiled ${input.kind} artifact is missing for ${input.id}`,\n      diagnostics: [\n        createDiagnostic({\n          code: \"DOCS_ARTIFACT_INVALID\",\n          message: `compiled ${input.kind} artifact is missing for ${input.id}`,\n          details: {\n            kind: input.kind,\n            id: input.id,\n            key,\n          },\n        }),\n      ],\n    });\n  }\n\n  return compiled;\n}\n\n/** One independent cache per site; raw modules are supplied by the site's Vite glob. */\nexport function createDocsSiteRuntime(\n  docsConfig: DocsConfig,\n  bundledContent: Record<string, string>,\n  bundledStatic: Record<string, string>,\n  modulePrefix = \"../../../\",\n) {\n  let serverStatePromise: Promise<DocsSiteServerState> | null = null;\n  async function loadDocsSiteServerState(): Promise<DocsSiteServerState> {\n    serverStatePromise ??= (async () => {\n        const siteRoot = \".\";\n        const config = docsConfig satisfies DocsConfig;\n        const provider = createBundledContentProvider(config);\n        const manifest = await buildManifest(provider, config);\n        const searchArtifact = await buildSearchIndex(manifest, {\n          search: config.search,\n          auth: config.auth,\n        });\n        const compatPreset = config.compat?.preset ?? \"none\";\n        const compiledCache = createCompiledCache({\n          manifest,\n          compatPreset,\n        });\n\n        return {\n          source: {\n            siteRoot,\n            manifest,\n            searchArtifact,\n            siteTitle: config.site.title,\n            canonicalUrl: config.site.canonicalUrl,\n            compatPreset,\n            config,\n          },\n          compiledCache,\n        };\n    })().catch((error) => {\n      serverStatePromise = null;\n      throw error;\n    });\n\n    return serverStatePromise;\n  }\n\n  async function loadDocsSiteSource(): Promise<DocsSiteSource> {\n    const state = await loadDocsSiteServerState();\n    return state.source;\n  }\n\n  async function getCompiledDocsPage(\n    pageId: string,\n  ): Promise<CompiledContentArtifact> {\n    const state = await loadDocsSiteServerState();\n    return getCompiledArtifactOrThrow({\n      kind: \"page\",\n      id: pageId,\n      cache: state.compiledCache,\n    });\n  }\n\n  async function getCompiledDocsPost(\n    postId: string,\n  ): Promise<CompiledContentArtifact> {\n    const state = await loadDocsSiteServerState();\n    return getCompiledArtifactOrThrow({\n      kind: \"post\",\n      id: postId,\n      cache: state.compiledCache,\n    });\n  }\n\n  async function getDocsSiteCompiledCacheSummary(): Promise<DocsSiteCompiledCacheSummary> {\n    const state = await loadDocsSiteServerState();\n    return {\n      framework: state.compiledCache.framework,\n      compatPreset: state.compiledCache.compatPreset,\n      pageKeys: [...state.compiledCache.pages.keys()].sort((left, right) =>\n        left.localeCompare(right, \"en\", {\n          sensitivity: \"variant\",\n          numeric: true,\n        }),\n      ),\n      postKeys: [...state.compiledCache.posts.keys()].sort((left, right) =>\n        left.localeCompare(right, \"en\", {\n          sensitivity: \"variant\",\n          numeric: true,\n        }),\n      ),\n    };\n  }\n\n  async function createDocsSiteSearchRuntime(): Promise<DocsSearchRuntime> {\n    const state = await loadDocsSiteServerState();\n    return createDocsSearchRuntime({\n      artifact: state.source.searchArtifact,\n    });\n  }\n\n  function createBundledContentProvider(\n    config: DocsConfig,\n  ): DocsContentProvider {\n    const modules = {\n      ...normalizeBundledModules(bundledContent, modulePrefix),\n      ...normalizeBundledModules(bundledStatic, modulePrefix),\n    };\n\n    return {\n      providerId: \"bundled\",\n      async listEntries(input) {\n        const entries = input.collections.flatMap((collection) =>\n          collectEntriesForCollection(collection, modules, config),\n        );\n        return assertValidSourceEntries(entries);\n      },\n      async loadEntry(input) {\n        return input.entry;\n      },\n      async list() {\n        const entries = await this.listEntries({\n          config,\n          collections: [\"docs\", \"pages\", \"blog\", \"api\", \"assets\"],\n        });\n\n[210 more lines in file. Use offset=301 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1791330802064}}
{"type":"message","id":"542f105f","parentId":"be53bcfc","timestamp":"2026-10-06T23:53:22.064Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_Mn92hDZnvTlQ4DhIsEhnkTlP|fc_055fb762f51dfcfc016ac589f1ed7c87d08e59c88c17758f01","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"// Audit-only thin fixtures. No application source mutation or dependency installation.\nimport assert from 'node:assert/strict';\nimport fs from 'node:fs';\nimport path from 'node:path';\nimport vm from 'node:vm';\nimport crypto from 'node:crypto';\nimport { execFileSync } from 'node:child_process';\nimport { createRequire } from 'node:module';\nimport { pathToFileURL } from 'node:url';\nconst A = path.dirname(new URL(import.meta.url).pathname);\nconst T = '/Users/serro/orca/workspaces/superfunctions/docs-pr-206-review-20260930';\nconst HEAD = '7bb23068fbbb17cb71b19f1f58c5d50352a7faac';\nconst runtime = '/Volumes/OS - Data/superfunctions-agent-storage/sf-docs-review-20260930/sequential-20261003T184612Z/verification-runtime';\nconst run = (cmd,args,cwd=T,env={}) => execFileSync(cmd,args,{cwd,encoding:'utf8',env:{...process.env,...env},maxBuffer:16*1024*1024});\nassert.equal(run('git',['rev-parse','HEAD']).trim(),HEAD);\nassert.equal(run('git',['status','--porcelain']).trim(),'');\nconst candidate = process.env.PR211_CANDIDATE;\nconst inputRoot = candidate ?? T;\nconst read = p => fs.readFileSync(path.join(inputRoot,p),'utf8');\nconst hash = s => crypto.createHash('sha256').update(s).digest('hex');\n// TypeScript is audit tooling only; copied hooks have only native Node imports after type erasure.\nconst require = createRequire('/Volumes/OS - Data/superfunctions-agent-storage/sf-docs-review-20260930/sequential-20261003T184612Z/PR-209/verification-latest-base-root/package.json');\nconst ts = require('typescript');\nconst tmp = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(runtime,'tmp-210/pr211-frozen-thin-'));\nconst put = (p,s,mode) => {const f=path.join(tmp,p); fs.mkdirSync(path.dirname(f),{recursive:true});fs.wri