 source absolutePath. Markdown links resolve from the actual source file, not whether its public route happens to have descendants. Full manifests, frontmatter, bodies and search indexes stay server-owned; only approved render/navigation DTOs cross hydration. Preserve API and native blog consumers, valid sidebar fallback and Promise/rejection contracts.\n2. **Faithful old failing boundary:** `frozen-actual-flat-link-result.json` runs exact frozen runtime/page source, type-erased only, with published Core 0.0.5 resolved through an existing consumer declaring that same version. Actual compiled HTML contains `/docs/flat/sibling.md`, while the producer's real sibling route is `/docs/sibling`. No invented DocPage fields. This is an audit-only SDK boundary, not a frozen locked install/native ExtFn build. Historical provider/payload failures from #206/#207/#209/#210 are retained, not replaced by this narrower example.\n3. **Coordinated ownership/failure plan:** Compose reviewed provider/page/blog/DTO enforcement from prior publications only after exact per-path provenance and caller assessment. Preserve original 85 paths and reviewed preparation-base DB/SecFn owners. Carry text normalization, metadata controls, first-colon paths, flat/index/Unicode links, native assets and all affected AuthFn/FileFn/ExtFn callers together. Do not strip full server content to silence a serialization oracle. Keep API display records only where explicitly admitted by the DTO contract.\n4. **Independent acceptance:** Actual pinned provider/manifest/compiler render blocks; flat-file-with-descendants and index routes, Unicode and multiple-colon filenames; approved output keys and private-marker absence in actual HTTP/hydration responses while server access and permitted compiled text remain available. Native blog/RSS/draft/title and text-versus-binary routes. Root and exactly three reused genuine consumer contexts, own dependencies/locks, native Vite HTTP plus ExtFn hydrated search/mobile/error-title. Helper/mock passes alone do not admit publication.\n\n## docs.consumer-conditional-runtime-ownership — four fields\n\n1. **Invariant:** Shared imports resolve through each consuming site's declared public ESM/subpath exports, without root/sibling dependency borrowing, guessed CJS sibling files or universal externalization. The same owner's Svelte runtime handles compilation, hydration, search and loader branches.\n2. **Faithful old failing boundary:** `frozen-native-ssr-owner-result.json`: literal frozen runtime/plugin bytes, real Vite 6.4.3 SSR loader and native loopback HTTP, isolated shared-source audit directory without a parent installation. The retained DevFn owner has the same frozen ExtFn Core declaration, Vite range/version and gray-matter declaration. HTTP returns 500 / `ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND` for gray-matter. Borrowed receiver is audit-only, not new genuine ExtFn proof. AuthFn/FileFn frozen manifests independently omit gray-matter although their shared runtime imports it. Prior family native/package-path failures remain qualified and retained.\n3. **Coordinated ownership/failure plan:** Reuse reviewed export-aware owner/plugin/test configuration only after source and physical package graph assessment. Declare gray-matter directly in AuthFn/FileFn; preserve ExtFn's existing declaration. Trace the actual AuthFn OpenAPI plugin graph before deciding about OAuth/observability peers; no removal based on direct text searches. Preserve Kit typing aliases unless native type/source ownership evidence supports removal. Restore consumers from archived preimages into the one SSD candidate and three existing slots only; no fourth installation or extra full root. Any active-slot conversion requires explicit source/archive/own-lock admission, not copying a sibling/root lock.\n4. **Independent acceptance:** Normal root npm10 ci with scripts and unchanged admitted lock; independently owned ordinary standalone installations where necessary. Physical closure and exact public export/version checks; real CLI generators, full consumer tsc, native tests/build/Vite SSR HTTP, single-owner hydrated browser and search/mobile drawer. Record npm10 Arborist, npm11, DNS/native, and inherited baseline failures distinctly. Existing #212 installations do not prove #213.\n\n## docs.public-origin-propagation — four fields (new cache sibling)\n\n1. **Invariant:** Executing producer/public HTML/LLM URLs use selected public origin only under deployment; assets are a separate role. Cached builds must distinguish every output-affecting environment role. Documented local and deployed /docs LLM endpoints must resolve; guides and generated full-text corpus agree with canonical public hosts.\n2. **Faithful old failing boundary:** `frozen213-cache-result.json`: actual installed Turbo CLI audits the frozen worktree/config/inputs with two distinct public origins. All three actual task hashes are unchanged (`@extfn/docs`, `@authfn/docs`, `@filefn/docs`); configured/inferred hash env arrays are empty. No build task or live deployment executed. Frozen AuthFn has advertised /docs LLM URLs but no explicit corresponding route handlers; real native HTTP reproduction remains required before claiming that endpoint repaired.\n3. **Coordinated ownership/failure plan:** Coordinate actual config/generator/deploy receivers, cache configuration and endpoint routes. Hash deployment/public/assets roles through the supported build/global env mechanism, respecting child Turbo configuration inheritance. Preserve reviewed canonicalUrl option AND returned value. Add native /docs endpoints rather than merely changing published docs to a root URL outside /docs Worker selection. Correct FileFn AI host siblings and regenerate affected corpus. No domain, route, DNS, certificate, secrets or live Worker mutation.\n4. **Independent acceptance:** Actual Turbo hashes change for output-affecting roles and stay stable on repeat, actual executing native config/generator default/deploy/dev/live/distinct-assets/missing-public/assets-only matrix, nonwriting freshness checks, actual native HTTP endpoint content/type/cache behavior. Offline Cloudflare build/emitted literals are not deployment/Worker execution. Windows junction/guard correction is checked against the actual test path without claiming Windows execution on macOS.\n\n## docs.llms-artifact-publication — new writer sibling\n\n1. **Invariant:** A public artifact pathname always exposes complete old or complete new bytes during generation. Failed replacement preserves old target and owner mode; temporary files belong to one write, never a predictable shared PID-only slot. Check mode does not create output directories. This is per-file atomic visibility, not a promised pair-level transaction or power-loss durability contract.\n2. **Faithful old failing OS boundary:** `old-native-artifact-reader-boundary.log`: exact frozen public writer runs in a separate normal Node child on the authorized SSD. An independent native public-path reader makes 102 reads and observes 9 violations, including empty/truncated bytes. No mocked filesystem, process kill or application source change. Owned audit outputs retained.\n3. **Coordinated ownership/failure plan:** Same-directory exclusively created unique temporary file, complete write/close before atomic rename, preserve existing target mode, and remove only that owned temporary on errors. Reject ambiguous symlink/nonregular target behavior rather than silently changing ownership semantics. Keep failures visible and existing target bytes intact. All shared generator callers use the enforcement point.\n4. **Independent acceptance:** Independent concurrent native public readers see only complete old/new bytes. Existing-mode preservation; absent target; repeat/check/missing/check-no-mkdir; injected write/rename failure proves old bytes unchanged and only owned temporary absent; disjoint concurrent writer temps. Preserve preexisting source/output/fixture bytes. No assertion of fsync/power-loss or pair transaction guarantees.\n\n## ExtFn CLI/head/layout and parallel frozen checks\n\nTrace unconditional `buildExtension` before scan/archive across guide mirrors, reference, getting-started and generated artifacts; fix all still-misleading siblings together. Navigation currentPath must be pathname, not context kind. Preserve one dynamic normal/error title, native TopBar/search/mobile drawer, reduced motion, observer disconnect and nonzero-height guard. UIFn constructor finding is unrelated to this source location and cannot justify suppressing it globally.\n\nFrozen JavaScript diagnostics are SecFn/DB API owner failures; compose the reviewed preparation base rather than reverting its DB0.3/SecFn0.0.3 contracts. Frozen Sonar reliability C/A and concrete annotations need individual current-source dispositions. Reviewer docstring coverage 17.07%/80% remains uncleared; no agent risk acceptance or inferred hosted green.\n\n## Admission status\n\nThe two mandatory recurring-family four-field assessments are recorded here, but this does NOT admit source mutation/publication: all56/supplementary original source/generated/lock assessment, exact provenance plan, archives, capacity guards, physical/native acceptance and staged tree/ancestry guards remain pending. Fresh visible primary reading now covers every line 1–826 in bounded untruncated chunks; source patch reading only covers 1–800 of 4364, and no full-source reading is claimed. Novel supplementary review/comment bodies were read untruncated; exact historical body/source reuse retains prior visibility qualifications.\n\nHosted pr-refetch-fix is controlling. The cubic check-pr-comments generic polling/thread-resolution/delegation defaults are not applied: no recollection/poll/retrigger/thread mutation/delegation, no stopped-PR revisit, no force push/admin bypass. #212 remains published once and stopped; #133 parked; #222 protected. Exactly one SSD root/three existing contexts; historical cleanup and relocation authority consumed.\n"}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-6.1-sol","usage":{"input":2657,"output":2627,"cacheRead":135936,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":516,"totalTokens":141220,"cost":{"input":0.005314,"output":0.02627,"cacheRead":0.0135936,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0451776}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1791330996514,"responseId":"resp_055fb762f51dfcfc016ac58ab501a087d0afdbef1bda134d90","rawStopReason":"completed","thinkingLevel":"high"}}
