{"type":"message","id":"30942fbd","parentId":"c4471f94","timestamp":"2026-10-06T23:58:54.868Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_CaXG3fEXbd8k2UgLq0MuyamO|fc_055fb762f51dfcfc016ac58b3ebf3487d0ab58b1d8a33eaaa1","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNmGb extfn/docs/src/lib/server/docs-site-source.ts\n![kody code-review](https://img.shields.io/badge/kody-code--review-312B4B?labelColor=C9BBF2) ![Bug](https://img.shields.io/badge/Bug-B71C1C) ![medium](https://img.shields.io/badge/severity_level-medium-1A7BBE)\n\n\nparseFrontmatter only recognizes frontmatter when the file starts with exactly \"---\\n\" (LF, no BOM), and it scans for \"\\n---\" without allowing CRLF before the closing fence. a markdown file with CRLF line endings or a BOM has its frontmatter treated as page body, so the title/description leak visibly into rendered docs pages and llms.txt artifacts. match /^---\\r?\\n/ for the opening fence and /\\r?\\n---(\\r?\\n|$)/ for the closing fence.\n\n```typescript\nif (!/^---\\r?\\n/.test(source)) {\n    return { body: source, frontmatter: {} };\n  }\n\n  const closingIndex = source.search(/\\r?\\n---(\\r?\\n|$)/, );\n```\n\n\n\n<details>\n\n<summary>Prompt for LLM</summary>\n\n```\n\nFile extfn/docs/src/lib/server/docs-site-source.ts:\n\nLine 447 to 457:\n\nparseFrontmatter only recognizes frontmatter when the file starts with exactly \"---\\n\" (LF, no BOM), and it scans for \"\\n---\" without allowing CRLF before the closing fence. a markdown file with CRLF line endings or a BOM has its frontmatter treated as page body, so the title/description leak visibly into rendered docs pages and llms.txt artifacts. match /^---\\r?\\n/ for the opening fence and /\\r?\\n---(\\r?\\n|$)/ for the closing fence.\n\nSuggested Code:\n\nif (!/^---\\r?\\n/.test(source)) {\n    return { body: source, frontmatter: {} };\n  }\n\n  const closingIndex = source.search(/\\r?\\n---(\\r?\\n|$)/, );\n\n```\n\n</details>\n\n\n<sub>Talk to Kody by mentioning @kody</sub>\n\n\n<sub>Was this suggestion helpful? React with 👍 or 👎 to help Kody learn from this interaction.</sub>\n\n<!-- kody-codereview -->&#8203;\n&#8203;\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNmI6 extfn/docs/src/lib/server/docs-site-source.ts\n![kody code-review](https://img.shields.io/badge/kody-code--review-312B4B?labelColor=C9BBF2) ![Bug](https://img.shields.io/badge/Bug-B71C1C) ![medium](https://img.shields.io/badge/severity_level-medium-1A7BBE)\n\n\nparseFrontmatter only recognizes frontmatter when the file starts with exactly `\"---\\n\"` and locates the closing delimiter with `indexOf(\"\\n---\", 4)`. any markdown file with CRLF line endings (e.g. authored on Windows) or a leading BOM silently fails frontmatter detection, so `title`/`description` render as literal body text and the page title falls back to the filename via deriveTitleFromPath. accept `---\\r\\n` (e.g. test with `/^---\\r?\\n/` or normalize line endings before parsing) and treat a BOM-prefixed source as frontmatter-bearing.\n\n\n\n\n\n<details>\n\n<summary>Prompt for LLM</summary>\n\n```\n\nFile extfn/docs/src/lib/server/docs-site-source.ts:\n\nLine 447 to 457:\n\nparseFrontmatter only recognizes frontmatter when the file starts with exactly `\"---\\n\"` and locates the closing delimiter with `indexOf(\"\\n---\", 4)`. any markdown file with CRLF line endings (e.g. authored on Windows) or a leading BOM silently fails frontmatter detection, so `title`/`description` render as literal body text and the page title falls back to the filename via deriveTitleFromPath. accept `---\\r\\n` (e.g. test with `/^---\\r?\\n/` or normalize line endings before parsing) and treat a BOM-prefixed source as frontmatter-bearing.\n\n```\n\n</details>\n\n\n<sub>Talk to Kody by mentioning @kody</sub>\n\n\n<sub>Was this suggestion helpful? React with 👍 or 👎 to help Kody learn from this interaction.</sub>\n\n<!-- kody-codereview -->&#8203;\n&#8203;\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNogZ extfn/docs/src/routes/+layout.server.ts\n<!-- cubic:v=11e9947b-9a89-45cf-9ffd-2ceb123583ac -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=89d77ea6-21bc-5bb6-986a-2332a2024346 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":8} -->\nP2: The root layout returns the entire `DocsSiteSource` (manifest with every page's body, the full search artifact, and config) from a server load. SvelteKit serializes this into the client payload of every page and every client-side navigation, even though the client only reads `source.config.navigation.topNav`, `source.config.site.showFooter`/`description`, and `source.siteTitle` (+layout.svelte, +page.svelte). `manifest` and `searchArtifact` are consumed only server-side by `/docs/[...slug]/+page.server.ts` via `parent()` (search already has its own `/search.json` endpoint), so the whole corpus and search index are duplicated into every HTML response. Return only the config fields the chrome needs and let child server loads import the state directly.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At extfn/docs/src/routes/+layout.server.ts, line 6:\n\n<comment>The root layout returns the entire `DocsSiteSource` (manifest with every page's body, the full search artifact, and config) from a server load. SvelteKit serializes this into the client payload of every page and every client-side navigation, even though the client only reads `source.config.navigation.topNav`, `source.config.site.showFooter`/`description`, and `source.siteTitle` (+layout.svelte, +page.svelte). `manifest` and `searchArtifact` are consumed only server-side by `/docs/[...slug]/+page.server.ts` via `parent()` (search already has its own `/search.json` endpoint), so the whole corpus and search index are duplicated into every HTML response. Return only the config fields the chrome needs and let child server loads import the state directly.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -0,0 +1,8 @@\n+\n+export const load: LayoutServerLoad = async () => {\n+  return {\n+    source: await loadDocsSiteSource(),\n+  };\n+};\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>\n\n✅ Addressed in [`3dd6ff1`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/3dd6ff1a256c8289979ff29b10f4a59a31869d47)\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNoga extfn/docs/vite.config.ts\n<!-- cubic:v=3f7dcd66-bd01-48b1-aaba-983ff346f98a -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=89d77ea6-21bc-5bb6-986a-2332a2024346 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":6} -->\nP2: Vite's string `find` aliases match by prefix, so these entries also intercept subpath imports. `searchfn/client/package.json` exports `@searchfn/client/constructors` and `@searchfn/client/in-memory-search`; if `@docsfn/core` or `@searchfn` source imports either, the import is rewritten to `searchfn/client/src/index.ts/constructors` (a non-existent path) instead of `src/constructors.ts`, breaking dev/build resolution. Anchor each alias with an anchored regex or a `$`-terminated find so only the bare specifier matches.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At extfn/docs/vite.config.ts, line 21:\n\n<comment>Vite's string `find` aliases match by prefix, so these entries also intercept subpath imports. `searchfn/client/package.json` exports `@searchfn/client/constructors` and `@searchfn/client/in-memory-search`; if `@docsfn/core` or `@searchfn` source imports either, the import is rewritten to `searchfn/client/src/index.ts/constructors` (a non-existent path) instead of `src/constructors.ts`, breaking dev/build resolution. Anchor each alias with an anchored regex or a `$`-terminated find so only the bare specifier matches.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -0,0 +1,28 @@\n+  },\n+  resolve: {\n+    alias: [\n+      { find: \"@searchfn/client\", replacement: path.resolve(dirname, \"../../searchfn/client/src/index.ts\") },\n+      { find: \"@searchfn/core\", replacement: path.resolve(dirname, \"../../searchfn/core/src/index.ts\") },\n+      { find: \"@searchfn/adapter-contracts\", replacement: path.resolve(dirname, \"../../searchfn/adapter-contracts/src/index.ts\") },\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>\n\n✅ Addressed in [`fec011e`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/fec011e7c940d9ddc09b282f33007d9c3ec1aca9)\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNogd extfn/docs/tsconfig.json\n<!-- cubic:v=16ae4880-db13-405a-9cb4-fe8c945a52f7 -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=89d77ea6-21bc-5bb6-986a-2332a2024346 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":7} -->\nP2: In tsconfig `extends`, the derived `include` replaces the `include` generated inside `.svelte-kit/tsconfig.json`, so `.svelte-kit/ambient.d.ts` and the generated types are left out of the TS program. Any `$env/*` import (or other kit-generated ambient type) will then fail with \"Cannot find module\" under svelte-check/editors while Vite build still passes. Note that `authfn/docs` and `filefn/docs` don't extend the kit config at all, and the repo's other SvelteKit apps (`filefn/examples/*/client/tsconfig.json`) extend it without overriding `include` — this file is the first to both extend and replace it. Add the `.svelte-kit` globs to `include` (or drop the block and let the generated config own the file list, keeping `vite.config.ts`/`svelte.config.js` covered).\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At extfn/docs/tsconfig.json, line 26:\n\n<comment>In tsconfig `extends`, the derived `include` replaces the `include` generated inside `.svelte-kit/tsconfig.json`, so `.svelte-kit/ambient.d.ts` and the generated types are left out of the TS program. Any `$env/*` import (or other kit-generated ambient type) will then fail with \"Cannot find module\" under svelte-check/editors while Vite build still passes. Note that `authfn/docs` and `filefn/docs` don't extend the kit config at all, and the repo's other SvelteKit apps (`filefn/examples/*/client/tsconfig.json`) extend it without overriding `include` — this file is the first to both extend and replace it. Add the `.svelte-kit` globs to `include` (or drop the block and let the generated config own the file list, keeping `vite.config.ts`/`svelte.config.js` covered).</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -0,0 +1,33 @@\n+      \"vite/client\"\n+    ]\n+  },\n+  \"include\": [\n+    \"src/**/*.ts\",\n+    \"src/**/*.js\",\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>\n\n```suggestion\n  \"include\": [\n    \".svelte-kit/ambient.d.ts\",\n    \".svelte-kit/types/**/*.d.ts\",\n    \"src/**/*.ts\",\n    \"src/**/*.js\",\n\n[873 more lines in file. Use offset=176 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1791331134868}}
{"type":"message","id":"0e7bff70","parentId":"30942fbd","timestamp":"2026-10-06T23:58:54.869Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_LchLmOp5PfwxUdiaG4i8LWxS|fc_055fb762f51dfcfc016ac58b3ebf4887d0ab1af07e120a77eb","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"    \"src/**/*.svelte\",\n    \"vite.config.ts\",\n    \"svelte.config.js\"\n  ]\n```\n\n✅ Addressed in [`fec011e`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/fec011e7c940d9ddc09b282f33007d9c3ec1aca9)\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNogf extfn/docs/content/docs/cli.md\n<!-- cubic:v=64e72c79-8e66-41e2-9f31-c002e7780093 -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=89d77ea6-21bc-5bb6-986a-2332a2024346 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":9} -->\nP2: `package` is not conditional: `runPackageCommand` calls `buildExtension` on every invocation before scanning or archiving. Document that it always rebuilds, or add an output-existence check before promising reuse. This can incur full builds and fail on source/config changes even when valid artifacts already exist.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At extfn/docs/content/docs/cli.md, line 8:\n\n<comment>`package` is not conditional: `runPackageCommand` calls `buildExtension` on every invocation before scanning or archiving. Document that it always rebuilds, or add an output-existence check before promising reuse. This can incur full builds and fail on source/config changes even when valid artifacts already exist.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@\n+\n+# CLI workflow\n+\n+`@extfn/cli` ships the `extfn` binary. `dev` watches exactly one target and supports `--open`, `--no-open`, and `--browser`. `build` builds all config targets by default or a selected target list. `scan` analyzes emitted files and manifests. `package` builds if needed, scans by default, and writes store-uploadable archives.\n+\n+```sh\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>\n\n✅ Addressed in [`fec011e`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/fec011e7c940d9ddc09b282f33007d9c3ec1aca9)\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNogk extfn/docs/content/docs/content-and-background.md\n<!-- cubic:v=8aac9b42-10d9-470a-be39-5b7cb24bfc36 -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=89d77ea6-21bc-5bb6-986a-2332a2024346 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":6} -->\nP3: The sentence lists `mount mode` as a per-content-script property, but the config puts `mountMode` on each anchor (selector/selector-list/resolver), not on the script itself. Rephrase so the script owns ID/entry/match patterns/anchors/style isolation and each anchor carries its own mount mode.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At extfn/docs/content/docs/content-and-background.md, line 8:\n\n<comment>The sentence lists `mount mode` as a per-content-script property, but the config puts `mountMode` on each anchor (selector/selector-list/resolver), not on the script itself. Rephrase so the script owns ID/entry/match patterns/anchors/style isolation and each anchor carries its own mount mode.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -0,0 +1,12 @@\n+\n+# Content and background handlers\n+\n+The config can declare several content scripts, each with its own ID, entry, match patterns, anchors, mount mode, and style isolation. Anchor kinds include `selector`, `selector-list`, and `resolver`; mount modes include `append`, `prepend`, `replace`, and `shadow`. The content helpers manage anchored mounting and reinjection.\n+\n+Background handlers are separate modules discovered from `messageHandlersDir` and `portHandlersDir`. A message handler uses `defineBackgroundHandler({ namespace, method, handle })`; a port handler uses `defineBackgroundPortHandler({ channel, onMessage })`. The namespace/method pair and port channel must each be unique across discovered handlers.\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>\n\n✅ Addressed in [`fec011e`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/fec011e7c940d9ddc09b282f33007d9c3ec1aca9)\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNogl extfn/docs/docsfn.config.ts\n<!-- cubic:v=4a365efe-16f0-45db-94f9-4583319cbcfa -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=89d77ea6-21bc-5bb6-986a-2332a2024346 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":6} -->\nP3: This site block omits `showFooter: false`, so the layout renders the default \"Built at 21n.co\" footer, while the sibling DocsFn sites authfn/docs/docsfn.config.ts and filefn/docs/docsfn.config.ts both set `showFooter: false`. Existing sites appear to deliberately suppress it; add it here for consistency unless the footer is intended.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At extfn/docs/docsfn.config.ts, line 8:\n\n<comment>This site block omits `showFooter: false`, so the layout renders the default \"Built at 21n.co\" footer, while the sibling DocsFn sites authfn/docs/docsfn.config.ts and filefn/docs/docsfn.config.ts both set `showFooter: false`. Existing sites appear to deliberately suppress it; add it here for consistency unless the footer is intended.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -0,0 +1,36 @@\n+  site: {\n+    title: \"ExtFn\",\n+    description: \"Browser extension configuration, runtime, build, scan, and packaging for Chromium and Firefox.\",\n+    basePath: \"/docs\",\n+    editLink: { pattern: \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/edit/dev/extfn/docs/{path}\" },\n+  },\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>\n\n```suggestion\n    basePath: \"/docs\",\n    showFooter: false,\n```\n\n✅ Addressed in [`8c1af41`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/8c1af4123a41b110375feb5aa98a4b68ad5f76b9)\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNogm extfn/docs/content/docs/configuration.md\n<!-- cubic:v=cc50b0fc-d611-4e9d-9f60-0ff02d94acc3 -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=89d77ea6-21bc-5bb6-986a-2332a2024346 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":6} -->\nP3: The example code block uses `defineExtension` without importing it, so a reader copying the snippet gets an unresolved-identifier error. `content/docs/getting-started.md` introduces the same example with `import { defineExtension } from \"@extfn/core\";`; add the matching import here or reference the getting-started guide.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At extfn/docs/content/docs/configuration.md, line 13:\n\n<comment>The example code block uses `defineExtension` without importing it, so a reader copying the snippet gets an unresolved-identifier error. `content/docs/getting-started.md` introduces the same example with `import { defineExtension } from \"@extfn/core\";`; add the matching import here or reference the getting-started guide.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -0,0 +1,31 @@\n+An example with modular background handlers:\n+\n+```ts\n+export default defineExtension({\n+  name: \"Example Extension\",\n+  version: \"0.1.0\",\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>\n\n```suggestion\nimport { defineExtension } from \"@extfn/core\";\n\nexport default defineExtension({\n```\n\n✅ Addressed in [`fec011e`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/fec011e7c940d9ddc09b282f33007d9c3ec1aca9)\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNogo extfn/docs/content/docs/runtime.md\n<!-- cubic:v=92a5513f-0079-4b6a-befd-8db36bc53a43 -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=89d77ea6-21bc-5bb6-986a-2332a2024346 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":8} -->\nP3: The example's `globals: globalThis as never` is redundant and teaches a bad pattern: `createRuntime` already defaults `globals` to `globalThis` and derives `rawBrowser` from `globals.browser ?? globals.chrome ?? {}` (extfn/core/src/runtime/getRuntime.ts:58-64), so both options add nothing here while `as never` is a confusing cast for readers to copy. Omit `globals` and `rawBrowser` entirely and keep only the explicit target.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At extfn/docs/content/docs/runtime.md, line 14:\n\n<comment>The example's `globals: globalThis as never` is redundant and teaches a bad pattern: `createRuntime` already defaults `globals` to `globalThis` and derives `rawBrowser` from `globals.browser ?? globals.chrome ?? {}` (extfn/core/src/runtime/getRuntime.ts:58-64), so both options add nothing here while `as never` is a confusing cast for readers to copy. Omit `globals` and `rawBrowser` entirely and keep only the explicit target.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -0,0 +1,26 @@\n+import { createRuntime } from \"@extfn/core\";\n+\n+const runtime = createRuntime({\n+  globals: globalThis as never,\n+  rawBrowser: (globalThis as { browser?: unknown; chrome?: unknown }).browser\n+    ?? (globalThis as { browser?: unknown; chrome?: unknown }).chrome\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>\n\n```suggestion\n  target: \"chromium-mv3\",\n```\n\n✅ Addressed in [`fec011e`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/fec011e7c940d9ddc09b282f33007d9c3ec1aca9)\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNogq extfn/docs/content/docs/reference/scan.md\n<!-- cubic:v=a9d6e688-119d-4687-a6a6-0d831dce355a -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=89d77ea6-21bc-5bb6-986a-2332a2024346 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":8} -->\nP3: The example for a custom report directory does not produce the report at the path shown. `resolveReportDir` in extfn/cli/src/commands/scan.ts resolves a relative `--report-dir` against `path.resolve(outDir, '..')` — the extension config directory — so running this command from the repo root writes the report to `extfn/examples/svelte-datafn-demo/extfn/examples/svelte-datafn-demo/dist/custom-scan/chromium-mv3.json` (the path is duplicated, since the example path already starts with `extfn/...`), not to `extfn/examples/svelte-datafn-demo/dist/custom-scan`. Use a path relative to the config directory instead, or note the base for relative `--report-dir` values.\n\n<details>\n\n[698 more lines in file. Use offset=351 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1791331134869}}
{"type":"message","id":"aec854ab","parentId":"0e7bff70","timestamp":"2026-10-06T23:58:54.869Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_zRhEmPyQcegHHms1Kto42Rtq|fc_055fb762f51dfcfc016ac58b3ebf5887d0b93b35cf122dcd67","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At extfn/docs/content/docs/reference/scan.md, line 94:\n\n<comment>The example for a custom report directory does not produce the report at the path shown. `resolveReportDir` in extfn/cli/src/commands/scan.ts resolves a relative `--report-dir` against `path.resolve(outDir, '..')` — the extension config directory — so running this command from the repo root writes the report to `extfn/examples/svelte-datafn-demo/extfn/examples/svelte-datafn-demo/dist/custom-scan/chromium-mv3.json` (the path is duplicated, since the example path already starts with `extfn/...`), not to `extfn/examples/svelte-datafn-demo/dist/custom-scan`. Use a path relative to the config directory instead, or note the base for relative `--report-dir` values.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -0,0 +1,116 @@\n+Custom report directory:\n+\n+```bash\n+npm exec extfn scan -- --config extfn/examples/svelte-datafn-demo/extfn.config.ts --report-dir extfn/examples/svelte-datafn-demo/dist/custom-scan\n+```\n+\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>\n\n```suggestion\nnpm exec extfn scan -- --config extfn/examples/svelte-datafn-demo/extfn.config.ts --report-dir dist/custom-scan\n```\n\n✅ Addressed in [`fec011e`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/fec011e7c940d9ddc09b282f33007d9c3ec1aca9)\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNogr extfn/docs/tsconfig.json\n<!-- cubic:v=7a2a8015-60df-4d71-81b5-0be4f103424f -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=89d77ea6-21bc-5bb6-986a-2332a2024346 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":5} -->\nP3: `types` restricts global type inclusion to `svelte` and `vite/client`, so `@types/node` (hoisted at the workspace root) is not loaded. With `checkJs: true` and `svelte.config.js` in `include`, `svelte-check`/`tsc`/editors will flag `process` in `svelte.config.js` (\"Cannot find name 'process'\"); `vite.config.ts`'s `node:path`/`node:url` imports also depend on `@types/node` being present. Either drop the `types` array so `@types/*` packages auto-load, or add `node` to the list.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At extfn/docs/tsconfig.json, line 21:\n\n<comment>`types` restricts global type inclusion to `svelte` and `vite/client`, so `@types/node` (hoisted at the workspace root) is not loaded. With `checkJs: true` and `svelte.config.js` in `include`, `svelte-check`/`tsc`/editors will flag `process` in `svelte.config.js` (\"Cannot find name 'process'\"); `vite.config.ts`'s `node:path`/`node:url` imports also depend on `@types/node` being present. Either drop the `types` array so `@types/*` packages auto-load, or add `node` to the list.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -0,0 +1,33 @@\n+      \"ES2022\",\n+      \"DOM\"\n+    ],\n+    \"types\": [\n+      \"svelte\",\n+      \"vite/client\"\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>\n\n```suggestion\n    \"types\": [\n      \"svelte\",\n      \"vite/client\",\n      \"node\"\n    ]\n```\n\n✅ Addressed in [`fec011e`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/fec011e7c940d9ddc09b282f33007d9c3ec1aca9)\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNpbG extfn/docs/package.json\n**Security issue**  \n🛑 Blocker — must fix before merge\n\n**Known vulnerabilities in svelte@5.0.0**\n\nOSV.dev reports 6 known vulnerabilities affecting `svelte@5.0.0`, introduced by this PR:\n\n- [GHSA-crpf-4hrx-3jrp](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-27125) **moderate**: Svelte SSR attribute spreading includes inherited properties from prototype chain — fixed in 5.51.5\n- [GHSA-f7gr-6p89-r883](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-27121) **moderate**: Svelte affected by cross-site scripting via spread attributes in Svelte SSR — fixed in 5.51.5\n- [GHSA-m56q-vw4c-c2cp](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-27122) **moderate**: Svelte SSR does not validate dynamic element tag names in `<svelte:element>` — fixed in 5.51.5\n\n…and 3 more — see the OSV links above.\n\nUpgrade to 5.51.5 or later.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn extfn/docs/package.json, upgrade the dependency svelte from 5.0.0 to a non-vulnerable version (5.51.5, 5.53.5, 5.55.7). Update any associated lockfile entries.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n> Not useful? Reply `@mira-rhombus reject` to dismiss this suggestion.\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNvgO extfn/docs/src/lib/components/DocsSiteSearch.svelte\nIn Cloudflare mode, the repo's docs Worker route matches only `/docs*`, so this absolute `/search.json` request bypasses the Worker that serves the new search endpoint. Search will fail on a docs host using the existing deployment pattern, even if the page under `/docs` loads.\n\n<details><summary>Technical details</summary>\n\n````markdown\n# Search endpoint outside Cloudflare route\n\n## Affected sites\n- `extfn/docs/src/lib/components/DocsSiteSearch.svelte:5` — fetches `/search.json`.\n- `extfn/docs/src/routes/search.json/+server.ts:5-8` — registers the handler at `/search.json`.\n- `scripts/cloudflare-docs/config.mjs:101-108` — Worker pattern is `${host}/docs*`.\n\n## Required outcome\n- Keep the search request and server endpoint within the configured Worker route, or explicitly route the root endpoint to the same Worker when ExtFn is deployed.\n````\n\n</details>\n\nAddressed in fec011e by moving both the search fetch and endpoint under /docs/search.json.\n\n<!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ -->\n<sup><a href=\"https://pullfrog.com\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\"><img src=\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\" width=\"9px\" height=\"9px\" style=\"vertical-align: middle; \" alt=\"Pullfrog\"></picture></a>&nbsp;&nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/36233492935/job/108380936639) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)</sup>\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNvgQ extfn/docs/content/docs/reference/consumer-host-abstraction.md\nThe guide includes content mounts as consumers of this host, but content scripts cannot call `tabs.create` directly ([MDN](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Mozilla/Add-ons/WebExtensions/Content_scripts#webextension_apis)). A shared panel using this `goto()` from a content mount will reject with `E_CONTEXT_UNAVAILABLE` instead of navigating.\n\n<details><summary>Technical details</summary>\n\n````markdown\n# Navigation in content mounts\n\n## Affected sites\n- `extfn/docs/content/docs/reference/consumer-host-abstraction.md:16-20,90-94` — the example applies one adapter to pages and content mounts.\n- `extfn/core/src/runtime/browser.ts:31-42` — missing browser methods reject with `E_CONTEXT_UNAVAILABLE`.\n- `extfn/docs/consumer-host-abstraction.md:85-91` — the mirrored root guide has the same example.\n\n## Required outcome\n- Show a navigation adapter valid for the contexts the guide promises, or explicitly scope this adapter to extension pages and show content mounts relaying privileged tab creation through a background handler. Keep the mirrored guide aligned.\n````\n\n</details>\n\nAddressed in fec011e by routing content navigation through the host page and extension-page tab creation through the browser facade.\n\n<!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ -->\n<sup><a href=\"https://pullfrog.com\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\"><img src=\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\" width=\"9px\" height=\"9px\" style=\"vertical-align: middle; \" alt=\"Pullfrog\"></picture></a>&nbsp;&nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/36233492935/job/108380936639) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)</sup>\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNvgR extfn/docs/content/docs/reference/consumer-host-abstraction.md\n`runtime.address.context` is a context label such as `\"popup\"` or `\"content\"`, not the current URL pathname returned by the SvelteKit adapter above. Shared route-aware UI using the stated `currentPath()` contract will see the wrong location in extension surfaces.\n\n<details><summary>Technical details</summary>\n\n````markdown\n# Extension currentPath contract\n\n## Affected sites\n- `extfn/docs/content/docs/reference/consumer-host-abstraction.md:29-31,64-66,95-97` — interface and web adapter describe a pathname but extension adapter returns a context enum.\n- `extfn/core/src/runtime/context.ts:4-17` — `RuntimeAddress.context` is a context kind.\n- `extfn/docs/consumer-host-abstraction.md:90-92` — the mirrored root guide has the same mismatch.\n\n## Required outcome\n- Make `currentPath()` represent an actual pathname in both host adapters, or change the host contract and both implementations to explicitly model different navigation semantics. Keep the mirrored guide aligned.\n````\n\n</details>\n\nAddressed in fec011e by returning the document pathname in both mirrored guides.\n\n<!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ -->\n<sup><a href=\"https://pullfrog.com\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\"><img src=\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\" width=\"9px\" height=\"9px\" style=\"vertical-align: middle; \" alt=\"Pullfrog\"></picture></a>&nbsp;&nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/36233492935/job/108380936639) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)</sup>\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNzq1 extfn/docs/src/app.css\n<!-- cubic:v=14c062be-3481-4a31-a39d-5f10b50ad1b2 -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=062ac4fa-f9cd-5b7a-bd4b-d89f86693fc7 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":5} -->\nP2: This rule wins only if the theme hides the mobile sidebar with `display: none` on the `.docsfn-sidebar-col` element itself; if the theme hides the drawer via visibility, transform, width/grid collapse, or a `--open` class on a wrapper element, `display: block` never re-shows it, and showing it inline in flow doesn't make it an overlay drawer. It also pins the site to theme internals and duplicates a 1023px magic breakpoint that can silently drift on a `@docsfn/svelte` upgrade. Verify the override against the installed theme.css (confirm the hide mechanism and where `--open` is toggled) and note the version + the theme rule this mirrors near this code so a future upgrade is caught; ideally drive open state through the theme's own drawer handling instead of a specificity patch.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At extfn/docs/src/app.css, line 76:\n\n[523 more lines in file. Use offset=526 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1791331134869}}
