{"type":"message","id":"14f8f31b","parentId":"41a3e3f8","timestamp":"2026-10-06T23:59:00.404Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_22d0c35bd5f7467b93f954e87ab59400|fc_055fb762f51dfcfc016ac58b420bc887d0aef9563f4f74ce4f","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n<comment>This rule wins only if the theme hides the mobile sidebar with `display: none` on the `.docsfn-sidebar-col` element itself; if the theme hides the drawer via visibility, transform, width/grid collapse, or a `--open` class on a wrapper element, `display: block` never re-shows it, and showing it inline in flow doesn't make it an overlay drawer. It also pins the site to theme internals and duplicates a 1023px magic breakpoint that can silently drift on a `@docsfn/svelte` upgrade. Verify the override against the installed theme.css (confirm the hide mechanism and where `--open` is toggled) and note the version + the theme rule this mirrors near this code so a future upgrade is caught; ideally drive open state through the theme's own drawer handling instead of a specificity patch.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -70,3 +70,8 @@ body {\n+\n+/* The published theme hides this column on mobile; an open drawer must override it. */\n+@media (max-width: 1023px) {\n+  .docsfn-sidebar-col.docsfn-sidebar-col--open { display: block; }\n+}\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>\n\n✅ Addressed in [`fec011e`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/fec011e7c940d9ddc09b282f33007d9c3ec1aca9)\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNzq4 extfn/docs/vite.config.ts\n<!-- cubic:v=2151a600-133d-49d5-8309-4c7fc40830c0 -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=062ac4fa-f9cd-5b7a-bd4b-d89f86693fc7 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":8} -->\nP2: These aliases rely on synchronous `import.meta.resolve`, which only exists unflagged from Node 18.19.0/20.6.0, but the root `engines` floor is `>=18.17.0`. On Node 18.17-18.18 the config file throws during load, breaking `vite dev` and `vite build` for those versions. Use `createRequire(import.meta.url).resolve(...)` (Node 12.2+, sync, Windows-safe) instead of `import.meta.resolve`, matching the existing `dirname` pattern.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At extfn/docs/vite.config.ts, line 22:\n\n<comment>These aliases rely on synchronous `import.meta.resolve`, which only exists unflagged from Node 18.19.0/20.6.0, but the root `engines` floor is `>=18.17.0`. On Node 18.17-18.18 the config file throws during load, breaking `vite dev` and `vite build` for those versions. Use `createRequire(import.meta.url).resolve(...)` (Node 12.2+, sync, Windows-safe) instead of `import.meta.resolve`, matching the existing `dirname` pattern.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -18,6 +18,9 @@ export default defineConfig({\n   resolve: {\n     alias: [\n+      // Resolve shared source against this site's pinned DocsFn installation.\n+      { find: /^@docsfn\\/core$/, replacement: fileURLToPath(import.meta.resolve(\"@docsfn/core\")) },\n+      { find: \"@docsfn/core/search-runtime\", replacement: fileURLToPath(import.meta.resolve(\"@docsfn/core/search-runtime\")) },\n       { find: \"@searchfn/client\", replacement: path.resolve(dirname, \"../../searchfn/client/src/index.ts\") },\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>\n\n✅ Addressed in [`fec011e`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/fec011e7c940d9ddc09b282f33007d9c3ec1aca9)\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mN94Z extfn/docs/src/app.css\nThe override makes the mobile sidebar visible, but the pinned DocsFn drawer is fixed at `top: 0` with `z-index: 40`, while `TopBar` remains sticky at `z-index: 50`. The header therefore covers the beginning of the sidebar, including its first navigation entries, so mobile readers cannot reach them normally.\n\n<details><summary>Technical details</summary>\n\n````markdown\n# Mobile drawer hidden beneath header\n\n## Affected sites\n- `extfn/docs/src/app.css:75-77` — the new override reveals the drawer without accounting for its position beneath the top bar.\n- `@docsfn/svelte@0.0.3/src/DocsLayout.svelte` — mobile sidebar is fixed at top: 0 with z-index: 40, and backdrop uses z-index: 30.\n- `@docsfn/svelte@0.0.3/dist/theme-base.css` — sticky top bar uses z-index: 50.\n\n## Required outcome\n- Keep the opened sidebar's first links visible and clickable at mobile widths, whether by stacking the drawer above the header or offsetting the drawer below it.\n````\n\n</details>\n\nAddressed in fec011e by offsetting the open drawer below the measured top bar and reducing its viewport height.\n\n<!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ -->\n<sup><a href=\"https://pullfrog.com\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\"><img src=\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\" width=\"9px\" height=\"9px\" style=\"vertical-align: middle; \" alt=\"Pullfrog\"></picture></a>&nbsp;&nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/36233492935/job/108380936639) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)</sup>\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mPpj3 extfn/docs/README.md\n<!-- cubic:v=ace3b9ec-0634-4982-8cca-e55e460eff94 -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=804fce71-3bb1-546d-b7cc-49349a868699 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":8} -->\nP3: The closing prose line is indented with two spaces, so it visually attaches to the preceding code fence and reads as a continuation of the shell block. Remove the leading indentation to restore it to a normal paragraph.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At extfn/docs/README.md, line 22:\n\n<comment>The closing prose line is indented with two spaces, so it visually attaches to the preceding code fence and reads as a continuation of the shell block. Remove the leading indentation to restore it to a normal paragraph.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -9,4 +9,14 @@ npm --workspace @extfn/docs run dev\n+npm run build --workspace @searchfn/client\n+npm exec --workspace @extfn/docs -- docsfn validate --root .\n+```\n+  The site defaults to port 6015. Set `site.canonicalUrl` in `docsfn.config.ts` after the public host is assigned.\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>\n\n```suggestion\nThe site defaults to port 6015. Set `site.canonicalUrl` in `docsfn.config.ts` after the public host is assigned.\n```\n\n✅ Addressed in [`dd11b96`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/dd11b96aea70743b7838ae7e5dd5e467c1ec2f64)\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mPpj- scripts/docs-site/layout.ts\n<!-- cubic:v=26e2d91d-2cd4-4e2d-a9de-da3646bb3536 -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=804fce71-3bb1-546d-b7cc-49349a868699 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":6} -->\nP3: `observeTopBar` silently returns a no-op when `.docsfn-topbar` isn't found, leaving the hardcoded `--docsfn-sticky-top-offset: 4rem` fallback in `extfn/docs/src/app.css` in effect — the same wrapped-mobile-links mismatch this helper exists to correct. TopBar is always rendered today, but this is shared runtime code that new site PRs copy (per `scripts/docs-site/README.md`), so a selector or theme-class drift would degrade the sticky drawer with no diagnosable signal. Log a warning from the no-op path so the fallback is observable.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At scripts/docs-site/layout.ts, line 4:\n\n<comment>`observeTopBar` silently returns a no-op when `.docsfn-topbar` isn't found, leaving the hardcoded `--docsfn-sticky-top-offset: 4rem` fallback in `extfn/docs/src/app.css` in effect — the same wrapped-mobile-links mismatch this helper exists to correct. TopBar is always rendered today, but this is shared runtime code that new site PRs copy (per `scripts/docs-site/README.md`), so a selector or theme-class drift would degrade the sticky drawer with no diagnosable signal. Log a warning from the no-op path so the fallback is observable.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -0,0 +1,10 @@\n+/** Keep sticky navigation below the actual top bar, including wrapped mobile links. */\n+export function observeTopBar(root: HTMLElement): () => void {\n+  const bar = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>(\".docsfn-topbar\");\n+  if (!bar) return () => {};\n+  const update = () => root.style.setProperty(\"--docsfn-sticky-top-offset\", `${bar.getBoundingClientRect().height}px`);\n+  update();\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>\n\n✅ Addressed in [`d10fbdb`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/d10fbdba0d2b61cc5beaff8741e914a24a72e215)\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mPpkC extfn/docs/src/app.css\n<!-- cubic:v=d98941ad-d77c-4487-9750-750d4c609faa -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=804fce71-3bb1-546d-b7cc-49349a868699 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":6} -->\nP3: `height: calc(100dvh - ...)` has no `vh` fallback. On engines without `dvh` support the declaration is dropped, so the open drawer keeps the theme's full-height sizing while gaining the new `top` offset, pushing its bottom edge past the viewport and making the last nav items unreachable. Add a `100vh` fallback line before the `dvh` one.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At extfn/docs/src/app.css, line 82:\n\n<comment>`height: calc(100dvh - ...)` has no `vh` fallback. On engines without `dvh` support the declaration is dropped, so the open drawer keeps the theme's full-height sizing while gaining the new `top` offset, pushing its bottom edge past the viewport and making the last nav items unreachable. Add a `100vh` fallback line before the `dvh` one.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -71,7 +71,14 @@ body {\n+  .docsfn-site-root .docsfn-sidebar-col.docsfn-sidebar-col--open {\n+    display: block;\n+    top: var(--docsfn-sticky-top-offset);\n+    height: calc(100dvh - var(--docsfn-sticky-top-offset));\n+  }\n }\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>\n\n```suggestion\n    height: calc(100vh - var(--docsfn-sticky-top-offset));\n    height: calc(100dvh - var(--docsfn-sticky-top-offset));\n```\n\n✅ Addressed in [`8c1af41`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/8c1af4123a41b110375feb5aa98a4b68ad5f76b9)\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mPrKM extfn/docs/package.json\n**Security issue**  \n🛑 Blocker — must fix before merge\n\n**Known vulnerabilities in vite@5.4.0**\n\nOSV.dev reports 15 known vulnerabilities affecting `vite@5.4.0`, introduced by this PR:\n\n- [GHSA-356w-63v5-8wf4](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-32395) **moderate**: Vite has an `server.fs.deny` bypass with an invalid `request-target` — fixed in 6.2.6, 6.1.5, 6.0.15, 5.4.18, 4.5.13\n- [GHSA-4r4m-qw57-chr8](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-31125) **moderate**: Vite has a `server.fs.deny` bypassed for `inline` and `raw` with `?import` query — fixed in 6.2.4, 6.1.3, 6.0.13, 5.4.16, 4.5.11\n- [GHSA-4w7w-66w2-5vf9](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-39365) **moderate**: Vite Vulnerable to Path Traversal in Optimized Deps `.map` Handling — fixed in 8.0.5, 7.3.2, 6.4.2\n\n[348 more lines in file. Use offset=701 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1791331140404}}
{"type":"message","id":"a151bc24","parentId":"14f8f31b","timestamp":"2026-10-06T23:59:00.405Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_b3fa677f15b3491e833203dbca2b3549|fc_055fb762f51dfcfc016ac58b443afc87d0aeb016bf2282d759","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n…and 12 more — see the OSV links above.\n\nUpgrade to 6.2.6, 6.1.5, 6.0.15, 5.4.18, 4.5.13 or later.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn extfn/docs/package.json, upgrade the dependency vite from 5.4.0 to a non-vulnerable version (0.1.24, 2.14.1, 2.9.0, 3.2.11, 4.5.10, 4.5.11, 4.5.12, 4.5.13, 4.5.14, 4.5.4, 4.5.6, 5.2.14, 5.3.6, 5.4.12, 5.4.15, 5.4.16, 5.4.17, 5.4.18, 5.4.19, 5.4.20, 5.4.21, 5.4.6, 5.4.9, 6.0.12, 6.0.13, 6.0.14, 6.0.15, 6.0.9, 6.1.2, 6.1.3, 6.1.4, 6.1.5, 6.1.6, 6.2.3, 6.2.4, 6.2.5, 6.2.6, 6.2.7, 6.3.4, 6.3.6, 6.4.1, 6.4.2, 6.4.3, 7.0.7, 7.0.8, 7.1.11, 7.1.5, 7.3.2, 7.3.5, 8.0.16, 8.0.5). Update any associated lockfile entries.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n> Not useful? Reply `@mira-rhombus reject` to dismiss this suggestion.\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mP2_J scripts/docs-site/README.md\n<!-- cubic:v=20ac4afe-88a5-41e5-947e-3a8cc4aac7a3 -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=7c66403b-fcbb-598b-9cd0-5dfbd7ebe6ff -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":10} -->\nP2: This says all factory wrappers use the canonical runtime, but AuthFn and FileFn still define local `docs-site-source.ts` copies and do not import `scripts/docs-site/runtime`. Following this guidance will make shared runtime edits silently miss those sites; document the exceptions or migrate them first.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At scripts/docs-site/README.md, line 9:\n\n<comment>This says all factory wrappers use the canonical runtime, but AuthFn and FileFn still define local `docs-site-source.ts` copies and do not import `scripts/docs-site/runtime`. Following this guidance will make shared runtime edits silently miss those sites; document the exceptions or migrate them first.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -4,8 +4,12 @@ The new per-function sites supply their config and Vite raw-content globs to `cr\n+Each site resolves the shared module's DocsFn imports through the scoped Vite resolver so it uses the versions pinned by that site. Run `npm run build` in the affected `<function>/docs` directory. After changing shared code, build all consumers and verify desktop search (including a result navigation and Escape) plus the mobile Menu drawer. Keep the responsive open-drawer override when using the current published theme.\n \n-The new-site PRs carry identical copies of this shared directory so they can land independently. Once merged, edits belong here rather than in the small per-site factory wrappers.\n+Each new-site PR includes this shared directory at the same repository path so it can land independently. All factory wrappers reference this one canonical directory. After merge, edit it directly rather than duplicating provider logic in individual sites.\n \n-AuthFn and FileFn currently retain their existing runtime copies; edits here affect only sites whose factory wrappers import this directory. Migrate those consumers in their respective PRs before treating this as the runtime for every SvelteKit docs site.\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>\n\n```suggestion\nEach new-site PR includes this shared directory at the same repository path so it can land independently. Wrappers that import it use this canonical runtime; AuthFn and FileFn still retain local copies until their migrations land. After merge, edit it directly rather than duplicating provider logic in individual sites.\n```\n\n✅ Addressed in [`d10fbdb`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/d10fbdba0d2b61cc5beaff8741e914a24a72e215)\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mP2_K extfn/docs/src/lib/server/docs-site-source.ts\n<!-- cubic:v=ca7a4445-73b0-46e2-b116-b0263d12dfb5 -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=7c66403b-fcbb-598b-9cd0-5dfbd7ebe6ff -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":6} -->\nP3: This glob restrictively narrows the bundled static assets to .txt/.json/.md, but `createDocsSiteRuntime` treats every file under `static/` as an asset entry (extension-agnostic `createAssetEntry`), so any future non-listed asset (e.g. .svg, .png, .xml, .webmanifest) added to `extfn/docs/static` will silently disappear from the manifest's assets collection with no error. The change also diverges from the sibling sites `authfn/docs/src/lib/server/docs-site-source.ts:30` and `filefn/docs/src/lib/server/docs-site-source.ts:30`, which both use the unrestricted `static/**/*` glob. Keep the unrestricted glob (matching the other sites) or add a comment documenting why only these three types are intended.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At extfn/docs/src/lib/server/docs-site-source.ts, line 7:\n\n<comment>This glob restrictively narrows the bundled static assets to .txt/.json/.md, but `createDocsSiteRuntime` treats every file under `static/` as an asset entry (extension-agnostic `createAssetEntry`), so any future non-listed asset (e.g. .svg, .png, .xml, .webmanifest) added to `extfn/docs/static` will silently disappear from the manifest's assets collection with no error. The change also diverges from the sibling sites `authfn/docs/src/lib/server/docs-site-source.ts:30` and `filefn/docs/src/lib/server/docs-site-source.ts:30`, which both use the unrestricted `static/**/*` glob. Keep the unrestricted glob (matching the other sites) or add a comment documenting why only these three types are intended.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -4,7 +4,7 @@ import { createDocsSiteRuntime } from \"../../../../../scripts/docs-site/runtime\"\n   query: \"?raw\", import: \"default\", eager: true,\n }) as Record<string, string>;\n-const assets = import.meta.glob(\"../../../static/**/*\", {\n+const assets = import.meta.glob(\"../../../static/**/*.{txt,json,md}\", {\n   query: \"?raw\", import: \"default\", eager: true,\n }) as Record<string, string>;\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>\n\n```suggestion\nconst assets = import.meta.glob(\"../../../static/**/*\", {\n```\n\n✅ Addressed in [`d10fbdb`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/d10fbdba0d2b61cc5beaff8741e914a24a72e215)\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mP2_L scripts/docs-site/LandingPage.svelte\n<!-- cubic:v=9ee47608-d1eb-4bc9-b55e-d0259be804be -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=7c66403b-fcbb-598b-9cd0-5dfbd7ebe6ff -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":7} -->\nP3: Landing quick-link cards only change appearance on `:hover`; keyboard users who Tab to a card get the browser default outline with none of the designed interaction cue. Add a `:focus-visible` rule mirroring the hover styles (border-color, box-shadow, translateY) so keyboard focus state matches the hover state.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At scripts/docs-site/LandingPage.svelte, line 178:\n\n<comment>Landing quick-link cards only change appearance on `:hover`; keyboard users who Tab to a card get the browser default outline with none of the designed interaction cue. Add a `:focus-visible` rule mirroring the hover styles (border-color, box-shadow, translateY) so keyboard focus state matches the hover state.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -0,0 +1,216 @@\n+      transform 0.15s ease;\n+  }\n+\n+  .landing-card:hover {\n+    border-color: var(--docsfn-color-primary);\n+    box-shadow: 0 8px 28px rgb(37 99 235 / 0.12);\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>\n\n✅ Addressed in [`8c1af41`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/8c1af4123a41b110375feb5aa98a4b68ad5f76b9)\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mP2_M scripts/docs-site/vitest.config.ts\n<!-- cubic:v=1f5ecf6d-dd1c-4770-a9b1-85ae24f45309 -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=7c66403b-fcbb-598b-9cd0-5dfbd7ebe6ff -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":7} -->\nP3: The plugin anchor resolves the site's package.json from `process.cwd()`, but the test root is fixed to this directory, so the config's behavior depends entirely on where vitest happens to be invoked. Running it from anywhere but a consuming site (e.g. `scripts/docs-site` or the repo root, the natural places given the test file and config live here) makes `createRequire(...package.json).resolve(\"@docsfn/core\")` in `docsSiteCorePlugin` throw MODULE_NOT_FOUND at config load, or silently pin a different hoisted version when one resolves — with no hint in the error. I verified there is no package.json in `scripts/docs-site` or `scripts/`, and resolving from there fails with `ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND`. The single supported invocation is `npm test` in `extfn/docs`, which the README documents but nothing enforces. Fail fast with a descriptive error when `process.cwd()/package.json` does not exist or does not provide `@docsfn/core`, so a wrong invocation doesn't produce a confusing crash (or worse, silent wrong-version resolution).\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At scripts/docs-site/vitest.config.ts, line 7:\n\n<comment>The plugin anchor resolves the site's package.json from `process.cwd()`, but the test root is fixed to this directory, so the config's behavior depends entirely on where vitest happens to be invoked. Running it from anywhere but a consuming site (e.g. `scripts/docs-site` or the repo root, the natural places given the test file and config live here) makes `createRequire(...package.json).resolve(\"@docsfn/core\")` in `docsSiteCorePlugin` throw MODULE_NOT_FOUND at config load, or silently pin a different hoisted version when one resolves — with no hint in the error. I verified there is no package.json in `scripts/docs-site` or `scripts/`, and resolving from there fails with `ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND`. The single supported invocation is `npm test` in `extfn/docs`, which the README documents but nothing enforces. Fail fast with a descriptive error when `process.cwd()/package.json` does not exist or does not provide `@docsfn/core`, so a wrong invocation doesn't produce a confusing crash (or worse, silent wrong-version resolution).</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@\n+import { docsSiteCorePlugin } from \"./vite\";\n+\n+export default defineConfig({\n+  plugins: [docsSiteCorePlugin(pathToFileURL(resolve(process.cwd(), \"package.json\")).href)],\n+  test: { root: fileURLToPath(new URL(\".\", import.meta.url)), include: [\"runtime.test.ts\"] },\n+});\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>\n\n✅ Addressed in [`f15540d`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/f15540d26c2329203c626ccb51eb9108c5bebd84)\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6nFylE scripts/cloudflare-docs/config.mjs\nRegistering `extfn` here makes the deploy workflow upload its Worker, but the separate route-sync workflow still cannot select `extfn` for a targeted `/docs*` binding. A successful deploy therefore does not activate either new docs host unless an operator syncs *all* product routes; please wire ExtFn into the route workflow before relying on the new deploy target.\n\n<details><summary>Technical details</summary>\n\n````markdown\n# ExtFn route activation is not independently selectable\n\n## Affected sites\n- `scripts/cloudflare-docs/config.mjs:8-17` — introduces both ExtFn hosts and their Worker route definitions.\n- `.github/workflows/superfunctions-docs-cloudflare-deploy.yml:115-119` — deploys the Worker but does not sync its zone route.\n- `.github/workflows/superfunctions-docs-cloudflare-routes.yml:14-19,43-50` — excludes `extfn` from dispatch choices and omits `CLOUDFLARE_ZONE_ID_EXTFN_COM`; `all` is the only selectable route-sync path and falls back to a Cloudflare zone lookup.\n\n## Required outcome\n- Allow the route-sync workflow to bind ExtFn's `/docs*` routes for dev and live without selecting and updating unrelated products; provide the zone ID input or ensure the route token can resolve the new zone.\n````\n\n</details>\n\nAddressed in d10fbdb by adding the ExtFn dispatch choice and zone ID to the route-sync workflow.\n\n<!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ -->\n<sup><a href=\"https://pullfrog.com\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\"><img src=\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\" width=\"9px\" height=\"9px\" style=\"vertical-align: middle; \" alt=\"Pullfrog\"></picture></a>&nbsp;&nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/36613785447/job/109561531905) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)</sup>\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6nF0_J extfn/docs/docsfn.config.ts\n<!-- cubic:v=614d870f-e7c9-4b37-8a48-ef8f55305038 -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=e3600364-f803-5837-8cd7-4222d9e23753 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":6} -->\nP2: Removing `canonicalUrl` drops the site's absolute public URLs now that this PR wires deployment to extfn.com/docs. With it absent, `buildCanonicalUrl(undefined, route)` in `+page.server.ts` returns a bare relative path as the page canonical, and `withSourceLinks` in scripts/docs-site/llms.mjs rewrites every `/docs/...` link to GitHub blob pages instead of the live docs host (the regenerated static/llms.txt and llms-full.txt confirm the links now point at github.com). Restore `canonicalUrl: \"https://extfn.com\"` and regenerate the LLM artifacts so the public index links to the docs site; if keeping the host-less fallback is deliberate for dev/prod domain sharing, document that in the config so the GitHub-link artifacts don't read as an oversight.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n\n[173 more lines in file. Use offset=876 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1791331140404}}
