es (primary.txt lines1–826) and all34 resolved bodies (resolved34-bodies.txt complete), plus the 4364-line novel/different human-source patch, have now been visibly read in bounded untruncated chunks. Historical exact supplementary-body/source reuse still retains previous visibility/pre-use qualifications. Generated corpora and lock are not fully assessed yet. No source mutation, commit, push, merge or reviewer mutation.\n\n## Actionable (10 surfaces, deduplicated below)\n\n- PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6n0Q4k / PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6n0Wlk / PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6n0Wlr: AuthFn advertises /docs/llms*.txt with no exact native handlers. Correct endpoints together, not merely remove /docs from links that must stay within Worker selection. Native HTTP negative/positive required; current finding is supported by exact tracked route/source inventory, not a new live-host claim.\n- PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6n0VHS: ExtFn getting-started still says package builds if needed. Reference/mirrored CLI already correctly say always rebuilds. Refresh source and generated corpus together; actual runPackageCommand caller remains authoritative.\n- PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6n0VHb: FileFn strict-rate-limit generated example needs matching current createFileFn stores.atomicKv/CAS wiring. Compose reviewed preparation-base API owner and source docs together; no direct generated-only patch.\n- PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6n0VHh: shared writer directly truncates public paths. Independent native OS reader/writer negative observed nine violations; see old-native-artifact-reader-boundary.log. Unique same-directory temp/rename and failure/mode guards required; no pair transaction/power-loss claim.\n- PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6n0VHk: AuthFn/FileFn directly consume shared runtime importing gray-matter but do not declare it. ExtFn already declares it. Owner-aware plugin enforcement is also necessary: actual isolated Vite6.4.3 SSR/loopback negative returns500 for gray-matter even through a receiver declaring it; declaration alone is not complete ownership repair. Borrowed receiver proof is audit-only.\n- PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6n0Wlo: actual Turbo frozen workspace/config dry-run yields identical three consumer build hashes for distinct public origins. Hash all relevant output roles in actual supported configuration and test propagation/inheritance, not a string-only deploy check.\n- PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6n0Wlz: FileFn AI guide host siblings remain to reconcile with canonical filefn.com; regenerate body with source correction and native endpoint check.\n- PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6n0Wl2: first origin matrix uses directory symlinks without Windows handling, while only second test is Windows-guarded. Prefer explicit Windows junction semantics for existing absolute directories; do not claim Windows execution from macOS.\n\nThese10 surfaces identify8 deduplicated direct primary causes: AuthFn endpoints, CLI getting-started, FileFn strict docs, atomic writer, parser dependency/owner resolution, Turbo public-role cache, FileFn guide host, Windows fixture link ownership. Related provider/DTO/title/layout/generated/cache siblings remain part of the coordinated scope, not separate rounds.\n\n## Skipped (Already Fixed / Stale) — 9\n\n- PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNogg / PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNz7d: both mirrored host examples now return globalThis.location?.pathname; content navigation is explicitly scoped to location.assign, extension pages to tabs.create. No context-kind currentPath remains in inspected examples.\n- PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNogi: original local parser replaced by shared gray-matter; actual structured-YAML/BOM/CRLF regression source exists. Need native current acceptance after ownership repair; do not replace it with a bespoke fence parser.\n- PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNogn: ExtFn wrapper now exports only loadDocsSiteSource/getCompiledDocsPage; shared post/cache/search interfaces have actual sibling owners. Do not remove shared native blog/cache contracts because this particular consumer has no posts.\n- PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNzqx: source deployment generator already emits nodejs_compat. Frozen executing guarded deploy test checks flag, but live Worker execution/deployment is excluded and not proved.\n- PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mP3IH / PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6nFwIM / PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6nF0_U: ExtFn registry/host, deployment paths/options/tags and separate route workflow option/EXTFN_COM zone input are present. Both dev/live hosts belong to extfn.com, so a separate DEV zone input is not inherently required. Code wiring is not proof routes/secrets/live hosts exist.\n- PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6nPuhT: reference/cli and mirrored CLI now unambiguously say always rebuilds selected targets before scanning/archive. Getting-started sibling remains separately Actionable and must be fixed in same batch.\n\n## Invalid — 3\n\n- PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mPpj0: current ExtFn Vite config has SearchFn-only aliases, not a second @site/docs-search mapping. Kit alias is the present owner used by DocsSiteSearch and generated typing. Removing it on this stale duplicate claim would break ownership.\n- PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mPs38: finding text names scripts/verify-uifn-react-18-runtime.mjs constructor, not current layout.ts. Do not mutate unrelated UIFn verification or suppress its finding globally.\n- PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6nPyrp: absence of direct docs text imports does not prove unused dependencies. Actual AuthFn OpenAPI generator imports social OAuth; social-oauth/src/index.ts imports @superfunctions/oauth-flow; oauth-support.ts imports SuperfunctionObservability type. Transitive build/type owner graph is relevant. Preserve peers pending current physical/build graph acceptance; no blind dependency removal.\n\n## Resolved34 and new related variants\n\nResolved state is not evidence of correctness. Source inspection confirms prior fixes for parsing delegation, ExtFn lean layout, anchored SearchFn aliases, Kit include ownership/Node types, conditional-build/mount-mode/import examples, footer, runtime defaults, report-directory base, known Svelte/Vite floors, /docs search, host navigation/path, mobile offset/fallback, warning, documentation runtime adoption, keyboard focus, config diagnostic/workspace hint, actual apifn/docsfn selector path, canonical/default-generator origin and static-title removal. Keep their positives while reconciling.\n\nNew related current variants needing coordinated acceptance: flat.md with descendant route resolves wrong sibling link (actual same-version SDK render negative); guessed Core file and unowned Kit/parser imports; AuthFn/FileFn parent full-source payload/caller ownership; static raw binary inclusion must become six text extensions with native binary passthrough; shared observer nonzero-height guard, reduced-motion styling and explicit normal/error title ownership; executing config public-origin roles as well as generator roles. Reviewed #212 source may be reused only by explicit path/byte/mode/provenance plan, never by assuming its installations already prove #213.\n\n## Parallel check/supplementary constraints\n\nFrozen checks:30success/5skip/2failure. JavaScript SecFn audit errors109/112 are concrete DB transaction API owner mismatches; reviewed42a preparation base must be assessed/composed rather than reverting it. Sonar C/A and concrete annotations remain individually assessable; async provider methods preserve Promise/rejection ABI, and static-title request cannot override one dynamic normal/error title contract. Docstring17.07%/80% remains uncleared. Codex review quota, Kody/Mira no-findings summaries and Socket dependency scores do not establish complete review or security/merge clearance.\n\nMutation/publication gates remain closed pending full canonical/generated/lock assessment, four-field machine ledger gate, immutable source plan, exact archives, physical/native acceptance and staging/ancestry guards. This is pre-edit classification, not final dispositions or proof of convergence; valid scoped causes after remain unchanged because no repair applied.\n"}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-6.1-sol"