=\",\"summary\":[]}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_KcUVwARKbzBfZ0I0VPHRkLRG|fc_055fb762f51dfcfc016ac5ce2e226487d09004807276fce66d","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/audits/sf-docs-review-20260930/sequential-20261003T184612Z/PR-213/source-composition-pre-use-assessment.md","content":"# #213 proposed composition — pre-use assessment, not publication clearance\n\n## Exact inputs and scope\n\nFrozen head remains f15540d26c2329203c626ccb51eb9108c5bebd84; one frozen collection, zero publications. The original 203-entry plan remains immutable. The 18-path composition supplement and subsequent three-path guide/platform supplement are separately hashed, explicit amendments, adding only FileFn's AI index and an atomic-writer test beyond that original plan. No application root or installation has changed.\n\nAll 8,314 retained #212 canonical source/absence hashes and Git modes were checked before composition and archival. Proposed source comes from exact frozen #213, exact reviewed42a, exact published/reviewed #212, or explicit novel text with recorded hashes. Exact reuse is not fresh native acceptance and retains earlier display/pre-use qualifications.\n\nThe 583-line novel proposal, 1,028-line/35-map focused lock proposal, 616-line frozen AuthFn/FileFn generated-versus-reviewed212 delta, 1,014-line amendment, 1,248-line/36-path frozen-only preserved source, and final guide/platform patch were displayed in contiguous bounded read calls without the character-truncation marker in this continuation. This does not retroactively establish complete visibility of older truncated reads of primary/supplementary feedback, the original 4,364-line patch, or prior assessments.\n\n## Generated and lock disposition\n\nThe frozen AuthFn generated delta rolls back reviewed prerequisite API-key ownership/scope/revocation guidance and reinstates nonexistent docs:llms/configuration instructions. The frozen FileFn delta reinstates removed rateLimit.persistence/logger contracts and loses bound services/migration documentation. These frozen generated bytes must not become accepted afterimages. Preserve/archive them, retain current42a source owners, and regenerate with the actual current consumer SDKs after normal installs and prerequisite builds. ExtFn's 784-line frozen full artifact is likewise an old generated snapshot, not clearance; its newly corrected getting-started/README/runtime ownership must be regenerated. Full final corpus/producer comparison remains required.\n\nReject wholesale reuse of the 196-map frozen-versus42a lock difference. The focused 35-map seed consists of affected AuthFn/FileFn published212 ownership/tooling leaves, exact frozenExtFn leaves, the required nested aria-query5.3.1 record for Svelte5.55.7, ExtFn workspace link, declared parser/search dependencies, and the reviewed trusted-types flag adjustment. DB/SecFn workspace owner maps stay byte-equivalent at the package-map level to reviewed42a. OAuth/observability stay: the actual OpenAPI generator imports social OAuth, whose transitive runtime/type owners require them. This is a seed, not physical closure proof; no npm normalization is authorized.\n\n## Coordinated repairs and corrections caught before use\n\n- Reuse the reviewed212 first-colon/filename-relative provider/page logic, export-aware consumer resolution, server-owned content/DTO/blog boundaries, native route ownership and reduced-motion/observer/search/drawer fixes. Preserve original ExtFn pages, config and runtime contract documentation.\n- Correct ExtFn unconditional packaging/rebuild guidance and remove the README's obsolete claim that Vite substitutes SearchFn source aliases. Keep search dependencies declared and build public exports through normal Turbo prerequisites.\n- Preserve original full affected-consumer selection for shared inputs. The first proposal's hard-coded three-product selector was rejected; its explicit supplement uses existingProductIds. No unrelated DevFn feature or entire branch is transplanted.\n- Hash deployment/public/assets roles in globalEnv so inherited child tasks cannot reuse cross-role outputs. Actual proposed/native Turbo hashes still require verification.\n- Keep AuthFn native /docs LLM handlers and its reviewed generator instructions. Correct remaining authoritative-host siblings.\n- URL-only FileFn substitutions were rejected: they created /docs/docs paths and invented MCP/raw/rich/skills endpoint readiness. Actual route inventory has no such native handlers. Seven coherent AI guides now distinguish generated context from separately owned integrations, without creating a new service. FileFn's actual manifest port is6006, not6001.\n- Preserve Kit's currently owned Search alias, Promise-returning/rejecting provider ABI, canonicalUrl option AND returned value, public roles independent of asset roles, Vitest3, native normal/error title ownership, six text extensions and native binary passthrough.\n- Existing absolute directory dependency fixture links select junction on Windows. POSIX-mode assertions in new tests are explicit Windows-qualified; this is not Windows execution proof.\n\n## Atomic-writer evidence\n\nThe proposed helper creates a unique exclusively owned same-directory temporary, writes/closes it before rename, preserves existing regular-file POSIX modes, and cleans only its own temporary. Nonregular targets are rejected. Cleanup errors remain visible with original causes. Contract: each public path exposes a complete old or new file; NOT a two-file transaction, fsync/power-loss durability, ACL/uid/xattr/hardlink preservation or hostile-directory security guarantee.\n\nFresh writable SSD UUID/same-device/>=15GiB admission was recorded. A normal separate Node writer and independent native reader made23,380 reads with zero old/new-byte violations and preserved0600 modes; no mocked filesystem/process kill. Seven controlled failure/check/mode/creation tests passed. Open/write/chmod/rename failure injection is explicitly mocked and is NOT an OS-fault claim. These were audit-only proposals, not installed #213 acceptance; repeat native and controlled gates against applied candidate.\n\n## Individual frozen failed-check assessment\n\n- JavaScript110232739883/run36819773803: source109/112 transaction capability/signature failure is an inherited SecFn/DB interface mismatch. Preserve exact reviewed42a executing sources/manifests and verify public physical closures, native SecFn/DB types/tests/builds. No native #213 pass yet; frozen failure retained.\n- Sonar110233284147: Reliability C versus A remains failed, docstring17.07% versus80% remains uncleared. Do not claim this failed check green from local changes.\n- Static ExtFn app.html title warning: native Svelte head owns normal titles; adding a static duplicate is invalid. The original template is preserved; native error title is explicitly supplied. Actual HTTP/hydration title acceptance pending.\n- listEntries/loadEntry async-without-await: removing async naively changes Promise/rejection ABI. Preserve the reviewed async boundary; do not introduce artificial await or claim hosted policy clearance.\n- startsWith selector style: original regex ownership semantics are correct; use a scoped startsWith correction only if separately assessed, otherwise retain this low-value style warning explicitly.\n- AuthFn loadDocsSiteSource unused-import warning: proposed exact212 loader actually uses its source acquisition; assess current source/type result rather than deleting an owned import based on a stale line reference.\n\n## Preservation and closed gates\n\nretained212-source-own-locks-installed-history.tar.gz and its index preserve24,064 regular files,574 links and42 public DocsFn SDK directories, source/own locks/installed manifests/hidden locks, with archive and unchanged-original hashes/modes verified. Exactly the existing DevFn/AuthFn/FileFn standalone contexts remain; no fourth consumer, root installation, relocation or cleanup. Outputs/installations remain in place. ExtFn standalone conversion is NOT yet admitted; it needs an explicit own-lock/source slot decision.\n\nCurrent status: source proposal review/archival substantially advanced, but candidate application, genuine root/three-slot installation, frozen endpoint negative, complete current corpus/physical/native types/tests/builds/HTTP/browser/cache/serialization/ancestry/staging/publication admission remain incomplete. All original plan install/publication gates and supplementary gates remain false. No feedback recollection, commit, push, merge, live mutation or reviewer-thread mutation is authorized by this artifact.\n"}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-6.1-sol","usage":{"input":3020,"output":2711,"cacheRead":153856,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":1034,"totalTokens":159587,"cost":{"input":0.006039999999999999,"output":0.027110000000000002,"cacheRead":0.015385600000000001,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0485356}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1791348218859,"responseId":"resp_055fb762f51dfcfc016ac5cdfb6bcc87d0a930b502c5a41b5a","rawStopReason":"completed","thinkingLevel":"high"}}
