{"type":"compaction","id":"33a35681","parentId":"9f0e362c","timestamp":"2026-10-07T06:04:31.245Z","summary":"## Goal\nComplete documentation PRs in **`21nCo/super-functions`** sequentially, preserving reviewed prerequisites and merging only fully assessed, applicable-green exact heads.\n\nUser authorization remains **“proceed and dont stop until you take up one after the other.”** This continuation advanced #213’s proposed composition, preservation archive and audit-only atomic-writer tests.\n\n**Latest state:** #213 active/incomplete, clean frozen **`f15540d26c2329203c626ccb51eb9108c5bebd84`**, collection1/publication0, mode **`architecture_reset`**. **No application-source mutation, candidate installation, commit, push or merge.** Candidate admission and genuine verification remain required before #214.\n\n#212 published once at **`3c733afa29ffb7c721870a8d5318cf656f3f1ca4`**, unmerged/stopped. #206/#207/#209/#210/#211 also stopped; #208/#223/#229 merged; #133 parked; #222 protected.\n\n## Constraints & Preferences\n- Controlling skill: **`21n/pr-refetch-fix` v1.4.0 revision6**.\n  - Hosted digest **`sha256:b6a6e7a8c670bc5ab12540910401d153e8eedd533d89fd1a1925bc9979112726`** at `data.version.digest`.\n  - Instructions SHA-256 **`78e6b66300287085d26e1cf15657a5010c6c93d0c2c23a9d4240064a6cdcd91c`**.\n  - Fresh pin per new PR; #213’s pin and sole collection already consumed. Caller model metadata remains `\"unknown\"`.\n- One bounded round per PR: exact checkout, one collection, scoped assessment/repair/verification, at most one integration/corrective commit and normal push, immediate receipt/report/stop.\n  - No feedback recollection, post-push polling/retrigger, metadata retry, stopped-PR revisit or automatic merge.\n  - Cubic `check-pr-comments` defaults do not override the hosted skill; cubic unavailable, no fetched learnings or new delegation.\n- Every `gh` command: **`GH_CONFIG_DIR=/Users/serro/.config/gh-other`**, active **thyaravind**, origin **`https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions.git`**.\n  - No alternate account/fork, force push, admin bypass, branch deletion or agent-accepted risk.\n  - Merge only assessed applicable-green exact heads using **`--match-head-commit`**.\n- Excluded: live Worker/domain/DNS/routes/certificate/infrastructure mutations, workflow dispatch, secrets/releases/trusted publishers/dist-tags, reviewer replies/resolutions/dismissals, #133 work.\n  - Cloudflare, if needed: **`cloudflare_mcp_azonal-hypate` / `cloudflare.request`** only.\n  - R2: personal u0/bucket-scoped credentials; no public access without direction.\n- Preserve unrelated worktrees, `.conduct`, `.entire`, `.codex/hooks.json`, `filefn/server/eng.traineddata`, source/locks/installations/caches/archives/logs/outputs.\n  - No blind reset/restore/prune, merge abort, Git metadata surgery, hook bypass, protected deletion, unverified WIP commit or #222 restoration.\n  - Entire remains enabled; no `core.hooksPath` override.\n- Resource policy: **one reused physical SSD candidate and exactly three existing genuine standalone contexts**.\n  - No extra full application root/fourth consumer installation, cleanup or relocation. Historical cleanup/relocation authority consumed.\n  - Writable **`/Volumes/OS - Data`**, UUID **`B86D5097-6E24-3D1D-A590-8CF9D44B6245`**; `/Volumes/OS` read-only.\n  - Fresh UUID/writable/same-device cache-temp/≥15GiB guards before installs; environment routing, not global npm configuration.\n  - Existing contexts remain DevFn/AuthFn/FileFn. **ExtFn slot conversion and own-lock admission are not yet authorized by an artifact**; no inference from preservation archive.\n  - User previously corrected internal-only gating: **“aren't we using external ssd?”**, then **“proceed.”**\n- Ordinary npm10 root/npm11 genuine standalone installs only. No `--force`, `--legacy-peer-deps`, broad lock normalization, root/sibling standalone-lock copying, parent application dependency borrowing, dependency surgery or metadata-only acceptance.\n  - Retain npm10 Arborist/npm11/ENOSPC/DNS/native/inherited failures distinctly.\n- Recurring-family resets require four fields before edits: **invariant, faithful old boundary, coordinated ownership/failure plan, independent acceptance**.\n  - Historical cross-product failed-round counts persist; unknown is not zero.\n  - Immutable original composition and explicit supplements remain distinct; merge entries in order only after admission.\n- Preserve: `buildLlmsSiteArtifacts` canonicalUrl option **and return value**, dynamic normal/error titles, config/sidebar/plugin typing/Node policy, native search/TopBar/mobile drawer, reduced motion, nonzero-height observer/disconnect, Vitest3, first-colon IDs/`absolutePath`, server-owned content/DTO/blog, declared public exports, six text extensions/native binary passthrough, Promise/rejection ABI.\n- Controlled fixtures excluded from publication and restored; generated outputs restored byte/mode exact.\n  - Historical noncanonical type fixtures preserved by exact membership, not deleted/excluded with broad `__` rules; legitimate `__tests__`/`__init__.py` remain canonical.\n- **Visibility honesty:** both earlier and **new continuation** displayed large reads contain **`[... characters truncated]`**.\n  - New assessment, ledger, checkpoint and REPORT assert untruncated visible review of583/1028/616/1248/1014-line artifacts. **Those assertions are not established by the actual displayed outputs.** Preserve these new visibility qualifications as well as historical ones.\n- Audit-only borrowed SDK/Vite/Turbo negatives and proposal-only atomic positives are **not genuine installed #213 acceptance**.\n  - No hosted-green/live Worker/Windows/security-wide/fullSQL/backend durability/OS IME/full Bun-auth clearance.\n  - Atomic scope: complete old/new visibility **per public file**, not paired transaction, fsync/power-loss, ACL/uid/xattr/hardlink recovery or hostile-directory security.\n  - Controlled open/write/chmod/rename faults are explicitly mocked, not actual OS-fault evidence.\n- Browser prerequisite `aside guide` completed during #212; previous native Playwright harness and its failures retained. No synthetic event workaround for real exposed backdrop/hit-tested mobile interactions.\n- Eight previous workers closed; no `--ignore-other-worktrees`; historical PIDs grant no kill authority.\n\n## Progress\n### Done\n- [x] Original22-PR inventory/provenance consolidated; `21nCo/docs` had no open PRs. Eight workers closed and19 owned historical worktrees archived/removed.\n  - Sequential206/207/209/210/211/212 stopped; active213; remaining213–222,224–226.\n- [x] Historical publications retained with their qualified scopes:\n  - #206: `c699cb63141af8c8c26c052a100c46cb63245c2e` → `2f04e0da43db117aec5bfc6a6e6e1fc7c3242dee` → `e457a0e42a2dfade73eec090a37db3b9739a8907` → `33bc933ce414d3ac2b9be2f484a722200187656f` → stopped **`a44402b3e47a410316720107721201fbcf1e36a1`**;103surfaces8/86/9, primary8/12/7; immediate metadata mismatch retained.\n  - #207: `6c5347e6a1051a329d6f2932a2ff4f93f53a8e87` → `66e7d189e5ad7f2a53e3892478482c6e2d269c36` → stopped **`e9a934257f4aaac959aac647fd36ee4d3a38a5fd`**, parents66e7/270b;36dispositions10/20/6, primary10/2/5;45Vitest+2Node/native scopes; docstring16.67%/80% uncleared.\n  - #209: `d2ff58998148593be2dd96961d28701c33555bb8` → stopped **`38931d19f72000264443c57be30be914d6e8c2a0`**, parentsd2ff/a40;37dispositions1/35/1,89maps/8303canonical/tree **`4a95b7276503cf54966b581992a1882ea13cae9a`**; npm10 `edgesOut`/553-map rejection retained.\n  - #210: frozen `d5633e3d036305b0c826ff65adc763bfb34919fe` → stopped **`4e67ac86a5de697568b6bf61c6064f13d925f88d`**, parentsd563/42a;46dispositions5/37/4,196-plan/35maps/8345canonical/tree **`8954a08643fb89ab7627b39f729e16c18d40fdf5`**; six contexts/nine closures; stale immediate metadata retained.\n  - #211: `7bb23068fbbb17cb71b19f1f58c5d50352a7faac` → stopped **`d927103f055e3421d296785f9b75c8225ed405eb`**, parents7bb/42a;19dispo