date changes:\n  - `supplement-reviewed-composition.py` → **`composition-assessment-supplement.json/.patch`**,18paths/1014lines, two extra paths: `filefn/docs/content/docs/ai-resources/index.md`, `scripts/docs-site/atomic-write.test.mjs`.\n  - Corrected first proposal’s hard-coded AuthFn/ExtFn/FileFn selector that omitted an existing shared consumer: shared inputs now return `existingProductIds()`.\n  - Corrected duplicate `/docs/docs` FileFn URLs by rewriting seven coherent AI guides; removed nonexistent MCP/raw/rich/skills/API/tool-readiness claims rather than inventing services.\n  - AuthFn five AI guides reused from212 with authoritative host `https://authfn.com/docs`; native generator guidance preserved.\n  - Turbo `globalEnv` deploy/public/assets variables preserved with reviewed42a formatting/tasks.\n  - Native atomic test added to all three proposed workspace test scripts.\n  - `supplement-final-guide-and-platform-assessment.py` → **`final-guide-platform-supplement.json/.patch`**,3paths:\n    - FileFn actual local port **6006**, not6001.\n    - ExtFn README corrected public SearchFn/DocsFn export prerequisite ownership; no obsolete source-alias bypass claim.\n    - Windows/POSIX chmod assertions explicitly qualified.\n  - Amendments bind preceding plan hashes; merge order original→composition→final, never silently rewrite original.\n- [x] Generated regression disposition recorded:\n  - Frozen AuthFn generated files roll back API-key ownership/scopes/revocation and reinstate obsolete `docs:llms`/config instructions.\n  - Frozen FileFn generated files regress current rateLimit/persistence/logger/bound-service/migration contracts.\n  - ExtFn frozen784-line full corpus also old; **none is accepted final generated afterimage**. Preserve/current42a source and regenerate with actual current consumer SDKs later.\n  - Created `preserved-original213-human-pre-use.patch`1248lines/36frozen-only paths and path inventory; original ExtFn pages/runtime/CLI/navigation preserved in proposals.\n- [x] **Audit-only proposed atomic implementation and tests**:\n  - `proposed-atomic-llms.mjs`: exclusive `\"wx\"` unique same-directory temp using `randomUUID`, regular target guard, complete write/fchmod/close/rename, preserve existing POSIX mode, clean only owned temp; aggregate cleanup failures with original cause.\n  - Preserves `loadLlmsSiteSource`, `buildLlmsSiteArtifacts`, canonicalUrl return, first-colon/pathname source-link behavior and nonwriting `--check`.\n  - Fresh SSD UUID/read-write/same-device admission, **167.22GiB** available.\n  - Native independent reader/normal separate Node writer: **23,380reads, zero violations**,0600 preservation, normal exit, no mocked filesystem/process kill.\n  - **Seven controlled tests passed**: open/write/fchmod/rename failure preservation and foreign-temp ownership, nonwriting/stale check, successful existing modes/bytes, missing-directory check/create.\n  - Audit test import changed to `./proposed-atomic-llms.mjs`; publication proposal uses `./llms.mjs`.\n  - **Final platform-qualified test version has not been executed against an applied candidate.**\n- [x] **Read-only retention archive executed/verified**:\n  - `archive-retained212-source-and-install-history.py` → **`retained212-source-own-locks-installed-history.tar.gz`**, **`retained212-history-index.json`**.\n  - **30,466,435bytes;24,064regular files;574links;42public DocsFn SDK directories**.\n  - Archive bytes/modes/linktext and original inputs verified unchanged; all8314prior canonical hashes/modes checked.\n  - Root/standalone sources/own locks/installed package manifests/hidden locks/public DocsFn SDKs retained, exact fixture inventory referenced.\n  - Existing output directories inventoried and left in place, not archived as complete build-output bytes; no ACL/xattr/hardlink-topology recovery promise.\n  - Exactly DevFn/AuthFn/FileFn genuine contexts retained with own-lock hashes; no standalone root `package.json` or `node_modules`, no conversion/installation/extra root.\n- [x] Written **`source-composition-pre-use-assessment.md`**, rewritten **`resumption-progress.md`**, updated/reparsed **`parent-ledger.json`**, **`checkpoint.json`**, **`REPORT.md`**.\n  - Active213/architecture_reset/collection1/publication0/completedfalse/source_mutations0 verified;118A213 artifacts.\n  - New checkpoint counters23,380native reads/0violations/7controlled tests/203original plan/18+3supplements/35maps/archiveverified.\n  - Earlier unsupported “all primary/resolved/full4364-line patch untruncated” assertions explicitly qualified.\n  - **New large-read assertions remain inaccurate too: displayed proposal/lock/generated/amendment/preserved-source outputs were truncated.**\n\n### In Progress\n- [ ] Finish genuinely visible/qualified source, feedback, lock, corpus and supplementary review; correct or qualify new unsupported nontruncated-read assertions.\n- [ ] Complete source/canonical admission over203original entries plus18/3amendments, original85 preservation and outside-plan ownership.\n- [ ] Explicit existing-slot ExtFn conversion/source/own ordinary npm11-lock admission; no fourth consumer.\n- [ ] Apply admitted coordinated repair to the existing SSD candidate, then normal installs and full physical/native/HTTP/browser/cache/serialization/generator acceptance.\n- [ ] Frozen AuthFn native endpoint HTTP negative, native regenerated final corpus/source comparison and final byte/mode/lock/ancestry/staging gates.\n- [ ] One guarded publication only after all applicable admissions; #214 afterward.\n\n### Blocked\n- **#213 application/install/publication:** gates remain false; assessment/archive/proposal tests do not admit application or genuine verification.\n- **#213 merge:** frozen JavaScript/Sonar failed; exact new-head hosted applicable-green readiness unassessed.\n- **Stopped206/207/209/210/211/212 merges:** no new hosted assessment or polling/revisit authority.\n- **#222:** `.git` and7966tracked regular files missing, actor unknown; no restoration authority.\n- No demonstrated current SSD capacity blocker; fresh install guards still required.\n- Live/Windows/security-wide/platform/durability/fullSQL/OSIME/fullBunauth clearance excluded.\n\n## Key Decisions\n- **Same #213 round**: collection consumed; continue without recollection, stopped212 revisit or new publication count.\n- **Proposal ≠ application ≠ acceptance ≠ merge**: both atomic proofs and archive are audit-only; retained installations remain #212 state.\n- **Preserve reviewed42a prerequisites**: DB0.3/SecFn0.0.3/FileFn0.2/current APIs must not regress to frozen ancestor contracts.\n- **Focused lock seed only**: reject196-map rollback;35-map seed needs ordinary install/physical validation, not normalization.\n- **Generated artifacts must be regenerated**: frozen AuthFn/FileFn contracts and ExtFn corpus are not final accepted bytes even though original plan contains frozen snapshots.\n- **Correct proposal defects before use**: explicit supplements fix shared consumer selection, FileFn fabricated endpoints/duplicated prefix, actual port and ExtFn build-ownership guidance.\n- **Native route truth over hostname replacement**: FileFn has no MCP/raw/rich/skills handlers; coherent context guides cannot claim service deployment.\n- **Public-origin includes executing config, generators, native endpoints and cache**: deployment-only public origin independent of assets; all role-sensitive child tasks hashed using `globalEnv`, actual positive still pending.\n- **Complete conditional owner repair**: consumer public ESM/subpaths/declared parser/search peers, no guessed Core entry/CJS sibling/universal externalization.\n- **Peer graph beats direct import grep**: OAuth/observability needed by OpenAPI/social OAuth; do not delete.\n- **Native title and Promise ABI beat stale style diagnostics**: no duplicate static title, artificial await or naïve async removal.\n- **Atomic contract narrowly stated**: per-file old/new visibility wit