</file context>\n```\n\n</details>\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6n0Wlr authfn/docs/content/docs/ai-resources/llms-txt.md\n<!-- cubic:v=dd67c191-2477-4536-8fca-bacde5e6db42 -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=9bf00f6a-ae76-5e76-a28b-73578ff700a9 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":7} -->\nP2: These local URLs are unreachable. `llms.txt`/`llms-full.txt` are emitted into `static/` and Vite serves `static/` from the site root, so the dev URLs are `http://localhost:6005/llms.txt` and `http://localhost:6005/llms-full.txt`. A request to `/docs/llms.txt` matches the catch-all `docs/[...slug]` route, whose `loadDocsPage` then throws a 404 because `resolveDocsRouteDataOrThrow(slug, manifest, { basePath: \"/docs\" })` finds no content page named `llms.txt`. Remove the `/docs` prefix from both local URLs.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. When an issue isn't valid or won't be fixed in this PR, reply in its thread with the reason and then resolve the thread. At authfn/docs/content/docs/ai-resources/llms-txt.md, line 42:\n\n<comment>These local URLs are unreachable. `llms.txt`/`llms-full.txt` are emitted into `static/` and Vite serves `static/` from the site root, so the dev URLs are `http://localhost:6005/llms.txt` and `http://localhost:6005/llms-full.txt`. A request to `/docs/llms.txt` matches the catch-all `docs/[...slug]` route, whose `loadDocsPage` then throws a 404 because `resolveDocsRouteDataOrThrow(slug, manifest, { basePath: \"/docs\" })` finds no content page named `llms.txt`. Remove the `/docs` prefix from both local URLs.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -33,14 +33,14 @@ The pipeline:\n ```\n-http://localhost:5173/llms.txt\n-http://localhost:5173/llms-full.txt\n+http://localhost:6005/docs/llms.txt\n+http://localhost:6005/docs/llms-full.txt\n ```\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>\n\n```suggestion\nhttp://localhost:6005/llms.txt\nhttp://localhost:6005/llms-full.txt\n```\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6n0Wlz filefn/docs/docsfn.config.ts\n<!-- cubic:v=80499fa9-7dea-4b1a-a1b2-ff815566b508 -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=9bf00f6a-ae76-5e76-a28b-73578ff700a9 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":9} -->\nP2: Changing FileFn's canonical origin leaves the AI guides and generated `llms-full.txt` body pointing at `docs.filefn.dev`. Update the remaining FileFn documentation URLs to the new public origin as part of this migration.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. When an issue isn't valid or won't be fixed in this PR, reply in its thread with the reason and then resolve the thread. At filefn/docs/docsfn.config.ts, line 9:\n\n<comment>Changing FileFn's canonical origin leaves the AI guides and generated `llms-full.txt` body pointing at `docs.filefn.dev`. Update the remaining FileFn documentation URLs to the new public origin as part of this migration.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -6,7 +6,7 @@ const config: DocsConfig = {\n     description: \"Self-hosted file uploads, storage, and processing for any stack. Multipart uploads, signed URLs, share links, OPFS offline, image/audio/video processing, and a typed SDK on every runtime.\",\n     basePath: \"/docs\",\n-    canonicalUrl: \"https://filefn.superfunctions.dev\",\n+    canonicalUrl: \"https://filefn.com\",\n     showFooter: false,\n     editLink: {\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6n0Wl2 scripts/docs-site/origin.test.mjs\n<!-- cubic:v=8f02d2a7-6a3a-4ec1-ae74-85806839ceb4 -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=9bf00f6a-ae76-5e76-a28b-73578ff700a9 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":6} -->\nP3: The first test calls `symlinkSync(directory, ..., \"dir\")`, which on Windows requires Developer Mode or elevated privileges and throws EPERM otherwise, yet only the second test in this file is guarded with `it.skipIf(process.platform === \"win32\")`. Add the same guard (or fall back to a junction) to the `it.each` test so the suite behaves consistently on Windows.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. When an issue isn't valid or won't be fixed in this PR, reply in its thread with the reason and then resolve the thread. At scripts/docs-site/origin.test.mjs, line 38:\n\n<comment>The first test calls `symlinkSync(directory, ..., \"dir\")`, which on Windows requires Developer Mode or elevated privileges and throws EPERM otherwise, yet only the second test in this file is guarded with `it.skipIf(process.platform === \"win32\")`. Add the same guard (or fall back to a junction) to the `it.each` test so the suite behaves consistently on Windows.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -0,0 +1,74 @@\n+      expect(fixturePins[`@docsfn/${dependency}`]).toBe(pins[`@docsfn/${dependency}`]);\n+      const directory = dirname(dirname(require.resolve(`@docsfn/${dependency}`)));\n+      expect(JSON.parse(readFileSync(join(directory, \"package.json\"), \"utf8\")).name).toBe(`@docsfn/${dependency}`);\n+      symlinkSync(directory, join(base, product, \"docs/node_modules/@docsfn\", dependency), \"dir\");\n+    }\n+    for (const [deploy, publicOrigin, expected] of [[\"0\", \"\", `https://${product}.com`], [\"1\", `https://dev.${product}.com`, `https://dev.${product}.com`], [\"1\", \"https://public.example.test\", \"https://public.example.test\"], [\"1\", \"\", `https://${product}.com`]]) {\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1791366879380}}
