{"type":"message","id":"3534a395","parentId":"61c0d822","timestamp":"2026-10-07T10:05:30.574Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_a411777581984bf49df9578e9862ce27|fc_055fb762f51dfcfc016ac61965b1d087d093457a95306ea5bd","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":" ## Use it from any tool\n@@ -50,7 +50,7 @@\n Most LLM clients accept arbitrary text context. Drop `llms.txt` into your project's prompt:\n \n ```bash\n-curl https://docs.filefn.dev/llms.txt > .ai/filefn-llms.txt\n+curl https://filefn.com/docs/llms.txt > .ai/filefn-llms.txt\n # include .ai/filefn-llms.txt in your assistant's system prompt\n ```\n \n@@ -73,7 +73,7 @@\n       \"title\": \"Upload sessions\",\n       \"description\": \"...\",\n       \"tags\": [\"multipart\", \"uploads\", \"lifecycle\"],\n-      \"url\": \"https://docs.filefn.dev/docs/core-concepts/upload-sessions\",\n+      \"url\": \"https://filefn.com/docs/docs/core-concepts/upload-sessions\",\n       \"body\": \"...\"\n     }\n   ],\n--- exact-provenance/filefn/docs/content/docs/ai-resources/mcp.md\n+++ proposed213/filefn/docs/content/docs/ai-resources/mcp.md\n@@ -19,7 +19,7 @@\n ## Installing\n \n ```bash\n-droid mcp add filefn https://docs.filefn.dev/mcp --type http\n+droid mcp add filefn https://filefn.com/docs/mcp --type http\n ```\n \n That registers the MCP server with Droid and similar MCP-aware clients.\n@@ -31,7 +31,7 @@\n   \"mcpServers\": {\n     \"filefn\": {\n       \"type\": \"http\",\n-      \"url\": \"https://docs.filefn.dev/mcp\"\n+      \"url\": \"https://filefn.com/docs/mcp\"\n     }\n   }\n }\n@@ -44,7 +44,7 @@\n   \"mcpServers\": {\n     \"filefn\": {\n       \"type\": \"http\",\n-      \"url\": \"https://docs.filefn.dev/mcp\"\n+      \"url\": \"https://filefn.com/docs/mcp\"\n     }\n   }\n }\n--- exact-provenance/filefn/docs/content/docs/ai-resources/skills.md\n+++ proposed213/filefn/docs/content/docs/ai-resources/skills.md\n@@ -20,7 +20,7 @@\n \n ## Discoverability\n \n-Skills are exposed via the MCP server (`list_skills` tool) and as static markdown under `https://docs.filefn.dev/skills/`. AI assistants that support skills (Claude Code, Cursor, Droid) discover them automatically once the MCP server is registered.\n+Skills are exposed via the MCP server (`list_skills` tool) and as static markdown under `https://filefn.com/docs/skills/`. AI assistants that support skills (Claude Code, Cursor, Droid) discover them automatically once the MCP server is registered.\n \n ## Authoring your own\n \n--- exact-provenance/scripts/cloudflare-docs/select-products.mjs\n+++ proposed213/scripts/cloudflare-docs/select-products.mjs\n@@ -46,16 +46,19 @@\n   };\n \n   for (const file of changedFiles) {\n-    if (/^(package\\.json|package-lock\\.json|turbo\\.json|scripts\\/cloudflare-docs\\/|scripts\\/docs-site\\/|\\.github\\/workflows\\/superfunctions-docs-cloudflare-)/.test(file)) {\n+    if (/^(package\\.json|package-lock\\.json|turbo\\.json|scripts\\/cloudflare-docs\\/|\\.github\\/workflows\\/superfunctions-docs-cloudflare-)/.test(file)) {\n       return existingProductIds();\n     }\n     if (/^packages\\/docs-theme\\//.test(file)) {\n       for (const productId of existingProductIds()) selectExisting(productId);\n       continue;\n     }\n-    if (/^apifn\\/docsfn\\//.test(file)) return existingProductIds();\n+    if (file.startsWith(\"docsfn/\") || file.startsWith(\"scripts/docs-site/\")) {\n+      for (const productId of [\"authfn\", \"extfn\", \"filefn\"]) selectExisting(productId);\n+      continue;\n+    }\n     if (/^datafn\\/docs\\//.test(file)) selectExisting(\"datafn\");\n-    if (/^extfn\\/docs\\//.test(file)) selectExisting(\"extfn\");\n+    if (file.startsWith(\"extfn/docs/\")) selectExisting(\"extfn\");\n     if (/^filefn\\/docs\\//.test(file)) selectExisting(\"filefn\");\n     if (/^searchfn\\/docs\\//.test(file)) selectExisting(\"searchfn\");\n     if (/^authfn\\/docs\\//.test(file)) selectExisting(\"authfn\");\n--- exact-provenance/scripts/docs-site/llms.mjs\n+++ proposed213/scripts/docs-site/llms.mjs\n@@ -1,4 +1,5 @@\n-import { mkdirSync, readFileSync, writeFileSync } from \"node:fs\";\n+import { closeSync, fchmodSync, lstatSync, mkdirSync, openSync, readFileSync, renameSync, unlinkSync, writeFileSync } from \"node:fs\";\n+import { randomUUID } from \"node:crypto\";\n import { resolve } from \"node:path\";\n /**\n  * Resolve DocsFn from the consumer site so each site's published package pin is honored.\n@@ -52,7 +53,7 @@\n   if (canonicalUrl) return text;\n   const sources = new Map(Object.values(manifest.pages)\n     .filter((page) => page.id.startsWith(\"docs:\"))\n-    .map((page) => [page.path, page.id.slice(\"docs:\".length)]));\n+    .map((page) => [new URL(page.path, \"https://docs.invalid\").pathname, page.id.slice(\"docs:\".length)]));\n   return text.replace(/\\]\\((\\/docs[^\\s)]*)\\)/g, (match, href) => {\n     const url = new URL(href, \"https://docs.invalid\");\n     const source = sources.get(url.pathname);\n@@ -60,6 +61,45 @@\n     const path = source.split(\"/\").map(encodeURIComponent).join(\"/\");\n     return `](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/blob/dev/${product}/docs/content/docs/${path}${url.hash})`;\n   });\n+}\n+\n+/**\n+ * Replace one regular artifact in a trusted output directory atomically.\n+ * This promises per-path visibility, not a two-file transaction or power-loss durability.\n+ * @param {string} target\n+ * @param {string} body\n+ */\n+function replaceArtifact(target, body) {\n+  let previous;\n+  try { previous = lstatSync(target); }\n+  catch (error) {\n+    if (!error || typeof error !== \"object\" || !(\"code\" in error) || error.code !== \"ENOENT\") throw error;\n+  }\n+  if (previous && !previous.isFile()) throw new Error(`Artifact target must be a regular file: ${target}`);\n+  const mode = previous ? previous.mode & 0o777 : undefined;\n+  const temporary = `${target}.${randomUUID()}.tmp`;\n+  let descriptor;\n+  let owned = false;\n+  try {\n+    descriptor = openSync(temporary, \"wx\", mode ?? 0o666);\n+    owned = true;\n+    writeFileSync(descriptor, body, \"utf8\");\n+    if (mode !== undefined) fchmodSync(descriptor, mode);\n+    closeSync(descriptor);\n+    descriptor = undefined;\n+    renameSync(temporary, target);\n+    owned = false;\n+  } catch (error) {\n+    const failures = [error];\n+    if (descriptor !== undefined) {\n+      try { closeSync(descriptor); } catch (closeError) { failures.push(closeError); }\n+    }\n+    if (owned) {\n+      try { unlinkSync(temporary); } catch (cleanupError) { failures.push(cleanupError); }\n+    }\n+    if (failures.length > 1) throw new AggregateError(failures, `Artifact replacement failed: ${target}`, { cause: error });\n+    throw error;\n+  }\n }\n \n /**\n@@ -77,7 +117,7 @@\n       let actual;\n\n[144 more lines in file. Use offset=441 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1791367530574}}
{"type":"message","id":"31fb6ecd","parentId":"3534a395","timestamp":"2026-10-07T10:05:30.574Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_f92339c27a784db18c865157abdd4a58|fc_055fb762f51dfcfc016ac6196a3b2487d0b6209cf26f8575f0","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"+\n+Side-panel support is target-gated; do not assume Firefox supports the Chromium side-panel surface. Resolver and manifest behavior live in the [config source](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/blob/dev/extfn/core/src/config.ts) and [manifest builder](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/blob/dev/extfn/vite/src/manifest/buildManifest.ts). Review generated manifests before requesting browser permissions.\n--- reviewed42a/extfn/docs/content/docs/content-and-background.md\n+++ preserved213/extfn/docs/content/docs/content-and-background.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,10 @@\n+---\n+title: Content and background handlers\n+description: Register multiple content modules and discover background handlers.\n+---\n+\n+The config can declare several content scripts, each with its own ID, entry, match patterns, anchors, and style isolation. Anchor kinds include `selector`, `selector-list`, and `resolver`; each anchor carries its own `mountMode`, with values including `append`, `prepend`, `replace`, and `shadow`. The content helpers manage anchored mounting and reinjection.\n+\n+Background handlers are separate modules discovered from `messageHandlersDir` and `portHandlersDir`. A message handler uses `defineBackgroundHandler({ namespace, method, handle })`; a port handler uses `defineBackgroundPortHandler({ channel, onMessage })`. The namespace/method pair and port channel must each be unique across discovered handlers.\n+\n+`@extfn/svelte` supplies thin page and content mount functions. Components remain ordinary Svelte components; config owns DOM placement and isolation. The [multi-content source guide](/docs/reference/multi-content-and-background-handlers) includes complete examples and the [Svelte demo](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/tree/dev/extfn/examples/svelte-multi-content-demo) shows shadow and light DOM mounts.\n--- reviewed42a/extfn/docs/content/docs/index.md\n+++ preserved213/extfn/docs/content/docs/index.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,10 @@\n+---\n+title: ExtFn\n+description: Code-first browser extension development for Chromium and Firefox.\n+---\n+\n+ExtFn provides code-first configuration, runtime helpers, a Vite build pipeline, a CLI, and a thin Svelte adapter for browser extensions. It supports Chromium MV3 and Firefox MV3 targets, background service workers, popup and options pages, Chromium side panels, and multiple anchored content modules.\n+\n+The [getting-started guide](/docs/getting-started) walks through a config and the CLI. Read [runtime](/docs/runtime) for browser APIs and messaging, [content and background](/docs/content-and-background) for handler discovery and mounts, and [scan and package](/docs/scan-and-package) before distributing an extension.\n+\n+ExtFn owns extension infrastructure. Domain logic stays in packages such as `@datafn/extfn`, which bridges DataFn authority into extension contexts. The optional `@extfn/admin` package currently declares an unavailable capability; it is not an operator UI. See [package integrations](/docs/integrations).\n--- reviewed42a/extfn/docs/content/docs/integrations.md\n+++ preserved213/extfn/docs/content/docs/integrations.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,10 @@\n+---\n+title: Integrations and Svelte\n+description: Keep domain contracts and host adapters with their owners.\n+---\n+\n+`@extfn/svelte` provides page and content mounting adapters. It does not turn an extension page into SvelteKit. Shared UI that imports `$app/*` directly needs consumer-owned host interfaces for navigation, session, and other app state before it can run in an extension. The [consumer host guide](/docs/reference/consumer-host-abstraction) shows a migration pattern.\n+\n+`@datafn/extfn` lives under `datafn/` and owns DataFn authority and proxy behavior in extension contexts. Keep any other domain-specific integration in its owning package tree, reusing its public contracts. The root ExtFn README names possible future SearchFn and FileFn integrations as examples; those examples are not shipped ExtFn packages here.\n+\n+`@extfn/admin` currently declares an `unavailable` Super Console capability and an unavailable adapter. There is no supported ExtFn operator action surface in that package. Check the [admin source](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/blob/dev/extfn/admin/src/index.ts) before planning a console integration.\n--- reviewed42a/extfn/docs/content/docs/meta.json\n+++ preserved213/extfn/docs/content/docs/meta.json\n@@ -0,0 +1,4 @@\n+{\n+  \"title\": \"ExtFn\",\n+  \"pages\": [\"index\", \"getting-started\", \"configuration\", \"runtime\", \"content-and-background\", \"cli\", \"scan-and-package\", \"integrations\", \"operations-and-limits\", \"reference\"]\n+}\n--- reviewed42a/extfn/docs/content/docs/operations-and-limits.md\n+++ preserved213/extfn/docs/content/docs/operations-and-limits.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,10 @@\n+---\n+title: Operations and limits\n+description: Supported browser targets, manual steps, and validation boundaries.\n+---\n+\n+ExtFn supports Chromium MV3 and Firefox MV3. Side-panel and other capabilities vary by target. Development output is an unpacked extension; Firefox loading remains manual after `--open`. Production archives are `.zip` for Chromium and `.xpi` for Firefox.\n+\n+CLI scans are strict by default but are limited to emitted files and manifests. Review permissions, CSP, externally connectable scope, privacy claims, and store listing content before release. A successful local scan or build does not prove installation, browser behavior, or store approval.\n+\n+Keep domain operations in their owner packages. The ExtFn runtime and CLI provide extension infrastructure; `@datafn/extfn` is a separate integration. The admin package currently marks its capability unavailable. See [reference guides](/docs/reference) for exact CLI behavior and content patterns.\n--- reviewed42a/extfn/docs/content/docs/reference/cli.md\n+++ preserved213/extfn/docs/content/docs/reference/cli.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,146 @@\n+---\n+title: CLI reference\n+description: Develop, build, scan, and package extension targets.\n+---\n+\n+The shipped binary is `extfn`.\n+\n+## Global options\n+\n+```text\n+Usage: extfn [options] [command]\n+\n+Options:\n+  --json\n+  --quiet\n+  --verbose\n+  --color\n+```\n+\n+`--json` switches command output to machine-readable mode. `--quiet` and `--verbose` are shared CLI concerns provided through `clifn`.\n+\n+## dev\n+\n+```text\n+Usage: extfn dev [options]\n+\n+Options:\n+  --config <path>\n+  --target <target>\n+  --open\n+  --no-open\n+  --browser <browser>\n+```\n+\n+Behavior:\n+\n+- `extfn dev` watches exactly one target.\n+- If the config declares multiple targets, `--target` is required.\n+- The unpacked extension is emitted under `dist/<target>-dev`.\n+- `--open` tries to launch a browser session.\n+- `--no-open` prints the unpacked extension path and keeps watching.\n+- Firefox launch support opens the browser to `about:debugging#/runtime/this-firefox`; loading is still manual.\n+\n+Examples:\n+\n+```bash\n+npm exec extfn dev -- --config extfn/examples/vanilla-messaging-demo/extfn.config.ts --target chromium-mv3 --no-open\n+npm exec extfn dev -- --config extfn/examples/svelte-multi-content-demo/extfn.config.ts --target firefox-mv3 --open --browser firefox\n+```\n+\n+## build\n+\n+```text\n+Usage: extfn build [options]\n+\n+Options:\n+  --config <path>\n+  --target <target>\n+```\n+\n+Behavior:\n+\n+- Builds all configured targets by default.\n+- `--target` accepts one target or a comma-separated target list.\n+- Uses `@extfn/vite` as the only build engine.\n+- Writes unpacked production outputs under `dist/<target>`.\n+\n+Examples:\n+\n+```bash\n+npm exec extfn build -- --config extfn/examples/vanilla-messaging-demo/extfn.config.ts\n+npm exec extfn build -- --config extfn/examples/svelte-multi-content-demo/extfn.config.ts --target chromium-mv3,firefox-mv3\n+```\n+\n+## scan\n+\n+```text\n+Usage: extfn scan [options]\n+\n+Options:\n+  --config <path>\n+  --target <target>\n+  --report-dir <path>\n+  --format <format>\n+  --no-strict\n+```\n+\n+Behavior:\n+\n+- Scans built outputs and writes JSON reports under `dist/scan` by default.\n+- `--format text` prints the human summary.\n+- `--format json` returns the structured JSON payload.\n+- `--format sarif` emits SARIF for review tooling.\n+- Strict mode is on by default.\n+- `--no-strict` keeps the same findings but returns success instead of failing on error-severity findings.\n+\n\n[949 more lines in file. Use offset=301 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1791367530574}}
{"type":"message","id":"d9c61f2e","parentId":"31fb6ecd","timestamp":"2026-10-07T10:05:30.575Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_659f8c16c4144550a2a82c878bf77e42|fc_055fb762f51dfcfc016ac6196a3b2487d0b1b291cafef42005","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"✅ Addressed in [`fec011e`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/fec011e7c940d9ddc09b282f33007d9c3ec1aca9)\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNogd extfn/docs/tsconfig.json\n<!-- cubic:v=16ae4880-db13-405a-9cb4-fe8c945a52f7 -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=89d77ea6-21bc-5bb6-986a-2332a2024346 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":7} -->\nP2: In tsconfig `extends`, the derived `include` replaces the `include` generated inside `.svelte-kit/tsconfig.json`, so `.svelte-kit/ambient.d.ts` and the generated types are left out of the TS program. Any `$env/*` import (or other kit-generated ambient type) will then fail with \"Cannot find module\" under svelte-check/editors while Vite build still passes. Note that `authfn/docs` and `filefn/docs` don't extend the kit config at all, and the repo's other SvelteKit apps (`filefn/examples/*/client/tsconfig.json`) extend it without overriding `include` — this file is the first to both extend and replace it. Add the `.svelte-kit` globs to `include` (or drop the block and let the generated config own the file list, keeping `vite.config.ts`/`svelte.config.js` covered).\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At extfn/docs/tsconfig.json, line 26:\n\n<comment>In tsconfig `extends`, the derived `include` replaces the `include` generated inside `.svelte-kit/tsconfig.json`, so `.svelte-kit/ambient.d.ts` and the generated types are left out of the TS program. Any `$env/*` import (or other kit-generated ambient type) will then fail with \"Cannot find module\" under svelte-check/editors while Vite build still passes. Note that `authfn/docs` and `filefn/docs` don't extend the kit config at all, and the repo's other SvelteKit apps (`filefn/examples/*/client/tsconfig.json`) extend it without overriding `include` — this file is the first to both extend and replace it. Add the `.svelte-kit` globs to `include` (or drop the block and let the generated config own the file list, keeping `vite.config.ts`/`svelte.config.js` covered).</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -0,0 +1,33 @@\n+      \"vite/client\"\n+    ]\n+  },\n+  \"include\": [\n+    \"src/**/*.ts\",\n+    \"src/**/*.js\",\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>\n\n```suggestion\n  \"include\": [\n    \".svelte-kit/ambient.d.ts\",\n    \".svelte-kit/types/**/*.d.ts\",\n    \"src/**/*.ts\",\n    \"src/**/*.js\",\n    \"src/**/*.svelte\",\n    \"vite.config.ts\",\n    \"svelte.config.js\"\n  ]\n```\n\n✅ Addressed in [`fec011e`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/fec011e7c940d9ddc09b282f33007d9c3ec1aca9)\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNogf extfn/docs/content/docs/cli.md\n<!-- cubic:v=64e72c79-8e66-41e2-9f31-c002e7780093 -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=89d77ea6-21bc-5bb6-986a-2332a2024346 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":9} -->\nP2: `package` is not conditional: `runPackageCommand` calls `buildExtension` on every invocation before scanning or archiving. Document that it always rebuilds, or add an output-existence check before promising reuse. This can incur full builds and fail on source/config changes even when valid artifacts already exist.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At extfn/docs/content/docs/cli.md, line 8:\n\n<comment>`package` is not conditional: `runPackageCommand` calls `buildExtension` on every invocation before scanning or archiving. Document that it always rebuilds, or add an output-existence check before promising reuse. This can incur full builds and fail on source/config changes even when valid artifacts already exist.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@\n+\n+# CLI workflow\n+\n+`@extfn/cli` ships the `extfn` binary. `dev` watches exactly one target and supports `--open`, `--no-open`, and `--browser`. `build` builds all config targets by default or a selected target list. `scan` analyzes emitted files and manifests. `package` builds if needed, scans by default, and writes store-uploadable archives.\n+\n+```sh\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>\n\n✅ Addressed in [`fec011e`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/fec011e7c940d9ddc09b282f33007d9c3ec1aca9)\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNogk extfn/docs/content/docs/content-and-background.md\n<!-- cubic:v=8aac9b42-10d9-470a-be39-5b7cb24bfc36 -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=89d77ea6-21bc-5bb6-986a-2332a2024346 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":6} -->\nP3: The sentence lists `mount mode` as a per-content-script property, but the config puts `mountMode` on each anchor (selector/selector-list/resolver), not on the script itself. Rephrase so the script owns ID/entry/match patterns/anchors/style isolation and each anchor carries its own mount mode.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At extfn/docs/content/docs/content-and-background.md, line 8:\n\n<comment>The sentence lists `mount mode` as a per-content-script property, but the config puts `mountMode` on each anchor (selector/selector-list/resolver), not on the script itself. Rephrase so the script owns ID/entry/match patterns/anchors/style isolation and each anchor carries its own mount mode.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -0,0 +1,12 @@\n+\n+# Content and background handlers\n+\n+The config can declare several content scripts, each with its own ID, entry, match patterns, anchors, mount mode, and style isolation. Anchor kinds include `selector`, `selector-list`, and `resolver`; mount modes include `append`, `prepend`, `replace`, and `shadow`. The content helpers manage anchored mounting and reinjection.\n+\n+Background handlers are separate modules discovered from `messageHandlersDir` and `portHandlersDir`. A message handler uses `defineBackgroundHandler({ namespace, method, handle })`; a port handler uses `defineBackgroundPortHandler({ channel, onMessage })`. The namespace/method pair and port channel must each be unique across discovered handlers.\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>\n\n✅ Addressed in [`fec011e`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/fec011e7c940d9ddc09b282f33007d9c3ec1aca9)\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNogl extfn/docs/docsfn.config.ts\n<!-- cubic:v=4a365efe-16f0-45db-94f9-4583319cbcfa -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=89d77ea6-21bc-5bb6-986a-2332a2024346 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":6} -->\nP3: This site block omits `showFooter: false`, so the layout renders the default \"Built at 21n.co\" footer, while the sibling DocsFn sites authfn/docs/docsfn.config.ts and filefn/docs/docsfn.config.ts both set `showFooter: false`. Existing sites appear to deliberately suppress it; add it here for consistency unless the footer is intended.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At extfn/docs/docsfn.config.ts, line 8:\n\n<comment>This site block omits `showFooter: false`, so the layout renders the default \"Built at 21n.co\" footer, while the sibling DocsFn sites authfn/docs/docsfn.config.ts and filefn/docs/docsfn.config.ts both set `showFooter: false`. Existing sites appear to deliberately suppress it; add it here for consistency unless the footer is intended.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -0,0 +1,36 @@\n+  site: {\n+    title: \"ExtFn\",\n+    description: \"Browser extension configuration, runtime, build, scan, and packaging for Chromium and Firefox.\",\n+    basePath: \"/docs\",\n+    editLink: { pattern: \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/edit/dev/extfn/docs/{path}\" },\n+  },\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>\n\n```suggestion\n    basePath: \"/docs\",\n    showFooter: false,\n```\n\n✅ Addressed in [`8c1af41`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/8c1af4123a41b110375feb5aa98a4b68ad5f76b9)\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNogm extfn/docs/content/docs/configuration.md\n<!-- cubic:v=cc50b0fc-d611-4e9d-9f60-0ff02d94acc3 -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=89d77ea6-21bc-5bb6-986a-2332a2024346 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":6} -->\nP3: The example code block uses `defineExtension` without importing it, so a reader copying the snippet gets an unresolved-identifier error. `content/docs/getting-started.md` introduces the same example with `import { defineExtension } from \"@extfn/core\";`; add the matching import here or reference the getting-started guide.\n\n[768 more lines in file. Use offset=281 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1791367530575}}
