tor review caught and corrected two FileFn claims: API material that this generator omits, and an obsolete fallback host. The checkpoint is current; publication remains closed pending final diff review and staging.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_055fb762f51dfcfc016ac619e8f45c87d0824c2e71a14c0601\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_ab5e23a06a7142379c759561c83e8592|fc_055fb762f51dfcfc016ac619ec263487d0b606b659b94b0d57","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/audits/sf-docs-review-20260930/sequential-20261003T184612Z/PR-213/resolved34-bodies.txt","offset":421,"limit":140}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_986a1999d91a429c88c5e11e0e31cc58|fc_055fb762f51dfcfc016ac619f0c9c887d082e288e6481c3b3b","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/audits/sf-docs-review-20260930/sequential-20261003T184612Z/PR-213/preserved-original213-human-pre-use.patch","offset":471,"limit":165}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_4333117cef1e4042adc401a3b115014e|fc_055fb762f51dfcfc016ac619f0c9cc87d0a2d1ac3bd8dd1f1e","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/audits/sf-docs-review-20260930/sequential-20261003T184612Z/PR-213/composition-assessment-supplement.patch","offset":291,"limit":165}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_51555f1f73b042f78f0a7c82a1ef420a|fc_055fb762f51dfcfc016ac619f0c9cc87d087a0ba8d750da39e","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/audits/sf-docs-review-20260930/sequential-20261003T184612Z/PR-213/final-afterimage-changes-since-plan.patch","offset":391,"limit":155}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-6.1-sol","usage":{"input":7619,"output":1404,"cacheRead":204288,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":1034,"totalTokens":213311,"cost":{"input":0.015238,"output":0.01404,"cacheRead":0.0204288,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.049706799999999995}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1791367599450,"responseId":"resp_055fb762f51dfcfc016ac619b08d9c87d0a3108eaa610ab57a","rawStopReason":"completed","thinkingLevel":"high"}}
{"type":"message","id":"17d5df62","parentId":"0ba78407","timestamp":"2026-10-07T10:07:45.061Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_ab5e23a06a7142379c759561c83e8592|fc_055fb762f51dfcfc016ac619ec263487d0b606b659b94b0d57","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n- [GHSA-crpf-4hrx-3jrp](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-27125) **moderate**: Svelte SSR attribute spreading includes inherited properties from prototype chain — fixed in 5.51.5\n- [GHSA-f7gr-6p89-r883](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-27121) **moderate**: Svelte affected by cross-site scripting via spread attributes in Svelte SSR — fixed in 5.51.5\n- [GHSA-m56q-vw4c-c2cp](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-27122) **moderate**: Svelte SSR does not validate dynamic element tag names in `<svelte:element>` — fixed in 5.51.5\n\n…and 3 more — see the OSV links above.\n\nUpgrade to 5.51.5 or later.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn extfn/docs/package.json, upgrade the dependency svelte from 5.0.0 to a non-vulnerable version (5.51.5, 5.53.5, 5.55.7). Update any associated lockfile entries.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n> Not useful? Reply `@mira-rhombus reject` to dismiss this suggestion.\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNvgO extfn/docs/src/lib/components/DocsSiteSearch.svelte\nIn Cloudflare mode, the repo's docs Worker route matches only `/docs*`, so this absolute `/search.json` request bypasses the Worker that serves the new search endpoint. Search will fail on a docs host using the existing deployment pattern, even if the page under `/docs` loads.\n\n<details><summary>Technical details</summary>\n\n````markdown\n# Search endpoint outside Cloudflare route\n\n## Affected sites\n- `extfn/docs/src/lib/components/DocsSiteSearch.svelte:5` — fetches `/search.json`.\n- `extfn/docs/src/routes/search.json/+server.ts:5-8` — registers the handler at `/search.json`.\n- `scripts/cloudflare-docs/config.mjs:101-108` — Worker pattern is `${host}/docs*`.\n\n## Required outcome\n- Keep the search request and server endpoint within the configured Worker route, or explicitly route the root endpoint to the same Worker when ExtFn is deployed.\n````\n\n</details>\n\nAddressed in fec011e by moving both the search fetch and endpoint under /docs/search.json.\n\n<!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ -->\n<sup><a href=\"https://pullfrog.com\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\"><img src=\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\" width=\"9px\" height=\"9px\" style=\"vertical-align: middle; \" alt=\"Pullfrog\"></picture></a>&nbsp;&nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/36233492935/job/108380936639) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)</sup>\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNvgQ extfn/docs/content/docs/reference/consumer-host-abstraction.md\nThe guide includes content mounts as consumers of this host, but content scripts cannot call `tabs.create` directly ([MDN](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Mozilla/Add-ons/WebExtensions/Content_scripts#webextension_apis)). A shared panel using this `goto()` from a content mount will reject with `E_CONTEXT_UNAVAILABLE` instead of navigating.\n\n<details><summary>Technical details</summary>\n\n````markdown\n# Navigation in content mounts\n\n## Affected sites\n- `extfn/docs/content/docs/reference/consumer-host-abstraction.md:16-20,90-94` — the example applies one adapter to pages and content mounts.\n- `extfn/core/src/runtime/browser.ts:31-42` — missing browser methods reject with `E_CONTEXT_UNAVAILABLE`.\n- `extfn/docs/consumer-host-abstraction.md:85-91` — the mirrored root guide has the same example.\n\n## Required outcome\n- Show a navigation adapter valid for the contexts the guide promises, or explicitly scope this adapter to extension pages and show content mounts relaying privileged tab creation through a background handler. Keep the mirrored guide aligned.\n````\n\n</details>\n\nAddressed in fec011e by routing content navigation through the host page and extension-page tab creation through the browser facade.\n\n<!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ -->\n<sup><a href=\"https://pullfrog.com\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\"><img src=\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\" width=\"9px\" height=\"9px\" style=\"vertical-align: middle; \" alt=\"Pullfrog\"></picture></a>&nbsp;&nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/36233492935/job/108380936639) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)</sup>\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNvgR extfn/docs/content/docs/reference/consumer-host-abstraction.md\n`runtime.address.context` is a context label such as `\"popup\"` or `\"content\"`, not the current URL pathname returned by the SvelteKit adapter above. Shared route-aware UI using the stated `currentPath()` contract will see the wrong location in extension surfaces.\n\n<details><summary>Technical details</summary>\n\n````markdown\n# Extension currentPath contract\n\n## Affected sites\n- `extfn/docs/content/docs/reference/consumer-host-abstraction.md:29-31,64-66,95-97` — interface and web adapter describe a pathname but extension adapter returns a context enum.\n- `extfn/core/src/runtime/context.ts:4-17` — `RuntimeAddress.context` is a context kind.\n- `extfn/docs/consumer-host-abstraction.md:90-92` — the mirrored root guide has the same mismatch.\n\n## Required outcome\n- Make `currentPath()` represent an actual pathname in both host adapters, or change the host contract and both implementations to explicitly model different navigation semantics. Keep the mirrored guide aligned.\n````\n\n</details>\n\nAddressed in fec011e by returning the document pathname in both mirrored guides.\n\n<!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ -->\n<sup><a href=\"https://pullfrog.com\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\"><img src=\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\" width=\"9px\" height=\"9px\" style=\"vertical-align: middle; \" alt=\"Pullfrog\"></picture></a>&nbsp;&nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/36233492935/job/108380936639) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)</sup>\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNzq1 extfn/docs/src/app.css\n<!-- cubic:v=14c062be-3481-4a31-a39d-5f10b50ad1b2 -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=062ac4fa-f9cd-5b7a-bd4b-d89f86693fc7 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":5} -->\nP2: This rule wins only if the theme hides the mobile sidebar with `display: none` on the `.docsfn-sidebar-col` element itself; if the theme hides the drawer via visibility, transform, width/grid collapse, or a `--open` class on a wrapper element, `display: block` never re-shows it, and showing it inline in flow doesn't make it an overlay drawer. It also pins the site to theme internals and duplicates a 1023px magic breakpoint that can silently drift on a `@docsfn/svelte` upgrade. Verify the override against the installed theme.css (confirm the hide mechanism and where `--open` is toggled) and note the version + the theme rule this mirrors near this code so a future upgrade is caught; ideally drive open state through the theme's own drawer handling instead of a specificity patch.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At extfn/docs/src/app.css, line 76:\n\n<comment>This rule wins only if the theme hides the mobile sidebar with `display: none` on the `.docsfn-sidebar-col` element itself; if the theme hides the drawer via visibility, transform, width/grid collapse, or a `--open` class on a wrapper element, `display: block` never re-shows it, and showing it inline in flow doesn't make it an overlay drawer. It also pins the site to theme internals and duplicates a 1023px magic breakpoint that can silently drift on a `@docsfn/svelte` upgrade. Verify the override against the installed theme.css (confirm the hide mechanism and where `--open` is toggled) and note the version + the theme rule this mirrors near this code so a future upgrade is caught; ideally drive open state through the theme's own drawer handling instead of a specificity patch.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -70,3 +70,8 @@ body {\n+\n+/* The published theme hides this column on mobile; an open drawer must override it. */\n+@media (max-width: 1023px) {\n+  .docsfn-sidebar-col.docsfn-sidebar-col--open { display: block; }\n+}\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>\n\n✅ Addressed in [`fec011e`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/fec011e7c940d9ddc09b282f33007d9c3ec1aca9)\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNzq4 extfn/docs/vite.config.ts\n<!-- cubic:v=2151a600-133d-49d5-8309-4c7fc40830c0 -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=062ac4fa-f9cd-5b7a-bd4b-d89f86693fc7 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":8} -->\nP2: These aliases rely on synchronous `import.meta.resolve`, which only exists unflagged from Node 18.19.0/20.6.0, but the root `engines` floor is `>=18.17.0`. On Node 18.17-18.18 the config file throws during load, breaking `vite dev` and `vite build` for those versions. Use `createRequire(import.meta.url).resolve(...)` (Node 12.2+, sync, Windows-safe) instead of `import.meta.resolve`, matching the existing `dirname` pattern.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At extfn/docs/vite.config.ts, line 22:\n\n<comment>These aliases rely on synchronous `import.meta.resolve`, which only exists unflagged from Node 18.19.0/20.6.0, but the root `engines` floor is `>=18.17.0`. On Node 18.17-18.18 the config file throws during load, breaking `vite dev` and `vite build` for those versions. Use `createRequire(import.meta.url).resolve(...)` (Node 12.2+, sync, Windows-safe) instead of `import.meta.resolve`, matching the existing `dirname` pattern.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -18,6 +18,9 @@ export default defineConfig({\n   resolve: {\n     alias: [\n\n[488 more lines in file. Use offset=561 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1791367665061}}
{"type":"message","id":"93596e46","parentId":"17d5df62","timestamp":"2026-10-07T10:07:45.061Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_986a1999d91a429c88c5e11e0e31cc58|fc_055fb762f51dfcfc016ac619f0c9c887d082e288e6481c3b3b","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"+- navigation semantics\n+- session/user loading\n+- router state\n+- feature-flag resolution\n+- environment-specific page state\n+\n+Put these in `extfn`-based extension entrypoints:\n+\n+- browser tab/window operations\n+- messaging to background handlers\n+- extension storage access\n+- content-script mount coordination\n+\n+Do not put these in `extfn`:\n+\n+- fake SvelteKit runtime shims\n+- `$app/*` compatibility layers\n+- consumer-specific router/session abstractions\n+\n+## Why this works for `nucleus`\n+\n+`nucleus` can keep a single shared component package as long as the package stops importing `$app/*` directly and accepts a consumer-owned host adapter instead.\n+\n+That lets the same shared component tree run in:\n+\n+- SvelteKit pages with a SvelteKit host adapter\n+- `extfn` pages with an extension host adapter\n+\n+without requiring changes in `extfn` itself.\n+\n+## Related guidance\n+\n+- `extfn` runtime APIs are documented in [ExtFn overview](/docs)\n+- CLI workflow is documented in [CLI reference](/docs/reference/cli)\n+- DataFn integration is documented in [DataFn ExtFn source](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/blob/dev/datafn/extfn/README.md)\n--- reviewed42a/extfn/docs/content/docs/reference/index.md\n+++ preserved213/extfn/docs/content/docs/reference/index.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@\n+---\n+title: Reference\n+description: Source-aligned ExtFn guides and examples.\n+---\n+\n+The detailed guides mirror the existing Markdown documents in `extfn/docs` so repository links remain valid:\n+\n+- [CLI reference](/docs/reference/cli)\n+- [Scanner report](/docs/reference/scan)\n+- [Multiple content scripts and background handlers](/docs/reference/multi-content-and-background-handlers)\n+- [Consumer host abstraction](/docs/reference/consumer-host-abstraction)\n+\n+The [getting-started guide](/docs/getting-started) and [runtime guide](/docs/runtime) provide a shorter path to the current packages.\n--- reviewed42a/extfn/docs/content/docs/reference/meta.json\n+++ preserved213/extfn/docs/content/docs/reference/meta.json\n@@ -0,0 +1,4 @@\n+{\n+  \"title\": \"Reference\",\n+  \"pages\": [\"index\", \"cli\", \"scan\", \"multi-content-and-background-handlers\", \"consumer-host-abstraction\"]\n+}\n--- reviewed42a/extfn/docs/content/docs/reference/multi-content-and-background-handlers.md\n+++ preserved213/extfn/docs/content/docs/reference/multi-content-and-background-handlers.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,150 @@\n+---\n+title: Content and background handlers\n+description: Multiple content modules, message handlers, ports, and Svelte mounts.\n+---\n+\n+This guide documents the repository pattern used by the example extensions for multiple content modules and modular background handlers.\n+\n+## Background layout\n+\n+Use one service worker plus directories for handlers.\n+\n+```ts\n+import { defineExtension } from \"@extfn/core\";\n+\n+export default defineExtension({\n+  name: \"Handler Demo\",\n+  version: \"0.1.0\",\n+  targets: [\"chromium-mv3\", \"firefox-mv3\"],\n+  background: {\n+    serviceWorker: \"./src/background/index.ts\",\n+    messageHandlersDir: \"./src/background/messages\",\n+    portHandlersDir: \"./src/background/ports\",\n+  },\n+});\n+```\n+\n+Message handler:\n+\n+```ts\n+import { defineBackgroundHandler } from \"@extfn/core\";\n+\n+export default defineBackgroundHandler({\n+  namespace: \"demo\",\n+  method: \"ping\",\n+  handle: async () => ({ ok: true }),\n+});\n+```\n+\n+Port handler:\n+\n+```ts\n+import { defineBackgroundPortHandler } from \"@extfn/core\";\n+\n+export default defineBackgroundPortHandler({\n+  channel: \"demo-stream\",\n+  async onMessage(_runtime, payload, _envelope, port) {\n+    await port.send({ echo: payload });\n+  },\n+});\n+```\n+\n+Notes:\n+\n+- `namespace + method` must be unique across discovered message handlers.\n+- `channel` must be unique across discovered port handlers.\n+- Keep domain logic in the owning package when possible; the handler file should be the extension integration edge, not the domain implementation itself.\n+\n+## Multiple content modules\n+\n+You can declare multiple content scripts in one config.\n+\n+```ts\n+contentScripts: [\n+  {\n+    id: \"twitter-anchor\",\n+    entry: \"./src/contents/twitter.ts\",\n+    matches: [\"https://twitter.com/*\"],\n+    anchors: [\n+      {\n+        kind: \"selector-list\",\n+        selector: \"[data-extfn-twitter-anchor]\",\n+        mountMode: \"shadow\",\n+      },\n+    ],\n+    styleIsolation: \"shadow-root\",\n+    normalizeRootStyles: true,\n+  },\n+  {\n+    id: \"youtube-anchor\",\n+    entry: \"./src/contents/youtube.ts\",\n+    matches: [\"https://www.youtube.com/*\"],\n+    anchors: [\n+      {\n+        kind: \"selector-list\",\n+        selector: \"[data-extfn-youtube-anchor]\",\n+        mountMode: \"append\",\n+      },\n+    ],\n+  },\n+];\n+```\n+\n+Anchor choices:\n+\n+- `selector`\n+- `selector-list`\n+- `resolver`\n+\n+Mount modes:\n+\n+- `append`\n+- `prepend`\n+- `replace`\n+- `shadow`\n\n[614 more lines in file. Use offset=636 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1791367665061}}
{"type":"message","id":"21e32a63","parentId":"93596e46","timestamp":"2026-10-07T10:07:45.061Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_4333117cef1e4042adc401a3b115014e|fc_055fb762f51dfcfc016ac619f0c9cc87d0a2d1ac3bd8dd1f1e","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"+| [Skills](./skills) | Application-owned recipes, not bundled executable tools. |\n--- immutable-original-plan/filefn/docs/content/docs/ai-resources/llms-txt.md\n+++ explicit-supplement/filefn/docs/content/docs/ai-resources/llms-txt.md\n@@ -1,92 +1,45 @@\n ---\n title: llms.txt\n-description: The static AI surfaces — llms.txt, llms-full.txt, llms-rich.json — generated on every docs build.\n+description: The two generated FileFn documentation context files and their native docs routes.\n ---\n \n # llms.txt\n \n-filefn publishes three machine-readable surfaces alongside the docs site:\n+The site generates two text artifacts:\n \n-| URL | Format | Use |\n-| --- | --- | --- |\n-| `/llms.txt` | Plain text outline | Lightweight context drop-in for any LLM. |\n-| `/llms-full.txt` | Full plain text | The entire docs as one file. ~150 KiB. |\n-| `/llms-rich.json` | Structured JSON | Pages with route maps, error codes, type signatures. |\n+| Configured publication URL | Content |\n+| --- | --- |\n+| `https://filefn.com/docs/llms.txt` | Page outline and links. |\n+| `https://filefn.com/docs/llms-full.txt` | Full documentation context and configured API material. |\n \n-These are generated automatically by `scripts/generate-llms.mjs` on every docs build (`npm run generate:llms` or `npm run build`).\n+These are configured URLs, not a claim of live deployment. Native prerendered `/docs/llms.txt` and `/docs/llms-full.txt` routes publish the artifacts; root-level static copies are not the advertised docs-owner URLs. There is no `llms-rich.json` generator or endpoint in this site.\n \n-## Format\n+## Generate and check\n \n-`llms.txt` follows the [llmstxt.org](https://llmstxt.org/) specification. A short version:\n+Prepare the repository-owned dependencies and build from the repository root:\n \n-```\n-# filefn\n-\n-> File uploads, downloads, processing, and previews — for any stack.\n-\n-## Docs\n-\n-- [Welcome](https://filefn.com/docs/docs): Overview and capability matrix.\n-- [Getting started](https://filefn.com/docs/docs/getting-started): 9-step walkthrough.\n-- [Quickstart](https://filefn.com/docs/docs/quickstart): Framework-specific.\n-- [Core Concepts](https://filefn.com/docs/docs/core-concepts): Architecture.\n-- [Features](https://filefn.com/docs/docs/features): Bundled features.\n-- [SDKs](https://filefn.com/docs/docs/sdk): Server, client, Python, Swift.\n-- [Adapters](https://filefn.com/docs/docs/adapters): Storage and DB.\n-- [Frameworks](https://filefn.com/docs/docs/frameworks): Production wiring.\n-- [Recipes](https://filefn.com/docs/docs/recipes): Production patterns.\n-- [Examples](https://filefn.com/docs/docs/examples): Reference apps.\n-- [Reference](https://filefn.com/docs/docs/reference): Routes, errors, events, schema.\n-\n-## Optional\n-\n-- [llms-full.txt](https://filefn.com/docs/llms-full.txt): The whole site.\n-- [OpenAPI](https://filefn.com/docs/api/filefn.json): Annotated spec.\n-- [MCP](https://filefn.com/docs/docs/ai-resources/mcp): Live search + fetch.\n+```sh\n+npm exec -- turbo run build --filter=@filefn/docs\n ```\n \n-## Use it from any tool\n+After prerequisites are built, from `filefn/docs`:\n \n-Most LLM clients accept arbitrary text context. Drop `llms.txt` into your project's prompt:\n-\n-```bash\n-curl https://filefn.com/docs/llms.txt > .ai/filefn-llms.txt\n-# include .ai/filefn-llms.txt in your assistant's system prompt\n+```sh\n+npm run generate:llms\n+npm run check:llms\n ```\n \n-For tools that read `llms.txt` directly (Cursor, certain MCP servers), they'll discover it via the well-known URL.\n+The generator loads the consumer's published DocsFn configuration and filesystem provider, builds a manifest, and writes `static/llms.txt` and `static/llms-full.txt`. The shared builder passes `site.canonicalUrl`, uses the published `includeBlog: false` option, and retains the returned canonical URL. `check:llms` compares content without writing.\n \n-## llms-full.txt\n+## Use as context\n \n-When the outline isn't enough — e.g. you want the full route reference and the entire processor catalog inline — use `llms-full.txt`. It's a single document containing every docs page, in IA order.\n+An assistant that supports URL retrieval can use the configured URLs above. If it cannot fetch them, supply a generated local file through that tool's supported context interface. Generated sizes vary with content; use the outline for smaller context budgets.\n \n-## llms-rich.json\n+The default local port is 6001:\n \n-Structured JSON for tools that want metadata (route HTTP methods, error code groups, page tags). Schema:\n-\n-```jsonc\n-{\n-  \"site\": { \"name\": \"filefn\", \"tagline\": \"...\", \"version\": \"...\" },\n-  \"pages\": [\n-    {\n-      \"slug\": \"core-concepts/upload-sessions\",\n-      \"title\": \"Upload sessions\",\n-      \"description\": \"...\",\n-      \"tags\": [\"multipart\", \"uploads\", \"lifecycle\"],\n-      \"url\": \"https://filefn.com/docs/docs/core-concepts/upload-sessions\",\n-      \"body\": \"...\"\n-    }\n-  ],\n-  \"routes\": [\n-    { \"method\": \"POST\", \"path\": \"/upload/init\", \"description\": \"...\" }\n-  ],\n-  \"errors\": [\n-    { \"code\": \"FILEFN_POLICY_NOT_FOUND\", \"status\": 404, \"description\": \"...\" }\n-  ]\n-}\n+```text\n+http://localhost:6001/docs/llms.txt\n+http://localhost:6001/docs/llms-full.txt\n ```\n \n-## See also\n-\n-- [MCP server](./mcp) — live alternative.\n-- [Reference](../reference) — the same content, formatted for humans.\n+Documentation context does not authenticate an assistant, grant access to your FileFn server, or create [MCP tools](./mcp).\n--- immutable-original-plan/filefn/docs/content/docs/ai-resources/claude.md\n+++ explicit-supplement/filefn/docs/content/docs/ai-resources/claude.md\n@@ -1,73 +1,19 @@\n ---\n title: Claude\n-description: Wire filefn into Claude Desktop and Claude Code — MCP server, CLAUDE.md, and recommended hints.\n+description: Ground Claude in reviewed FileFn source and generated documentation context.\n ---\n \n # Claude\n \n-## Claude Desktop\n+Use the generated [LLM context files](./llms-txt) through the context mechanism supported by your Claude client. For repository work, add project-specific instructions to `CLAUDE.md`:\n \n-In `~/Library/Application Support/Claude/claude_desktop_config.json`:\n+```md\n+# FileFn project instructions\n \n-```json\n-{\n-  \"mcpServers\": {\n-    \"filefn\": {\n-      \"type\": \"http\",\n-      \"url\": \"https://filefn.com/docs/mcp\"\n-    }\n-  }\n-}\n+- Read FileFn documentation at https://filefn.com/docs.\n+- Inspect the installed package versions and public exports before changing configuration.\n+- Keep file authorization, tenant context, and upload-session tokens intact.\n+- Verify changes with this repository's tests before running them against live storage.\n ```\n \n-Restart Claude Desktop. The MCP tools panel now lists filefn search / fetch.\n-\n-## Claude Code\n-\n-```bash\n-claude mcp add filefn https://filefn.com/docs/mcp --type http\n-```\n-\n-Or use Droid's wrapper:\n-\n-```bash\n-droid mcp add filefn https://filefn.com/docs/mcp --type http\n-```\n\n[560 more lines in file. Use offset=456 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1791367665061}}
{"type":"message","id":"c36710b3","parentId":"21e32a63","timestamp":"2026-10-07T10:07:45.061Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_51555f1f73b042f78f0a7c82a1ef420a|fc_055fb762f51dfcfc016ac619f0c9cc87d087a0ba8d750da39e","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"+- [OpenTelemetry instrumentation](https://authfn.com/docs/recipes/observability-otel) — Wire authfn's observability events into OpenTelemetry spans for full distributed tracing.\n+- [Password reset](https://authfn.com/docs/recipes/password-reset) — Full password-reset flow — start, verify, change. Two routes, three UI screens.\n+- [Placement-bound auth context](https://authfn.com/docs/recipes/placement-bound-auth-context) — Trusted in-process and private-service AuthFn context for regional application data planes.\n+- [Rotating 2FA encryption keys](https://authfn.com/docs/recipes/rotate-2fa-encryption) — What the shipped two-factor plugin encrypts, and how to change keys without a private crypto API.\n+- [Changelog](https://authfn.com/docs/reference/changelog) — Release history of authfn and @authfn/* packages.\n+- [Configuration](https://authfn.com/docs/reference/configuration) — Every option you can pass to authfn() and app.createServer().\n+- [Envelopes](https://authfn.com/docs/reference/envelopes) — The shape of every authfn HTTP response — success and error.\n+- [Error codes](https://authfn.com/docs/reference/errors) — Every AuthFnErrorCode the kernel emits — HTTP status, retryability, when it fires.\n+- [Observability events](https://authfn.com/docs/reference/events) — Every AuthFnEventType the kernel emits — when it fires and what's in its metadata.\n+- [Reference](https://authfn.com/docs/reference) — The exhaustive reference — every route, error, event, table, envelope, and configuration option.\n+- [HTTP routes](https://authfn.com/docs/reference/routes) — Every authfn route, organized by plugin. Auto-generated from the OpenAPI spec.\n+- [Database schema](https://authfn.com/docs/reference/schema) — Every table generated by `@superfunctions/cli generate-schema` — fields, types, and relationships.\n+- [@authfn/client](https://authfn.com/docs/sdk/client) — The TypeScript client — works in browsers, Node, Bun, Deno; cookie or bearer; with an automatic CSRF, region-aware routing, and a typed surface for every kernel route.\n+- [authfn](https://authfn.com/docs/sdk/core) — The Node server kernel — declare an app with authfn(), then inject runtime dependencies with createServer().\n+- [SDKs](https://authfn.com/docs/sdk) — First-party authfn SDKs — Node kernel, TypeScript client, Svelte bindings, Python kernel, Swift client.\n+- [Python SDK](https://authfn.com/docs/sdk/python) — The authfn Python kernel — same routes, same envelopes, same OpenAPI as the TypeScript kernel, on FastAPI / Flask / Starlette.\n+- [@authfn/svelte](https://authfn.com/docs/sdk/svelte) — Svelte stores, context, and SvelteKit-friendly patterns for displaying sign-in state and reacting to session changes.\n+- [Swift SDK (AuthFnSwift)](https://authfn.com/docs/sdk/swift) — The Swift package for iOS / macOS — bearer-token sessions, native Sign in with Apple, web→native handoff, and SwiftUI helpers.\n \n ## API Reference\n \n-- [Authfn](https://authfn.superfunctions.dev/docs/api/authfn)\n+- [Authfn](https://authfn.com/docs/api/authfn)\n--- reviewed42a/extfn/docs/static/llms-full.txt\n+++ current213/extfn/docs/static/llms-full.txt\n@@ -0,0 +1,784 @@\n+# ExtFn\n+\n+> Browser extension configuration, runtime, build, scan, and packaging for Chromium and Firefox.\n+\n+This file concatenates the full text of every documentation page so it can be loaded into\n+an LLM-based assistant in a single shot. For a page index, see /docs/llms.txt.\n+\n+# Documentation\n+\n+<!-- page:docs:cli.md path:/docs/cli -->\n+# CLI workflow\n+\n+> Develop, build, scan, and package extension targets.\n+\n+\n+`@extfn/cli` ships the `extfn` binary. `dev` watches exactly one target and supports `--open`, `--no-open`, and `--browser`. `build` builds all config targets by default or a selected target list. `scan` analyzes emitted files and manifests. `package` always rebuilds the extension, scans by default, and writes store-uploadable archives.\n+\n+```sh\n+npm exec extfn dev -- --config extfn.config.ts --target chromium-mv3 --no-open\n+npm exec extfn build -- --config extfn.config.ts --target chromium-mv3,firefox-mv3\n+npm exec extfn scan -- --config extfn.config.ts --format sarif\n+npm exec extfn package -- --config extfn.config.ts --target firefox-mv3\n+```\n+\n+Global output flags are `--json`, `--quiet`, `--verbose`, and `--color`. Scan is strict by default: error-severity findings cause a nonzero exit. `--no-strict` preserves findings while allowing success; `package --no-scan` skips scanning. Use these opt-outs deliberately and review the reports before distribution. The [full CLI reference](/docs/reference/cli) lists every option and output path.\n+\n+---\n+\n+<!-- page:docs:configuration.md path:/docs/configuration -->\n+# Configuration\n+\n+> Choose targets, background handlers, page surfaces, and content mounts.\n+\n+\n+`defineExtension` takes a name, version, target list, and background definition. The resolver requires a nonempty name and version and a `background.serviceWorker`. Supported targets are `chromium-mv3` and `firefox-mv3`. Add `popup`, `options`, or `sidepanel` surfaces with entry files, and declare `contentScripts` with stable IDs, entries, URL matches, and anchors.\n+\n+An example with modular background handlers:\n+\n+```ts\n+import { defineExtension } from \"@extfn/core\";\n+\n+export default defineExtension({\n+  name: \"Example Extension\",\n+  version: \"0.1.0\",\n+  targets: [\"chromium-mv3\", \"firefox-mv3\"],\n+  background: {\n+    serviceWorker: \"./src/background/index.ts\",\n+    messageHandlersDir: \"./src/background/messages\",\n+    portHandlersDir: \"./src/background/ports\",\n+  },\n+  contentScripts: [{\n+    id: \"panel\",\n+    entry: \"./src/contents/panel.ts\",\n+    matches: [\"https://example.com/*\"],\n+    anchors: [{ kind: \"selector-list\", selector: \"[data-panel]\", mountMode: \"append\" }],\n+  }],\n+});\n+```\n+\n+Side-panel support is target-gated; do not assume Firefox supports the Chromium side-panel surface. Resolver and manifest behavior live in the [config source](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/blob/dev/extfn/core/src/config.ts) and [manifest builder](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/blob/dev/extfn/vite/src/manifest/buildManifest.ts). Review generated manifests before requesting browser permissions.\n+\n+---\n+\n+<!-- page:docs:content-and-background.md path:/docs/content-and-background -->\n+# Content and background handlers\n+\n+> Register multiple content modules and discover background handlers.\n+\n+\n+The config can declare several content scripts, each with its own ID, entry, match patterns, anchors, and style isolation. Anchor kinds include `selector`, `selector-list`, and `resolver`; each anchor carries its own `mountMode`, with values including `append`, `prepend`, `replace`, and `shadow`. The content helpers manage anchored mounting and reinjection.\n+\n+Background handlers are separate modules discovered from `messageHandlersDir` and `portHandlersDir`. A message handler uses `defineBackgroundHandler({ namespace, method, handle })`; a port handler uses `defineBackgroundPortHandler({ channel, onMessage })`. The namespace/method pair and port channel must each be unique across discovered handlers.\n+\n+`@extfn/svelte` supplies thin page and content mount functions. Components remain ordinary Svelte components; config owns DOM placement and isolation. The [multi-content source guide](/docs/reference/multi-content-and-background-handlers) includes complete examples and the [Svelte demo](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/tree/dev/extfn/examples/svelte-multi-content-demo) shows shadow and light DOM mounts.\n+\n+---\n+\n+<!-- page:docs:getting-started.md path:/docs/getting-started -->\n+# Getting started\n+\n+> Define an extension and run the canonical ExtFn workflow.\n+\n+\n+Create `extfn.config.ts` and default-export `defineExtension(...)`. Configure one or more targets and a background service worker. Add page surfaces and content scripts as needed:\n+\n+```ts\n+import { defineExtension } from \"@extfn/core\";\n+\n+export default defineExtension({\n+  name: \"Example Extension\",\n+  version: \"0.1.0\",\n+  targets: [\"chromium-mv3\", \"firefox-mv3\"],\n+  background: { serviceWorker: \"./src/background/index.ts\" },\n+  popup: { entry: \"./src/popup.html\", title: \"Example Extension\" },\n+});\n+```\n+\n+The CLI is the workflow entry point. Choose one target for `dev` when the config has multiple targets. Production `build` handles all configured targets by default.\n+\n+```sh\n+npm exec extfn dev -- --config extfn.config.ts --target chromium-mv3 --no-open\n+npm exec extfn build -- --config extfn.config.ts\n+npm exec extfn scan -- --config extfn.config.ts\n+npm exec extfn package -- --config extfn.config.ts\n+```\n+\n+Development emits an unpacked extension at `dist/<target>-dev`; production builds emit `dist/<target>`. `package` always rebuilds the selected targets, scans by default, and emits `.zip` for Chromium or `.xpi` for Firefox. Loading an unpacked extension into Firefox remains manual even when `--open` launches `about:debugging`. See [CLI workflow](/docs/cli) and the [vanilla example](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/tree/dev/extfn/examples/vanilla-messaging-demo).\n+\n+---\n+\n+<!-- page:docs:index.md path:/docs -->\n+# ExtFn\n+\n+> Code-first browser extension development for Chromium and Firefox.\n+\n+\n+ExtFn provides code-first configuration, runtime helpers, a Vite build pipeline, a CLI, and a thin Svelte adapter for browser extensions. It supports Chromium MV3 and Firefox MV3 targets, background service workers, popup and options pages, Chromium side panels, and multiple anchored content modules.\n+\n+The [getting-started guide](/docs/getting-started) walks through a config and the CLI. Read [runtime](/docs/runtime) for browser APIs and messaging, [content and background](/docs/content-and-background) for handler discovery and mounts, and [scan and package](/docs/scan-and-package) before distributing an extension.\n+\n+ExtFn owns extension infrastructure. Domain logic stays in packages such as `@datafn/extfn`, which bridges DataFn authority into extension contexts. The optional `@extfn/admin` package currently declares an unavailable capability; it is not an operator UI. See [package integrations](/docs/integrations).\n+\n+---\n+\n+<!-- page:docs:integrations.md path:/docs/integrations -->\n+# Integrations and Svelte\n+\n+> Keep domain contracts and host adapters with their owners.\n+\n\n[2646 more lines in file. Use offset=546 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1791367665061}}
