{"type":"message","id":"e23c332a","parentId":"b372d939","timestamp":"2026-10-07T10:09:55.430Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_ZpIdJmqQ9BPEB9vJw81j8Pa2|fc_055fb762f51dfcfc016ac61a73157c87d0af4bb63baa85a027","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"--- frozen213/.github/workflows/superfunctions-docs-cloudflare-routes.yml\n+++ actual213/.github/workflows/superfunctions-docs-cloudflare-routes.yml\n@@ -13,8 +13,8 @@\n         default: all\n         options:\n           - all\n+          - datafn\n           - extfn\n-          - datafn\n           - filefn\n           - searchfn\n           - authfn\n@@ -44,8 +44,8 @@\n       - name: Sync Cloudflare docs routes\n         env:\n           CLOUDFLARE_ROUTES_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.CLOUDFLARE_ROUTES_TOKEN || secrets.CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN }}\n+          CLOUDFLARE_ZONE_ID_EXTFN_COM: ${{ vars.CLOUDFLARE_ZONE_ID_EXTFN_COM }}\n           CLOUDFLARE_ZONE_ID_DATAFN_DEV: ${{ vars.CLOUDFLARE_ZONE_ID_DATAFN_DEV }}\n-          CLOUDFLARE_ZONE_ID_EXTFN_COM: ${{ vars.CLOUDFLARE_ZONE_ID_EXTFN_COM }}\n           CLOUDFLARE_ZONE_ID_FILEFN_COM: ${{ vars.CLOUDFLARE_ZONE_ID_FILEFN_COM }}\n           CLOUDFLARE_ZONE_ID_SEARCHFN_COM: ${{ vars.CLOUDFLARE_ZONE_ID_SEARCHFN_COM }}\n           CLOUDFLARE_ZONE_ID_AUTHFN_COM: ${{ vars.CLOUDFLARE_ZONE_ID_AUTHFN_COM }}\n--- frozen213/authfn/docs/package.json\n+++ actual213/authfn/docs/package.json\n@@ -7,7 +7,8 @@\n     \"dev\": \"vite dev --port 6005\",\n     \"build\": \"vite build\",\n     \"preview\": \"vite preview --port 6005\",\n-    \"test\": \"vitest run --passWithNoTests\",\n+    \"test\": \"npm run check:llms && node --test ../../scripts/docs-site/check-built-site.test.mjs ../../scripts/docs-site/atomic-write.test.mjs && vitest run --config ../../scripts/docs-site/vitest.config.ts\",\n+    \"check:llms\": \"node scripts/generate-llms.mjs --check\",\n     \"generate:openapi\": \"node scripts/generate-openapi.mjs\",\n     \"generate:llms\": \"node scripts/generate-llms.mjs\",\n     \"prebuild\": \"npm run generate:openapi && npm run generate:llms\"\n@@ -17,7 +18,9 @@\n     \"@docsfn/core\": \"0.0.5\",\n     \"@docsfn/provider-fs\": \"0.0.2\",\n     \"@docsfn/svelte\": \"0.0.3\",\n-    \"@docsfn/sveltekit\": \"0.0.2\"\n+    \"@docsfn/sveltekit\": \"0.0.2\",\n+    \"gray-matter\": \"^4.0.3\",\n+    \"@searchfn/client\": \"0.3.0\"\n   },\n   \"devDependencies\": {\n     \"@authfn/api-keys\": \"0.1.1\",\n@@ -34,13 +37,15 @@\n     \"@sveltejs/adapter-auto\": \"^3.0.0\",\n     \"@sveltejs/adapter-cloudflare\": \"^7.0.0\",\n     \"@sveltejs/kit\": \"^2.0.0\",\n-    \"@sveltejs/vite-plugin-svelte\": \"^4.0.0\",\n+    \"@sveltejs/vite-plugin-svelte\": \"^5.1.1\",\n+    \"@types/node\": \"^20.0.0\",\n     \"@tailwindcss/vite\": \"^4.0.0\",\n     \"@uifn/core\": \"0.0.1\",\n     \"authfn\": \"0.2.0\",\n     \"svelte\": \"^5.0.0\",\n     \"tailwindcss\": \"^4.0.0\",\n     \"typescript\": \"^5.0.0\",\n-    \"vite\": \"^5.4.0\"\n+    \"vite\": \"^6.4.3\",\n+    \"vitest\": \"^3.2.4\"\n   }\n }\n--- frozen213/extfn/docs/README.md\n+++ actual213/extfn/docs/README.md\n@@ -2,23 +2,23 @@\n \n This SvelteKit site uses DocsFn. Consumer guides live in `content/docs`; detailed reference pages mirror the existing Markdown guides in this directory to preserve repository links. Keep both copies aligned when changing an ExtFn contract.\n \n-From the repository root:\n+Prepare repository-owned dependencies and build from the repository root:\n+\n+```sh\n+npm exec -- turbo run build --filter=@extfn/docs\n+```\n+\n+The site resolves its declared public SearchFn/DocsFn dependencies. It does not substitute SearchFn workspace source aliases or prepare missing public `dist` exports during an ordinary direct Vite invocation.\n+\n+After prerequisites are prepared, run from the repository root:\n \n ```sh\n npm --workspace @extfn/docs run dev\n-npm --workspace @extfn/docs run build\n+npm --workspace @extfn/docs run generate:llms\n+npm --workspace @extfn/docs run check:llms\n+npm exec --workspace @extfn/docs -- docsfn validate --root .\n ```\n \n-The build regenerates `static/llms.txt` and `static/llms-full.txt`. For CLI validation, first build the SearchFn workspace dependencies from the repository root (the Vite site build uses source aliases and does not require these separate builds):\n+The native build regenerates `static/llms.txt` and `static/llms-full.txt`. The site defaults to port 6015; documentation and the native LLM-resource routes live under `/docs`.\n \n-```sh\n-npm run build --workspace @searchfn/core\n-npm run build --workspace @searchfn/adapter-contracts\n-npm run build --workspace @searchfn/adapter-memory\n-npm run build --workspace @searchfn/adapter-indexeddb\n-npm run build --workspace @searchfn/client\n-npm exec --workspace @extfn/docs -- docsfn validate --root .\n-```\n-The site defaults to port 6015. The public documentation route is `/docs`.\n-\n-The LLM resources are served at `/docs/llms.txt` and `/docs/llms-full.txt`.\n+Public-origin configuration is applied only when `CLOUDFLARE_DOCS_DEPLOY=1`. `CLOUDFLARE_DOCS_PUBLIC_ORIGIN` names the public receiver independently of `CLOUDFLARE_DOCS_ASSETS_ORIGIN`. A successful local build does not prove live Worker execution, domain readiness, extension behavior, or store approval.\n--- frozen213/extfn/docs/content/docs/getting-started.md\n+++ actual213/extfn/docs/content/docs/getting-started.md\n@@ -26,4 +26,4 @@\n npm exec extfn package -- --config extfn.config.ts\n ```\n \n-Development emits an unpacked extension at `dist/<target>-dev`; production builds emit `dist/<target>`. `package` builds if needed, scans by default, and emits `.zip` for Chromium or `.xpi` for Firefox. Loading an unpacked extension into Firefox remains manual even when `--open` launches `about:debugging`. See [CLI workflow](/docs/cli) and the [vanilla example](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/tree/dev/extfn/examples/vanilla-messaging-demo).\n+Development emits an unpacked extension at `dist/<target>-dev`; production builds emit `dist/<target>`. `package` always rebuilds the selected targets, scans by default, and emits `.zip` for Chromium or `.xpi` for Firefox. Loading an unpacked extension into Firefox remains manual even when `--open` launches `about:debugging`. See [CLI workflow](/docs/cli) and the [vanilla example](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/tree/dev/extfn/examples/vanilla-messaging-demo).\n--- frozen213/extfn/docs/docsfn.config.ts\n+++ actual213/extfn/docs/docsfn.config.ts\n@@ -6,7 +6,9 @@\n     title: \"ExtFn\",\n     description: \"Browser extension configuration, runtime, build, scan, and packaging for Chromium and Firefox.\",\n     basePath: \"/docs\",\n-    canonicalUrl: \"https://extfn.com\",\n+    canonicalUrl: process.env.CLOUDFLARE_DOCS_DEPLOY === \"1\"\n+      ? process.env.CLOUDFLARE_DOCS_PUBLIC_ORIGIN || \"https://extfn.com\"\n+      : \"https://extfn.com\",\n     showFooter: false,\n     editLink: { pattern: \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/edit/dev/extfn/docs/{path}\" },\n   },\n--- frozen213/extfn/docs/package.json\n+++ actual213/extfn/docs/package.json\n@@ -7,7 +7,7 @@\n     \"dev\": \"vite dev --port 6015\",\n     \"build\": \"vite build\",\n     \"preview\": \"vite preview --port 6015\",\n-    \"test\": \"npm run check:llms && vitest run --config ../../scripts/docs-site/vitest.config.ts\",\n+    \"test\": \"npm run check:llms && node --test ../../scripts/docs-site/check-built-site.test.mjs ../../scripts/docs-site/atomic-write.test.mjs && vitest run --config ../../scripts/docs-site/vitest.config.ts\",\n     \"generate:llms\": \"node scripts/generate-llms.mjs\",\n     \"prebuild\": \"npm run generate:llms\",\n     \"check:llms\": \"node scripts/generate-llms.mjs --check\"\n@@ -18,7 +18,8 @@\n     \"@docsfn/provider-fs\": \"0.0.2\",\n     \"@docsfn/svelte\": \"0.0.3\",\n     \"@docsfn/sveltekit\": \"0.0.2\",\n-    \"gray-matter\": \"^4.0.3\"\n+    \"gray-matter\": \"^4.0.3\",\n+    \"@searchfn/client\": \"0.3.0\"\n   },\n   \"devDependencies\": {\n     \"@docsfn/cli\": \"0.0.2\",\n--- frozen213/extfn/docs/src/lib/server/docs-site-source.ts\n+++ actual213/extfn/docs/src/lib/server/docs-site-source.ts\n@@ -1,10 +1,10 @@\n import docsConfig from \"../../../docsfn.config\";\n import { createDocsSiteRuntime } from \"../../../../../scripts/docs-site/runtime\";\n \n-const content = import.meta.glob(\"../../../content/**/*\", {\n+const content = import.meta.glob(\"../../../content/**/*.{md,mdx,json,yaml,yml}\", {\n   query: \"?raw\", import: \"default\", eager: true,\n }) as Record<string, string>;\n-const assets = import.meta.glob(\"../../../static/**/*\", {\n+const assets = import.meta.glob(\"../../../static/**/*.{txt,json,yaml,yml,md,mdx}\", {\n   query: \"?raw\", import: \"default\", eager: true,\n }) as Record<string, string>;\n \n--- frozen213/extfn/docs/src/routes/+error.svelte\n+++ actual213/extfn/docs/src/routes/+error.svelte\n@@ -0,0 +1,12 @@\n+<script lang=\"ts\">\n+  import { page } from \"$app/stores\";\n+</script>\n+\n+<svelte:head>\n+  <title>{$page.status} — ExtFn docs</title>\n+</svelte:head>\n\n[989 more lines in file. Use offset=171 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1791367795430}}
{"type":"message","id":"0c37980e","parentId":"e23c332a","timestamp":"2026-10-07T10:09:55.430Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_zrSZ2ARnPpRH3KtH2r0v0XFP|fc_055fb762f51dfcfc016ac61a73158c87d09e0d3cf471b5df6b","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"+\n+## Svelte content mounts\n+\n+The Svelte adapter stays thin. Mount from the content entrypoint and keep DOM policy in your extension config.\n+\n+```ts\n+import { mountSvelteContent } from \"@extfn/svelte\";\n+import Badge from \"./Badge.svelte\";\n+\n+for (const anchor of document.querySelectorAll(\"[data-extfn-anchor]\")) {\n+  const host = document.createElement(\"div\");\n+  anchor.append(host);\n+  mountSvelteContent(Badge, host, {\n+    props: {\n+      label: \"Mounted from extfn content\",\n+    },\n+  });\n+}\n+```\n+\n+The Svelte multi-content example in this repo demonstrates both:\n+\n+- shadow-root isolation for one content module\n+- light-DOM append mounts for another content module\n+\n+## Browser facade versus raw browser access\n+\n+For content and page code:\n+\n+- use `createRuntime()` to get `rpc`, `events`, `ports`, `capabilities`, and `browser`\n+- use `runtime.browser.call(...)` for Promise-first access\n+- use `runtime.browser.raw` when you need the raw browser global directly\n+\n+## Guidance for package-owned integrations\n+\n+If a package such as `datafn`, `searchfn`, or `filefn` needs extension integration:\n+\n+- keep the integration package under the owning package tree\n+- keep domain contracts in the owning package or shared package\n+- expose only extension-facing glue here\n+\n+Examples:\n+\n+- `@datafn/extfn` owns background authority and proxy client wiring\n+- future `searchfn/extfn` should reuse `@searchfn/adapter-contracts` and `@searchfn/datafn-provider`\n+- future `filefn/extfn` should reuse `@filefn/client`, `@filefn/viewer`, `@superfunctions/files`, and `@superfunctions/storage`\n--- reviewed42a/extfn/docs/content/docs/reference/scan.md\n+++ preserved213/extfn/docs/content/docs/reference/scan.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,114 @@\n+---\n+title: Scanner and report\n+description: Strict scan rules, findings, formats, and packaging behavior.\n+---\n+\n+`extfn scan` analyzes built extension outputs for review-blocking and store-readiness concerns.\n+\n+## Strict by default\n+\n+Default behavior:\n+\n+- error-severity findings return a non-zero exit code\n+- warning and info findings still appear in the report\n+- manual-review reminders are preserved but do not block by themselves\n+\n+Opt-out behavior:\n+\n+```bash\n+npm exec extfn scan -- --config extfn.config.ts --no-strict\n+npm exec extfn package -- --config extfn.config.ts --no-strict\n+```\n+\n+`--no-strict` does not suppress findings. It only changes gating behavior.\n+\n+## Report model\n+\n+Each finding includes:\n+\n+- `ruleId`\n+- `severity`\n+- `category`\n+- `actionability`\n+- `target`\n+- `message`\n+- `file` when available\n+- `details` when available\n+\n+Top-level report fields:\n+\n+- `ok`\n+- `strict`\n+- `generatedAt`\n+- `configPath`\n+- `targets`\n+- `findings`\n+- `summary`\n+\n+Formats:\n+\n+- `text`\n+- `json`\n+- `sarif`\n+\n+## Rule coverage in this repo\n+\n+Current rule families:\n+\n+- remote hosted code\n+- insecure transport\n+- dynamic execution\n+- risky permissions and permission breadth\n+- externally connectable scope\n+- CSP issues\n+- content-script socket usage\n+- manual-review reminders for privacy, single purpose, and store listing readiness\n+\n+The rule layer evaluates emitted manifests plus built files, so package-owned integrations can contribute manifest state without needing an extfn-local duplicate contract.\n+\n+## Structured observability\n+\n+Structured scan and failure logs redact sensitive fields by default. If payloads contain keys such as `token`, `secret`, `password`, or `cookie`, those values are replaced with `[REDACTED]`.\n+\n+This is why the report model is suitable for local automation and CI output without blindly leaking sensitive values.\n+\n+## Practical examples\n+\n+Human-readable scan:\n+\n+```bash\n+npm exec extfn scan -- --config extfn/examples/vanilla-messaging-demo/extfn.config.ts\n+```\n+\n+SARIF:\n+\n+```bash\n+npm exec extfn scan -- --config extfn/examples/svelte-multi-content-demo/extfn.config.ts --format sarif\n+```\n+\n+Custom report directory (relative paths resolve from the parent of the configured output directory, normally the extension config directory):\n+\n+```bash\n+npm exec extfn scan -- --config extfn/examples/svelte-datafn-demo/extfn.config.ts --report-dir dist/custom-scan\n+```\n+\n+## Packaging interaction\n+\n+`extfn package` runs the scanner first unless you pass `--no-scan`.\n+\n+Default:\n+\n+- blocking scan findings prevent archive emission\n+\n+Relaxed:\n+\n+- `--no-strict` still writes the report\n+- the archive is emitted anyway\n+\n+## Example matrix\n+\n+```bash\n+npm exec extfn scan -- --config extfn/examples/vanilla-messaging-demo/extfn.config.ts\n+npm exec extfn scan -- --config extfn/examples/svelte-multi-content-demo/extfn.config.ts\n+npm exec extfn scan -- --config extfn/examples/svelte-datafn-demo/extfn.config.ts\n+```\n--- reviewed42a/extfn/docs/content/docs/runtime.md\n+++ preserved213/extfn/docs/content/docs/runtime.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,20 @@\n+---\n+title: Runtime and browser access\n+description: Use the Promise-first browser facade, messaging, events, and capabilities.\n+---\n\n[444 more lines in file. Use offset=806 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1791367795430}}
{"type":"message","id":"2695d091","parentId":"0c37980e","timestamp":"2026-10-07T10:09:55.430Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_TpTO83JUHWBRPyfSyeGEIkKs|fc_055fb762f51dfcfc016ac61a73159887d0bacdf4701f0b0f43","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"+      // Resolve shared source against this site's pinned DocsFn installation.\n+      { find: /^@docsfn\\/core$/, replacement: fileURLToPath(import.meta.resolve(\"@docsfn/core\")) },\n+      { find: \"@docsfn/core/search-runtime\", replacement: fileURLToPath(import.meta.resolve(\"@docsfn/core/search-runtime\")) },\n       { find: \"@searchfn/client\", replacement: path.resolve(dirname, \"../../searchfn/client/src/index.ts\") },\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>\n\n✅ Addressed in [`fec011e`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/fec011e7c940d9ddc09b282f33007d9c3ec1aca9)\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mN94Z extfn/docs/src/app.css\nThe override makes the mobile sidebar visible, but the pinned DocsFn drawer is fixed at `top: 0` with `z-index: 40`, while `TopBar` remains sticky at `z-index: 50`. The header therefore covers the beginning of the sidebar, including its first navigation entries, so mobile readers cannot reach them normally.\n\n<details><summary>Technical details</summary>\n\n````markdown\n# Mobile drawer hidden beneath header\n\n## Affected sites\n- `extfn/docs/src/app.css:75-77` — the new override reveals the drawer without accounting for its position beneath the top bar.\n- `@docsfn/svelte@0.0.3/src/DocsLayout.svelte` — mobile sidebar is fixed at top: 0 with z-index: 40, and backdrop uses z-index: 30.\n- `@docsfn/svelte@0.0.3/dist/theme-base.css` — sticky top bar uses z-index: 50.\n\n## Required outcome\n- Keep the opened sidebar's first links visible and clickable at mobile widths, whether by stacking the drawer above the header or offsetting the drawer below it.\n````\n\n</details>\n\nAddressed in fec011e by offsetting the open drawer below the measured top bar and reducing its viewport height.\n\n<!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ -->\n<sup><a href=\"https://pullfrog.com\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\"><img src=\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\" width=\"9px\" height=\"9px\" style=\"vertical-align: middle; \" alt=\"Pullfrog\"></picture></a>&nbsp;&nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/36233492935/job/108380936639) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)</sup>\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mPpj3 extfn/docs/README.md\n<!-- cubic:v=ace3b9ec-0634-4982-8cca-e55e460eff94 -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=804fce71-3bb1-546d-b7cc-49349a868699 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":8} -->\nP3: The closing prose line is indented with two spaces, so it visually attaches to the preceding code fence and reads as a continuation of the shell block. Remove the leading indentation to restore it to a normal paragraph.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At extfn/docs/README.md, line 22:\n\n<comment>The closing prose line is indented with two spaces, so it visually attaches to the preceding code fence and reads as a continuation of the shell block. Remove the leading indentation to restore it to a normal paragraph.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -9,4 +9,14 @@ npm --workspace @extfn/docs run dev\n+npm run build --workspace @searchfn/client\n+npm exec --workspace @extfn/docs -- docsfn validate --root .\n+```\n+  The site defaults to port 6015. Set `site.canonicalUrl` in `docsfn.config.ts` after the public host is assigned.\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>\n\n```suggestion\nThe site defaults to port 6015. Set `site.canonicalUrl` in `docsfn.config.ts` after the public host is assigned.\n```\n\n✅ Addressed in [`dd11b96`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/dd11b96aea70743b7838ae7e5dd5e467c1ec2f64)\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mPpj- scripts/docs-site/layout.ts\n<!-- cubic:v=26e2d91d-2cd4-4e2d-a9de-da3646bb3536 -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=804fce71-3bb1-546d-b7cc-49349a868699 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":6} -->\nP3: `observeTopBar` silently returns a no-op when `.docsfn-topbar` isn't found, leaving the hardcoded `--docsfn-sticky-top-offset: 4rem` fallback in `extfn/docs/src/app.css` in effect — the same wrapped-mobile-links mismatch this helper exists to correct. TopBar is always rendered today, but this is shared runtime code that new site PRs copy (per `scripts/docs-site/README.md`), so a selector or theme-class drift would degrade the sticky drawer with no diagnosable signal. Log a warning from the no-op path so the fallback is observable.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At scripts/docs-site/layout.ts, line 4:\n\n<comment>`observeTopBar` silently returns a no-op when `.docsfn-topbar` isn't found, leaving the hardcoded `--docsfn-sticky-top-offset: 4rem` fallback in `extfn/docs/src/app.css` in effect — the same wrapped-mobile-links mismatch this helper exists to correct. TopBar is always rendered today, but this is shared runtime code that new site PRs copy (per `scripts/docs-site/README.md`), so a selector or theme-class drift would degrade the sticky drawer with no diagnosable signal. Log a warning from the no-op path so the fallback is observable.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -0,0 +1,10 @@\n+/** Keep sticky navigation below the actual top bar, including wrapped mobile links. */\n+export function observeTopBar(root: HTMLElement): () => void {\n+  const bar = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>(\".docsfn-topbar\");\n+  if (!bar) return () => {};\n+  const update = () => root.style.setProperty(\"--docsfn-sticky-top-offset\", `${bar.getBoundingClientRect().height}px`);\n+  update();\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>\n\n✅ Addressed in [`d10fbdb`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/d10fbdba0d2b61cc5beaff8741e914a24a72e215)\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mPpkC extfn/docs/src/app.css\n<!-- cubic:v=d98941ad-d77c-4487-9750-750d4c609faa -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=804fce71-3bb1-546d-b7cc-49349a868699 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":6} -->\nP3: `height: calc(100dvh - ...)` has no `vh` fallback. On engines without `dvh` support the declaration is dropped, so the open drawer keeps the theme's full-height sizing while gaining the new `top` offset, pushing its bottom edge past the viewport and making the last nav items unreachable. Add a `100vh` fallback line before the `dvh` one.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At extfn/docs/src/app.css, line 82:\n\n<comment>`height: calc(100dvh - ...)` has no `vh` fallback. On engines without `dvh` support the declaration is dropped, so the open drawer keeps the theme's full-height sizing while gaining the new `top` offset, pushing its bottom edge past the viewport and making the last nav items unreachable. Add a `100vh` fallback line before the `dvh` one.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -71,7 +71,14 @@ body {\n+  .docsfn-site-root .docsfn-sidebar-col.docsfn-sidebar-col--open {\n+    display: block;\n+    top: var(--docsfn-sticky-top-offset);\n+    height: calc(100dvh - var(--docsfn-sticky-top-offset));\n+  }\n }\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>\n\n```suggestion\n    height: calc(100vh - var(--docsfn-sticky-top-offset));\n    height: calc(100dvh - var(--docsfn-sticky-top-offset));\n```\n\n✅ Addressed in [`8c1af41`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/8c1af4123a41b110375feb5aa98a4b68ad5f76b9)\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mPrKM extfn/docs/package.json\n**Security issue**  \n🛑 Blocker — must fix before merge\n\n**Known vulnerabilities in vite@5.4.0**\n\nOSV.dev reports 15 known vulnerabilities affecting `vite@5.4.0`, introduced by this PR:\n\n- [GHSA-356w-63v5-8wf4](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-32395) **moderate**: Vite has an `server.fs.deny` bypass with an invalid `request-target` — fixed in 6.2.6, 6.1.5, 6.0.15, 5.4.18, 4.5.13\n- [GHSA-4r4m-qw57-chr8](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-31125) **moderate**: Vite has a `server.fs.deny` bypassed for `inline` and `raw` with `?import` query — fixed in 6.2.4, 6.1.3, 6.0.13, 5.4.16, 4.5.11\n- [GHSA-4w7w-66w2-5vf9](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-39365) **moderate**: Vite Vulnerable to Path Traversal in Optimized Deps `.map` Handling — fixed in 8.0.5, 7.3.2, 6.4.2\n\n…and 12 more — see the OSV links above.\n\nUpgrade to 6.2.6, 6.1.5, 6.0.15, 5.4.18, 4.5.13 or later.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn extfn/docs/package.json, upgrade the dependency vite from 5.4.0 to a non-vulnerable version (0.1.24, 2.14.1, 2.9.0, 3.2.11, 4.5.10, 4.5.11, 4.5.12, 4.5.13, 4.5.14, 4.5.4, 4.5.6, 5.2.14, 5.3.6, 5.4.12, 5.4.15, 5.4.16, 5.4.17, 5.4.18, 5.4.19, 5.4.20, 5.4.21, 5.4.6, 5.4.9, 6.0.12, 6.0.13, 6.0.14, 6.0.15, 6.0.9, 6.1.2, 6.1.3, 6.1.4, 6.1.5, 6.1.6, 6.2.3, 6.2.4, 6.2.5, 6.2.6, 6.2.7, 6.3.4, 6.3.6, 6.4.1, 6.4.2, 6.4.3, 7.0.7, 7.0.8, 7.1.11, 7.1.5, 7.3.2, 7.3.5, 8.0.16, 8.0.5). Update any associated lockfile entries.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n> Not useful? Reply `@mira-rhombus reject` to dismiss this suggestion.\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mP2_J scripts/docs-site/README.md\n<!-- cubic:v=20ac4afe-88a5-41e5-947e-3a8cc4aac7a3 -->\n\n[328 more lines in file. Use offset=721 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1791367795430}}
