{"type":"message","id":"4ec42aaa","parentId":"b8d183f8","timestamp":"2026-10-07T10:10:38.832Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_428c390abab34dceb9ba874b667fcb21|fc_055fb762f51dfcfc016ac61a94ea9087d0bbd97c261b6f5e20","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"+\n+<main class=\"docsfn-layout\">\n+  <h1>{$page.status}</h1>\n+  <p>{$page.error?.message ?? \"Unable to load this page.\"}</p>\n+</main>\n--- frozen213/extfn/docs/tsconfig.json\n+++ actual213/extfn/docs/tsconfig.json\n@@ -23,6 +23,34 @@\n       \"svelte\",\n       \"vite/client\",\n       \"node\"\n-    ]\n+    ],\n+    \"paths\": {\n+      \"$lib\": [\n+        \"./src/lib\"\n+      ],\n+      \"$lib/*\": [\n+        \"./src/lib/*\"\n+      ],\n+      \"@docsfn/core\": [\n+        \"./node_modules/@docsfn/core\",\n+        \"../../node_modules/@docsfn/core\"\n+      ],\n+      \"@docsfn/sveltekit\": [\n+        \"./node_modules/@docsfn/sveltekit\",\n+        \"../../node_modules/@docsfn/sveltekit\"\n+      ],\n+      \"@sveltejs/kit\": [\n+        \"./node_modules/@sveltejs/kit\",\n+        \"../../node_modules/@sveltejs/kit\"\n+      ],\n+      \"gray-matter\": [\n+        \"./node_modules/gray-matter\",\n+        \"../../node_modules/gray-matter\"\n+      ],\n+      \"vite\": [\n+        \"./node_modules/vite\",\n+        \"../../node_modules/vite\"\n+      ]\n+    }\n   }\n }\n--- frozen213/extfn/docs/vite.config.ts\n+++ actual213/extfn/docs/vite.config.ts\n@@ -7,24 +7,14 @@\n \n const dirname = path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url));\n export default defineConfig({\n-  plugins: [docsSiteCorePlugin(import.meta.url), tailwindcss(), sveltekit()] as unknown as PluginOption[],\n+  plugins: [docsSiteCorePlugin(import.meta.url), tailwindcss(), sveltekit()] satisfies PluginOption[],\n   ssr: {\n-    // Force @docsfn/core through Vite's transform pipeline so the\n-    // `@searchfn/client` alias below resolves the workspace source in dev.\n-    // Without this, the dynamic `import(\"@searchfn/client\")` inside\n-    // @docsfn/core is externalized and resolved by Node, which fails because\n-    // @searchfn/client is not installed as a dependency and its dist is not\n-    // built in the monorepo.\n+    // Declared consumer peers resolve public exports; Turbo prepares workspace dist.\n     noExternal: [\"@docsfn/core\", \"@docsfn/svelte\"],\n   },\n   resolve: {\n     alias: [\n       // Resolve shared source against this site's pinned DocsFn installation.\n-      { find: /^@searchfn\\/client$/, replacement: path.resolve(dirname, \"../../searchfn/client/src/index.ts\") },\n-      { find: /^@searchfn\\/core$/, replacement: path.resolve(dirname, \"../../searchfn/core/src/index.ts\") },\n-      { find: /^@searchfn\\/adapter-contracts$/, replacement: path.resolve(dirname, \"../../searchfn/adapter-contracts/src/index.ts\") },\n-      { find: /^@searchfn\\/adapter-memory$/, replacement: path.resolve(dirname, \"../../searchfn/adapter-memory/src/index.ts\") },\n-      { find: /^@searchfn\\/adapter-indexeddb$/, replacement: path.resolve(dirname, \"../../searchfn/adapter-indexeddb/src/index.ts\") },\n     ],\n   },\n });\n--- frozen213/filefn/docs/content/docs/ai-resources/claude.md\n+++ actual213/filefn/docs/content/docs/ai-resources/claude.md\n@@ -1,73 +1,19 @@\n ---\n title: Claude\n-description: Wire filefn into Claude Desktop and Claude Code — MCP server, CLAUDE.md, and recommended hints.\n+description: Ground Claude in reviewed FileFn source and generated documentation context.\n ---\n \n # Claude\n \n-## Claude Desktop\n+Use the generated [LLM context files](./llms-txt) through the context mechanism supported by your Claude client. For repository work, add project-specific instructions to `CLAUDE.md`:\n \n-In `~/Library/Application Support/Claude/claude_desktop_config.json`:\n+```md\n+# FileFn project instructions\n \n-```json\n-{\n-  \"mcpServers\": {\n-    \"filefn\": {\n-      \"type\": \"http\",\n-      \"url\": \"https://docs.filefn.dev/mcp\"\n-    }\n-  }\n-}\n+- Read FileFn documentation at https://filefn.com/docs.\n+- Inspect the installed package versions and public exports before changing configuration.\n+- Keep file authorization, tenant context, and upload-session tokens intact.\n+- Verify changes with this repository's tests before running them against live storage.\n ```\n \n-Restart Claude Desktop. The MCP tools panel now lists filefn search / fetch.\n-\n-## Claude Code\n-\n-```bash\n-claude mcp add filefn https://docs.filefn.dev/mcp --type http\n-```\n-\n-Or use Droid's wrapper:\n-\n-```bash\n-droid mcp add filefn https://docs.filefn.dev/mcp --type http\n-```\n-\n-## CLAUDE.md\n-\n-Drop a `CLAUDE.md` into your repo root:\n-\n-```md\n-# filefn\n-\n-This repo uses **filefn** for file uploads, processing, and previews.\n-\n-Key packages:\n-- `@filefn/server` — server kernel (createFileFn, FileProvider, Authorizer).\n-- `@filefn/client` — browser/Bun/Deno client (uploadFile, resumeUpload, resolveRenderable).\n-- `@filefn/processing` — bundled processors (thumbnails, PDF, OCR, image transforms, video, audio).\n-- `FileFnClient` (Swift) — native iOS/macOS client.\n-\n-Common operations:\n-- New upload: `client.uploadFile({ policy, file })` returns an `UploadHandle`.\n-- Resumable: `client.resumeUpload(uploadSessionId, file, { uploadSessionToken })`.\n-- Render: `client.resolveRenderable({ fileId, intent: \"preview\" })`.\n-- Server routes: mount `fileFn.router.handle(request)`.\n-\n-For docs, use the filefn MCP server (`search_docs`, `fetch_page`, `get_route`, `get_error`).\n-For workflows, use filefn skills (`list_skills` then `run_skill`).\n-\n-Common error codes:\n-- `FILEFN_POLICY_NOT_FOUND` — policy name doesn't exist.\n-- `FILEFN_POLICY_MAX_SIZE_EXCEEDED` — file too large for policy.\n-- `FILEFN_UPLOAD_SESSION_EXPIRED` — session past TTL.\n-- `FILEFN_QUOTA_EXCEEDED` — storage quota hit.\n-```\n-\n-Claude reads `CLAUDE.md` on every conversation in that repo and uses it to ground its answers.\n-\n-## See also\n-\n-- [MCP server](./mcp).\n-- [Skills](./skills).\n+These are instructions you own, not installed tools or an automatic workflow. This docs site does not implement a FileFn MCP endpoint or publish a verified tool list. See [MCP integration boundaries](./mcp) before registering any independently supplied service.\n--- frozen213/filefn/docs/content/docs/ai-resources/codex.md\n+++ actual213/filefn/docs/content/docs/ai-resources/codex.md\n@@ -1,91 +1,19 @@\n ---\n title: Codex\n-description: Wire filefn into OpenAI Codex / GPT-based agents — system prompt bundle, JSON schema, and tool wrappers.\n+description: Provide FileFn source and generated documentation context to coding agents.\n ---\n \n # Codex\n \n-For agents based on OpenAI Codex / GPT (Codex CLI, ChatGPT custom GPTs, Continue.dev with GPT models):\n+Give your agent the [short index or full context](./llms-txt) through its supported URL or file context interface. Prefer inspected installed versions and repository source over guessed APIs.\n \n-## System prompt bundle\n+Suggested repository instructions:\n \n-Drop `https://docs.filefn.dev/llms.txt` (lightweight) or `https://docs.filefn.dev/llms-full.txt` (full) into the agent's system prompt. The lightweight version is ~3 KiB and gives the agent enough scaffolding to know what's available; the full version is ~150 KiB and is suitable for agents that pre-cache context.\n-\n-## Function tools\n-\n-For agents that support function calling, register the filefn MCP tools. Most clients (Cursor, Continue, ChatGPT custom GPT) speak MCP natively; for ones that don't, write a thin wrapper:\n-\n\n[809 more lines in file. Use offset=351 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1791367838832}}
{"type":"message","id":"68e50ac3","parentId":"4ec42aaa","timestamp":"2026-10-07T10:10:38.832Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_eb58218b96e046fe86c83073f6e229b9|fc_055fb762f51dfcfc016ac61a9e96c487d0985817e0ed8ddf33","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"+\n+`@extfn/core` provides `createRuntime`, context and capability detection, browser access, RPC, events, ports, envelopes, and content primitives. Create a runtime in an extension entry point and pass the active target:\n+\n+```ts\n+import { createRuntime } from \"@extfn/core\";\n+\n+const runtime = createRuntime({\n+  target: \"chromium-mv3\",\n+});\n+\n+const tabs = await runtime.browser.call(\"tabs.query\", { active: true, currentWindow: true });\n+```\n+\n+Use `runtime.browser.call(...)` for Promise-first calls, `runtime.browser.namespace(...)` for a specific API namespace, and `runtime.browser.raw` only when raw behavior is needed. Branch on `runtime.capabilities` for side panel, offscreen, and scripting support. The runtime does not grant browser permissions; declare and justify them in extension config and generated manifests.\n+\n+Use `runtime.rpc`, `runtime.events`, and `runtime.ports` to communicate across extension contexts. Define background handlers in the service worker and avoid putting domain authority in a content script. The [source runtime exports](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/blob/dev/extfn/core/src/index.ts) and [messaging example](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/tree/dev/extfn/examples/vanilla-messaging-demo) show the concrete APIs.\n--- reviewed42a/extfn/docs/content/docs/scan-and-package.md\n+++ preserved213/extfn/docs/content/docs/scan-and-package.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,10 @@\n+---\n+title: Scan and package\n+description: Interpret strict findings and produce extension archives.\n+---\n+\n+`extfn scan` examines built manifests and files for remote code, insecure transport, dynamic execution, risky permissions, externally connectable scope, CSP issues, content-script sockets, and store-readiness reminders. Findings include rule ID, severity, category, actionability, target, message, and optional file and details. Reports can be text, JSON, or SARIF.\n+\n+Strict mode returns a nonzero exit code for error findings. `--no-strict` does not hide findings; it only changes the command result and whether `package` can emit an archive. `package --no-scan` bypasses the scanner entirely. Default packaging runs the scanner first and blocks archives on error findings.\n+\n+The scanner is a local static check of emitted artifacts. It cannot prove that store review, browser permissions, network behavior, or extension runtime behavior will pass in a deployed browser. Run the [example validation matrix](/docs/reference/cli) and inspect the generated manifest and [scan report contract](/docs/reference/scan) before distribution.\n--- reviewed42a/extfn/docs/scan.md\n+++ preserved213/extfn/docs/scan.md\n@@ -83,10 +83,10 @@\n npm exec extfn scan -- --config extfn/examples/svelte-multi-content-demo/extfn.config.ts --format sarif\n ```\n \n-Custom report directory:\n+Custom report directory (relative paths resolve from the parent of the configured output directory, normally the extension config directory):\n \n ```bash\n-npm exec extfn scan -- --config extfn/examples/svelte-datafn-demo/extfn.config.ts --report-dir extfn/examples/svelte-datafn-demo/dist/custom-scan\n+npm exec extfn scan -- --config extfn/examples/svelte-datafn-demo/extfn.config.ts --report-dir dist/custom-scan\n ```\n \n ## Packaging interaction\n--- reviewed42a/extfn/docs/scripts/generate-llms.mjs\n+++ preserved213/extfn/docs/scripts/generate-llms.mjs\n@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@\n+#!/usr/bin/env node\n+import { dirname, resolve } from \"node:path\";\n+import { fileURLToPath } from \"node:url\";\n+import { buildLlmsTxtArtifacts, buildManifest, loadDocsConfig } from \"@docsfn/core\";\n+import { FsContentProvider } from \"@docsfn/provider-fs\";\n+import { buildLlmsSiteArtifacts, withSourceLinks, writeLlmsArtifacts } from \"../../../scripts/docs-site/llms.mjs\";\n+\n+const cwd = resolve(dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), \"..\");\n+const deploymentOrigin = process.env.CLOUDFLARE_DOCS_DEPLOY === \"1\"\n+  ? process.env.CLOUDFLARE_DOCS_PUBLIC_ORIGIN || undefined\n+  : undefined;\n+const { artifacts, manifest, canonicalUrl } = await buildLlmsSiteArtifacts(cwd, {\n+  buildLlmsTxtArtifacts, buildManifest, loadDocsConfig, FsContentProvider,\n+}, { canonicalUrl: deploymentOrigin });\n+artifacts.llmsTxt = withSourceLinks(artifacts.llmsTxt, manifest, \"extfn\", canonicalUrl);\n+artifacts.llmsFullTxt = withSourceLinks(artifacts.llmsFullTxt, manifest, \"extfn\", canonicalUrl);\n+const generatedFooter = \"For programmatic access, prefer the MCP server\\nor the structured manifest emitted alongside this file.\";\n+if (!artifacts.llmsFullTxt.includes(generatedFooter)) {\n+  throw new Error(\"Unexpected DocsFn llms-full footer; review the generated artifact before publishing\");\n+}\n+artifacts.llmsFullTxt = artifacts.llmsFullTxt.replace(generatedFooter, \"For a page index, see /docs/llms.txt.\");\n+writeLlmsArtifacts(resolve(cwd, \"static\"), artifacts);\n--- reviewed42a/extfn/docs/src/app.css\n+++ preserved213/extfn/docs/src/app.css\n@@ -0,0 +1,85 @@\n+@import \"@21n/fonts/styles.css\";\n+@import \"tailwindcss\";\n+@import \"@docsfn/svelte/theme.css\";\n+\n+/* Twenty One Native — same stack as @superfunctions/docs-theme / other monorepo docs */\n+:root {\n+  --docsfn-font-sans: \"Twenty One Native\", system-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\",\n+    Roboto, sans-serif;\n+  /* Tailwind v4 sets html { font-family: var(--default-font-family) } from --font-sans; align it */\n+  --font-sans: var(--docsfn-font-sans);\n+  /* Component theme uses --docsfn-color-* (see @docsfn/svelte theme.css), not --docsfn-primary */\n+  --docsfn-color-primary: hsl(154, 33%, 24%);\n+  --docsfn-color-primary-hover: hsl(154, 33%, 20%);\n+  --docsfn-color-accent-soft: hsl(154 33% 24% / 0.12);\n+  /*\n+   * TopBar is outside DocsLayout but uses position:sticky in theme.css.\n+   * Set this to roughly the rendered top bar height so the docs sidebar/TOC stick below it.\n+   */\n+  --docsfn-sticky-top-offset: 4rem;\n+\n+  /* Whole docs chrome (left sidebar + article + right TOC) max width; centers as a group */\n+  --docsfn-docs-shell-max-width: min(100rem, 100%);\n+\n+  /* Article column max inside the middle grid cell; justify-self:center centers it when capped */\n+  --docsfn-main-column-max-width: 48rem;\n+\n+  /* Sidebar column + full-bleed gutter to the left when the docs shell is centered */\n+  --docsfn-sidebar-panel-bg: #f4f4f5;\n+}\n+\n+@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {\n+  :root {\n+    --docsfn-sidebar-panel-bg: #232326;\n+    --docsfn-color-primary: hsl(155, 39%, 58%);\n+    --docsfn-color-primary-hover: hsl(155, 39%, 54%);\n+    --docsfn-color-accent-soft: hsl(155 39% 58% / 0.12);\n+  }\n+}\n+\n+/*\n+ * Tailwind @layer base wins over unscoped rules in the same file order for html — but unlayered\n+ * rules beat @layer. Force the document font so we are not stuck on ui-sans-serif / system-ui.\n+ */\n+html,\n+body {\n+  font-family: var(--docsfn-font-sans);\n+}\n+\n+/* ─── Site-specific layout (see @docsfn/svelte theme.css for defaults) ───── */\n+\n+/* Homepage / blog: keep top bar content centered with a comfortable max width */\n+.docsfn-topbar-container {\n+  max-width: var(--fd-layout-width, 1600px);\n+  margin-inline: auto;\n+  padding-inline: 1rem;\n+  box-sizing: border-box;\n+}\n+\n+/*\n+ * Docs routes: TopBar inner width matches the docs shell so nav lines up with the article column.\n+ * Same max-width as --docsfn-docs-shell-max-width + asymmetric padding = sidebar + main padding.\n+ */\n+@media (min-width: 1024px) {\n+  .docsfn-site-root.docsfn-docs-chrome .docsfn-topbar-container {\n+    max-width: var(--docsfn-docs-shell-max-width, none);\n+    margin-inline: auto;\n+    width: 100%;\n+    padding-left: calc(var(--docsfn-sidebar-width) + var(--docsfn-main-padding-inline));\n+    padding-right: var(--docsfn-main-padding-inline);\n+    box-sizing: border-box;\n+  }\n+}\n+\n+/* @docsfn/svelte 0.0.3 theme hides .docsfn-sidebar-col with display:none below 1024px.\n+ * DocsLayout toggles --open on that element and supplies its fixed drawer/transform.\n+ * Override display and keep the drawer below TopBar (z-index 50 versus drawer 40).\n+ * Recheck this rule against the pinned theme when upgrading DocsFn. */\n+@media (max-width: 1023px) {\n+  .docsfn-site-root .docsfn-sidebar-col.docsfn-sidebar-col--open {\n+    display: block;\n+    top: var(--docsfn-sticky-top-offset);\n+    height: calc(100vh - var(--docsfn-sticky-top-offset));\n+    height: calc(100dvh - var(--docsfn-sticky-top-offset));\n+  }\n+}\n--- reviewed42a/extfn/docs/src/app.html\n+++ preserved213/extfn/docs/src/app.html\n@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@\n+<!doctype html>\n+<html lang=\"en\">\n+  <head>\n+    <meta charset=\"utf-8\" />\n+    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\" />\n+    %sveltekit.head%\n+  </head>\n+  <body data-sveltekit-preload-data=\"hover\">\n+    <div style=\"display: contents\">%sveltekit.body%</div>\n+  </body>\n\n[274 more lines in file. Use offset=976 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1791367838832}}
{"type":"message","id":"7ef27097","parentId":"68e50ac3","timestamp":"2026-10-07T10:10:38.832Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_a8e383f739d24451bdf8e6401c5fcb60|fc_055fb762f51dfcfc016ac61a9e96c487d0aa77b4a47d7f06e2","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<!-- cubic:review-run=7c66403b-fcbb-598b-9cd0-5dfbd7ebe6ff -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":10} -->\nP2: This says all factory wrappers use the canonical runtime, but AuthFn and FileFn still define local `docs-site-source.ts` copies and do not import `scripts/docs-site/runtime`. Following this guidance will make shared runtime edits silently miss those sites; document the exceptions or migrate them first.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At scripts/docs-site/README.md, line 9:\n\n<comment>This says all factory wrappers use the canonical runtime, but AuthFn and FileFn still define local `docs-site-source.ts` copies and do not import `scripts/docs-site/runtime`. Following this guidance will make shared runtime edits silently miss those sites; document the exceptions or migrate them first.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -4,8 +4,12 @@ The new per-function sites supply their config and Vite raw-content globs to `cr\n+Each site resolves the shared module's DocsFn imports through the scoped Vite resolver so it uses the versions pinned by that site. Run `npm run build` in the affected `<function>/docs` directory. After changing shared code, build all consumers and verify desktop search (including a result navigation and Escape) plus the mobile Menu drawer. Keep the responsive open-drawer override when using the current published theme.\n \n-The new-site PRs carry identical copies of this shared directory so they can land independently. Once merged, edits belong here rather than in the small per-site factory wrappers.\n+Each new-site PR includes this shared directory at the same repository path so it can land independently. All factory wrappers reference this one canonical directory. After merge, edit it directly rather than duplicating provider logic in individual sites.\n \n-AuthFn and FileFn currently retain their existing runtime copies; edits here affect only sites whose factory wrappers import this directory. Migrate those consumers in their respective PRs before treating this as the runtime for every SvelteKit docs site.\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>\n\n```suggestion\nEach new-site PR includes this shared directory at the same repository path so it can land independently. Wrappers that import it use this canonical runtime; AuthFn and FileFn still retain local copies until their migrations land. After merge, edit it directly rather than duplicating provider logic in individual sites.\n```\n\n✅ Addressed in [`d10fbdb`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/d10fbdba0d2b61cc5beaff8741e914a24a72e215)\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mP2_K extfn/docs/src/lib/server/docs-site-source.ts\n<!-- cubic:v=ca7a4445-73b0-46e2-b116-b0263d12dfb5 -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=7c66403b-fcbb-598b-9cd0-5dfbd7ebe6ff -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":6} -->\nP3: This glob restrictively narrows the bundled static assets to .txt/.json/.md, but `createDocsSiteRuntime` treats every file under `static/` as an asset entry (extension-agnostic `createAssetEntry`), so any future non-listed asset (e.g. .svg, .png, .xml, .webmanifest) added to `extfn/docs/static` will silently disappear from the manifest's assets collection with no error. The change also diverges from the sibling sites `authfn/docs/src/lib/server/docs-site-source.ts:30` and `filefn/docs/src/lib/server/docs-site-source.ts:30`, which both use the unrestricted `static/**/*` glob. Keep the unrestricted glob (matching the other sites) or add a comment documenting why only these three types are intended.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At extfn/docs/src/lib/server/docs-site-source.ts, line 7:\n\n<comment>This glob restrictively narrows the bundled static assets to .txt/.json/.md, but `createDocsSiteRuntime` treats every file under `static/` as an asset entry (extension-agnostic `createAssetEntry`), so any future non-listed asset (e.g. .svg, .png, .xml, .webmanifest) added to `extfn/docs/static` will silently disappear from the manifest's assets collection with no error. The change also diverges from the sibling sites `authfn/docs/src/lib/server/docs-site-source.ts:30` and `filefn/docs/src/lib/server/docs-site-source.ts:30`, which both use the unrestricted `static/**/*` glob. Keep the unrestricted glob (matching the other sites) or add a comment documenting why only these three types are intended.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -4,7 +4,7 @@ import { createDocsSiteRuntime } from \"../../../../../scripts/docs-site/runtime\"\n   query: \"?raw\", import: \"default\", eager: true,\n }) as Record<string, string>;\n-const assets = import.meta.glob(\"../../../static/**/*\", {\n+const assets = import.meta.glob(\"../../../static/**/*.{txt,json,md}\", {\n   query: \"?raw\", import: \"default\", eager: true,\n }) as Record<string, string>;\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>\n\n```suggestion\nconst assets = import.meta.glob(\"../../../static/**/*\", {\n```\n\n✅ Addressed in [`d10fbdb`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/d10fbdba0d2b61cc5beaff8741e914a24a72e215)\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mP2_L scripts/docs-site/LandingPage.svelte\n<!-- cubic:v=9ee47608-d1eb-4bc9-b55e-d0259be804be -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=7c66403b-fcbb-598b-9cd0-5dfbd7ebe6ff -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":7} -->\nP3: Landing quick-link cards only change appearance on `:hover`; keyboard users who Tab to a card get the browser default outline with none of the designed interaction cue. Add a `:focus-visible` rule mirroring the hover styles (border-color, box-shadow, translateY) so keyboard focus state matches the hover state.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At scripts/docs-site/LandingPage.svelte, line 178:\n\n<comment>Landing quick-link cards only change appearance on `:hover`; keyboard users who Tab to a card get the browser default outline with none of the designed interaction cue. Add a `:focus-visible` rule mirroring the hover styles (border-color, box-shadow, translateY) so keyboard focus state matches the hover state.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -0,0 +1,216 @@\n+      transform 0.15s ease;\n+  }\n+\n+  .landing-card:hover {\n+    border-color: var(--docsfn-color-primary);\n+    box-shadow: 0 8px 28px rgb(37 99 235 / 0.12);\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>\n\n✅ Addressed in [`8c1af41`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/8c1af4123a41b110375feb5aa98a4b68ad5f76b9)\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mP2_M scripts/docs-site/vitest.config.ts\n<!-- cubic:v=1f5ecf6d-dd1c-4770-a9b1-85ae24f45309 -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=7c66403b-fcbb-598b-9cd0-5dfbd7ebe6ff -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":7} -->\nP3: The plugin anchor resolves the site's package.json from `process.cwd()`, but the test root is fixed to this directory, so the config's behavior depends entirely on where vitest happens to be invoked. Running it from anywhere but a consuming site (e.g. `scripts/docs-site` or the repo root, the natural places given the test file and config live here) makes `createRequire(...package.json).resolve(\"@docsfn/core\")` in `docsSiteCorePlugin` throw MODULE_NOT_FOUND at config load, or silently pin a different hoisted version when one resolves — with no hint in the error. I verified there is no package.json in `scripts/docs-site` or `scripts/`, and resolving from there fails with `ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND`. The single supported invocation is `npm test` in `extfn/docs`, which the README documents but nothing enforces. Fail fast with a descriptive error when `process.cwd()/package.json` does not exist or does not provide `@docsfn/core`, so a wrong invocation doesn't produce a confusing crash (or worse, silent wrong-version resolution).\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At scripts/docs-site/vitest.config.ts, line 7:\n\n<comment>The plugin anchor resolves the site's package.json from `process.cwd()`, but the test root is fixed to this directory, so the config's behavior depends entirely on where vitest happens to be invoked. Running it from anywhere but a consuming site (e.g. `scripts/docs-site` or the repo root, the natural places given the test file and config live here) makes `createRequire(...package.json).resolve(\"@docsfn/core\")` in `docsSiteCorePlugin` throw MODULE_NOT_FOUND at config load, or silently pin a different hoisted version when one resolves — with no hint in the error. I verified there is no package.json in `scripts/docs-site` or `scripts/`, and resolving from there fails with `ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND`. The single supported invocation is `npm test` in `extfn/docs`, which the README documents but nothing enforces. Fail fast with a descriptive error when `process.cwd()/package.json` does not exist or does not provide `@docsfn/core`, so a wrong invocation doesn't produce a confusing crash (or worse, silent wrong-version resolution).</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@\n+import { docsSiteCorePlugin } from \"./vite\";\n+\n+export default defineConfig({\n+  plugins: [docsSiteCorePlugin(pathToFileURL(resolve(process.cwd(), \"package.json\")).href)],\n+  test: { root: fileURLToPath(new URL(\".\", import.meta.url)), include: [\"runtime.test.ts\"] },\n+});\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>\n\n✅ Addressed in [`f15540d`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/f15540d26c2329203c626ccb51eb9108c5bebd84)\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6nFylE scripts/cloudflare-docs/config.mjs\nRegistering `extfn` here makes the deploy workflow upload its Worker, but the separate route-sync workflow still cannot select `extfn` for a targeted `/docs*` binding. A successful deploy therefore does not activate either new docs host unless an operator syncs *all* product routes; please wire ExtFn into the route workflow before relying on the new deploy target.\n\n<details><summary>Technical details</summary>\n\n````markdown\n# ExtFn route activation is not independently selectable\n\n## Affected sites\n- `scripts/cloudflare-docs/config.mjs:8-17` — introduces both ExtFn hosts and their Worker route definitions.\n- `.github/workflows/superfunctions-docs-cloudflare-deploy.yml:115-119` — deploys the Worker but does not sync its zone route.\n- `.github/workflows/superfunctions-docs-cloudflare-routes.yml:14-19,43-50` — excludes `extfn` from dispatch choices and omits `CLOUDFLARE_ZONE_ID_EXTFN_COM`; `all` is the only selectable route-sync path and falls back to a Cloudflare zone lookup.\n\n## Required outcome\n- Allow the route-sync workflow to bind ExtFn's `/docs*` routes for dev and live without selecting and updating unrelated products; provide the zone ID input or ensure the route token can resolve the new zone.\n````\n\n</details>\n\nAddressed in d10fbdb by adding the ExtFn dispatch choice and zone ID to the route-sync workflow.\n\n<!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ -->\n<sup><a href=\"https://pullfrog.com\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\"><img src=\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\" width=\"9px\" height=\"9px\" style=\"vertical-align: middle; \" alt=\"Pullfrog\"></picture></a>&nbsp;&nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/36613785447/job/109561531905) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)</sup>\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6nF0_J extfn/docs/docsfn.config.ts\n<!-- cubic:v=614d870f-e7c9-4b37-8a48-ef8f55305038 -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=e3600364-f803-5837-8cd7-4222d9e23753 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":6} -->\nP2: Removing `canonicalUrl` drops the site's absolute public URLs now that this PR wires deployment to extfn.com/docs. With it absent, `buildCanonicalUrl(undefined, route)` in `+page.server.ts` returns a bare relative path as the page canonical, and `withSourceLinks` in scripts/docs-site/llms.mjs rewrites every `/docs/...` link to GitHub blob pages instead of the live docs host (the regenerated static/llms.txt and llms-full.txt confirm the links now point at github.com). Restore `canonicalUrl: \"https://extfn.com\"` and regenerate the LLM artifacts so the public index links to the docs site; if keeping the host-less fallback is deliberate for dev/prod domain sharing, document that in the config so the GitHub-link artifacts don't read as an oversight.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At extfn/docs/docsfn.config.ts, line 9:\n\n<comment>Removing `canonicalUrl` drops the site's absolute public URLs now that this PR wires deployment to extfn.com/docs. With it absent, `buildCanonicalUrl(undefined, route)` in `+page.server.ts` returns a bare relative path as the page canonical, and `withSourceLinks` in scripts/docs-site/llms.mjs rewrites every `/docs/...` link to GitHub blob pages instead of the live docs host (the regenerated static/llms.txt and llms-full.txt confirm the links now point at github.com). Restore `canonicalUrl: \"https://extfn.com\"` and regenerate the LLM artifacts so the public index links to the docs site; if keeping the host-less fallback is deliberate for dev/prod domain sharing, document that in the config so the GitHub-link artifacts don't read as an oversight.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -3,10 +3,10 @@ import type { DocsConfig } from \"@docsfn/core\";\n     title: \"ExtFn\",\n     description: \"Browser extension configuration, runtime, build, scan, and packaging for Chromium and Firefox.\",\n     basePath: \"/docs\",\n\n[163 more lines in file. Use offset=886 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1791367838832}}
{"type":"message","id":"2143f067","parentId":"7ef27097","timestamp":"2026-10-07T10:10:38.832Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_3d50c1b369c9432882f14e57c65e1faa|fc_055fb762f51dfcfc016ac61a9e96c487d0be436da11b8d65d9","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"-\n-## CLAUDE.md\n-\n-Drop a `CLAUDE.md` into your repo root:\n-\n-```md\n-# filefn\n-\n-This repo uses **filefn** for file uploads, processing, and previews.\n-\n-Key packages:\n-- `@filefn/server` — server kernel (createFileFn, FileProvider, Authorizer).\n-- `@filefn/client` — browser/Bun/Deno client (uploadFile, resumeUpload, resolveRenderable).\n-- `@filefn/processing` — bundled processors (thumbnails, PDF, OCR, image transforms, video, audio).\n-- `FileFnClient` (Swift) — native iOS/macOS client.\n-\n-Common operations:\n-- New upload: `client.uploadFile({ policy, file })` returns an `UploadHandle`.\n-- Resumable: `client.resumeUpload(uploadSessionId, file, { uploadSessionToken })`.\n-- Render: `client.resolveRenderable({ fileId, intent: \"preview\" })`.\n-- Server routes: mount `fileFn.router.handle(request)`.\n-\n-For docs, use the filefn MCP server (`search_docs`, `fetch_page`, `get_route`, `get_error`).\n-For workflows, use filefn skills (`list_skills` then `run_skill`).\n-\n-Common error codes:\n-- `FILEFN_POLICY_NOT_FOUND` — policy name doesn't exist.\n-- `FILEFN_POLICY_MAX_SIZE_EXCEEDED` — file too large for policy.\n-- `FILEFN_UPLOAD_SESSION_EXPIRED` — session past TTL.\n-- `FILEFN_QUOTA_EXCEEDED` — storage quota hit.\n-```\n-\n-Claude reads `CLAUDE.md` on every conversation in that repo and uses it to ground its answers.\n-\n-## See also\n-\n-- [MCP server](./mcp).\n-- [Skills](./skills).\n+These are instructions you own, not installed tools or an automatic workflow. This docs site does not implement a FileFn MCP endpoint or publish a verified tool list. See [MCP integration boundaries](./mcp) before registering any independently supplied service.\n--- immutable-original-plan/filefn/docs/content/docs/ai-resources/cursor.md\n+++ explicit-supplement/filefn/docs/content/docs/ai-resources/cursor.md\n@@ -1,64 +1,21 @@\n ---\n title: Cursor\n-description: Wire filefn into Cursor — MCP server, project rules, and recommended .cursorrules.\n+description: Use FileFn documentation and project rules as Cursor context.\n ---\n \n # Cursor\n \n-## MCP\n+Supply the [LLM context files](./llms-txt) using the context interface supported by your Cursor version. Example project rules:\n \n-In `.cursor/mcp.json`:\n+```md\n+# FileFn\n \n-```json\n-{\n-  \"mcpServers\": {\n-    \"filefn\": {\n-      \"type\": \"http\",\n-      \"url\": \"https://filefn.com/docs/mcp\"\n-    }\n-  }\n-}\n+Documentation: https://filefn.com/docs\n+\n+- Confirm installed @filefn/server and @filefn/client public contracts.\n+- Preserve policy checks, tenant context, and server-side authorization.\n+- Use CAS-capable stores.atomicKv when the FileFn server requires strict shared rate limits.\n+- Run the project's type checks and tests; do not infer live readiness from a local build.\n ```\n \n-Reload Cursor. The Composer panel now has search / fetch tools wired to the filefn docs.\n-\n-## .cursorrules\n-\n-```md\n-# filefn rules\n-\n-This project uses filefn for file uploads, processing, and previews.\n-\n-When asked about file uploads:\n-- Prefer @filefn/client (`uploadFile`, `resumeUpload`).\n-- Always pass a `policy` matching one defined on the server.\n-- Honour OPFS offline if `offline.enabled` is true.\n-\n-When asked about server config:\n-- Use `createFileFn` from @filefn/server.\n-- Wire @superfunctions/db and @superfunctions/storage adapters.\n-- For processing, use processors from @filefn/processing.\n-\n-Reference docs at https://filefn.com/docs. Use the MCP search_docs / fetch_page tools to find the latest content.\n-```\n-\n-## Project rules folder\n-\n-For larger setups, create `.cursor/rules/filefn.md`:\n-\n-```md\n-# filefn\n-\n-@filefn/server is the kernel. @filefn/client is the browser SDK. @filefn/processing has bundled processors.\n-\n-Routes are mounted via `fileFn.router.handle(request)`. The kernel returns `Response | null`; null means 404.\n-\n-Errors throw `FileFnError` with a canonical `code` (e.g. `FILEFN_POLICY_NOT_FOUND`). On the client, errors are `FileFnHttpError`.\n-\n-For more, query the filefn MCP server: search_docs / fetch_page / get_route / get_error.\n-```\n-\n-## See also\n-\n-- [MCP server](./mcp) — the underlying tools.\n-- [Skills](./skills) — pre-baked workflows.\n+This site does not implement a FileFn MCP service, expose executable skills, or guarantee editor-specific automatic discovery. [MCP integration](./mcp) and [recipes](./skills) require separate application ownership.\n--- immutable-original-plan/filefn/docs/content/docs/ai-resources/codex.md\n+++ explicit-supplement/filefn/docs/content/docs/ai-resources/codex.md\n@@ -1,91 +1,19 @@\n ---\n title: Codex\n-description: Wire filefn into OpenAI Codex / GPT-based agents — system prompt bundle, JSON schema, and tool wrappers.\n+description: Provide FileFn source and generated documentation context to coding agents.\n ---\n \n # Codex\n \n-For agents based on OpenAI Codex / GPT (Codex CLI, ChatGPT custom GPTs, Continue.dev with GPT models):\n+Give your agent the [short index or full context](./llms-txt) through its supported URL or file context interface. Prefer inspected installed versions and repository source over guessed APIs.\n \n-## System prompt bundle\n+Suggested repository instructions:\n \n-Drop `https://filefn.com/docs/llms.txt` (lightweight) or `https://filefn.com/docs/llms-full.txt` (full) into the agent's system prompt. The lightweight version is ~3 KiB and gives the agent enough scaffolding to know what's available; the full version is ~150 KiB and is suitable for agents that pre-cache context.\n-\n-## Function tools\n-\n-For agents that support function calling, register the filefn MCP tools. Most clients (Cursor, Continue, ChatGPT custom GPT) speak MCP natively; for ones that don't, write a thin wrapper:\n-\n-```ts\n-const tools = [\n-  {\n-    type: \"function\",\n-    function: {\n-      name: \"filefn_search_docs\",\n-      description: \"Search filefn documentation\",\n-      parameters: {\n-        type: \"object\",\n-        properties: {\n-          query: { type: \"string\" },\n-          limit: { type: \"integer\", default: 5 },\n-        },\n-        required: [\"query\"],\n-      },\n-    },\n-  },\n-  {\n-    type: \"function\",\n-    function: {\n-      name: \"filefn_fetch_page\",\n-      description: \"Fetch a filefn docs page\",\n-      parameters: {\n-        type: \"object\",\n-        properties: {\n-          slug: { type: \"string\" },\n-        },\n-        required: [\"slug\"],\n-      },\n-    },\n\n[390 more lines in file. Use offset=626 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1791367838832}}
