ead","arguments":{"path":"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/audits/sf-docs-review-20260930/sequential-20261003T184612Z/PR-213/resolved34-bodies.txt","offset":886,"limit":170}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_c002041c1110451dadb0acd95f448d2a|fc_055fb762f51dfcfc016ac61b71cad887d0ab6de075ff7eecc3","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/audits/sf-docs-review-20260930/sequential-20261003T184612Z/PR-213/composition-assessment-supplement.patch","offset":626,"limit":180}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_f8b9df28cee04ca7ba615cdd669bf14d|fc_055fb762f51dfcfc016ac61b71cad887d0867d09b38446a766","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/audits/sf-docs-review-20260930/sequential-20261003T184612Z/PR-213/final-current-afterimage-guide-followup.patch","offset":1,"limit":40}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-6.1-sol","usage":{"input":1317,"output":850,"cacheRead":243968,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":516,"totalTokens":246135,"cost":{"input":0.002634,"output":0.0085,"cacheRead":0.024396800000000003,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0355308}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1791368007023,"responseId":"resp_055fb762f51dfcfc016ac61b47c48c87d0bf58636c7413f802","rawStopReason":"completed","thinkingLevel":"high"}}
{"type":"message","id":"80a28f54","parentId":"a6308f1a","timestamp":"2026-10-07T10:14:10.418Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_88e4467bbc0e482181bafc0b39718758|fc_055fb762f51dfcfc016ac61b6ba7a487d0b1ffc2e864877219","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"-```ts\n-const tools = [\n-  {\n-    type: \"function\",\n-    function: {\n-      name: \"filefn_search_docs\",\n-      description: \"Search filefn documentation\",\n-      parameters: {\n-        type: \"object\",\n-        properties: {\n-          query: { type: \"string\" },\n-          limit: { type: \"integer\", default: 5 },\n-        },\n-        required: [\"query\"],\n-      },\n-    },\n-  },\n-  {\n-    type: \"function\",\n-    function: {\n-      name: \"filefn_fetch_page\",\n-      description: \"Fetch a filefn docs page\",\n-      parameters: {\n-        type: \"object\",\n-        properties: {\n-          slug: { type: \"string\" },\n-        },\n-        required: [\"slug\"],\n-      },\n-    },\n-  },\n-];\n-\n-async function handleToolCall(name, args) {\n-  if (name === \"filefn_search_docs\") {\n-    return await fetch(`https://docs.filefn.dev/search.json?q=${encodeURIComponent(args.query)}&limit=${args.limit}`)\n-      .then((r) => r.json());\n-  }\n-  if (name === \"filefn_fetch_page\") {\n-    return await fetch(`https://docs.filefn.dev/docs/${args.slug}/raw`).then((r) => r.text());\n-  }\n-}\n+```md\n+Use https://filefn.com/docs and the generated LLM context files for FileFn guidance.\n+Inspect the actual installed public exports before writing examples.\n+Preserve policy, tenant, quota, and authorization checks.\n+Run local tests before proposing changes; ask before operating live infrastructure.\n ```\n \n-The kernel exposes `/search.json` and `/docs/<slug>/raw` for non-MCP consumers.\n-\n-## ChatGPT custom GPT\n-\n-In the GPT builder:\n-\n-1. Knowledge → Upload `llms-full.txt`.\n-2. Actions → Import the OpenAPI from `https://docs.filefn.dev/api/filefn.json` (the docs site OpenAPI, not the filefn server's OpenAPI).\n-3. Instructions → \"When the user asks about filefn, search the knowledge base or call the search_docs / fetch_page actions before answering.\"\n-\n-## Continue.dev\n-\n-`config.json`:\n-\n-```json\n-{\n-  \"mcpServers\": [\n-    {\n-      \"name\": \"filefn\",\n-      \"type\": \"http\",\n-      \"url\": \"https://docs.filefn.dev/mcp\"\n-    }\n-  ]\n-}\n-```\n-\n-## See also\n-\n-- [MCP server](./mcp) — the canonical surface.\n-- [llms.txt](./llms-txt) — static alternative.\n+The native `/docs/search.json` route is a search index, not a `?q=` query API or MCP service. This docs site has no `/docs/<slug>/raw`, `/mcp`, `/skills/`, `/api/filefn.json`, or `llms-rich.json` route contract. Do not register tool wrappers against invented endpoints. Any independent tool service must define and verify its own schema, authentication, authorization, and deployment.\n--- frozen213/filefn/docs/content/docs/ai-resources/cursor.md\n+++ actual213/filefn/docs/content/docs/ai-resources/cursor.md\n@@ -1,64 +1,21 @@\n ---\n title: Cursor\n-description: Wire filefn into Cursor — MCP server, project rules, and recommended .cursorrules.\n+description: Use FileFn documentation and project rules as Cursor context.\n ---\n \n # Cursor\n \n-## MCP\n+Supply the [LLM context files](./llms-txt) using the context interface supported by your Cursor version. Example project rules:\n \n-In `.cursor/mcp.json`:\n+```md\n+# FileFn\n \n-```json\n-{\n-  \"mcpServers\": {\n-    \"filefn\": {\n-      \"type\": \"http\",\n-      \"url\": \"https://docs.filefn.dev/mcp\"\n-    }\n-  }\n-}\n+Documentation: https://filefn.com/docs\n+\n+- Confirm installed @filefn/server and @filefn/client public contracts.\n+- Preserve policy checks, tenant context, and server-side authorization.\n+- Use CAS-capable stores.atomicKv when the FileFn server requires strict shared rate limits.\n+- Run the project's type checks and tests; do not infer live readiness from a local build.\n ```\n \n-Reload Cursor. The Composer panel now has search / fetch tools wired to the filefn docs.\n-\n-## .cursorrules\n-\n-```md\n-# filefn rules\n-\n-This project uses filefn for file uploads, processing, and previews.\n-\n-When asked about file uploads:\n-- Prefer @filefn/client (`uploadFile`, `resumeUpload`).\n-- Always pass a `policy` matching one defined on the server.\n-- Honour OPFS offline if `offline.enabled` is true.\n-\n-When asked about server config:\n-- Use `createFileFn` from @filefn/server.\n-- Wire @superfunctions/db and @superfunctions/storage adapters.\n-- For processing, use processors from @filefn/processing.\n-\n-Reference docs at https://docs.filefn.dev. Use the MCP search_docs / fetch_page tools to find the latest content.\n-```\n-\n-## Project rules folder\n-\n-For larger setups, create `.cursor/rules/filefn.md`:\n-\n-```md\n-# filefn\n-\n-@filefn/server is the kernel. @filefn/client is the browser SDK. @filefn/processing has bundled processors.\n-\n-Routes are mounted via `fileFn.router.handle(request)`. The kernel returns `Response | null`; null means 404.\n-\n-Errors throw `FileFnError` with a canonical `code` (e.g. `FILEFN_POLICY_NOT_FOUND`). On the client, errors are `FileFnHttpError`.\n-\n-For more, query the filefn MCP server: search_docs / fetch_page / get_route / get_error.\n-```\n-\n-## See also\n-\n-- [MCP server](./mcp) — the underlying tools.\n-- [Skills](./skills) — pre-baked workflows.\n+This site does not implement a FileFn MCP service, expose executable skills, or guarantee editor-specific automatic discovery. [MCP integration](./mcp) and [recipes](./skills) require separate application ownership.\n--- frozen213/filefn/docs/content/docs/ai-resources/index.md\n+++ actual213/filefn/docs/content/docs/ai-resources/index.md\n@@ -1,33 +1,21 @@\n ---\n title: AI Resources\n-description: Use filefn from your AI coding assistant — llms.txt, MCP server, Skills, and editor configurations.\n+description: Use FileFn documentation as assistant context without assuming unimplemented integrations.\n ---\n \n # AI Resources\n \n-filefn ships first-class support for AI coding assistants. The same documentation you read here is mirrored as machine-readable surfaces.\n+FileFn provides generated documentation context at its configured publication URLs:\n \n-| Surface | Use it from | Best for |\n-| --- | --- | --- |\n-| [llms.txt](./llms-txt) | Anywhere | Auto-included context in tools that read llms.txt. |\n-| [llms-full.txt](./llms-txt) | Anywhere | The whole site as a single text file. |\n-| [MCP server](./mcp) | MCP-aware clients (Claude Desktop, Cursor, etc.) | Live search + page fetch. |\n-| [Skills](./skills) | Skill-aware assistants | Pre-baked workflows (set up filefn, add a processor, debug a stuck upload). |\n-| [Cursor](./cursor) | Cursor IDE | Project-level rules + skills. |\n-| [Claude](./claude) | Claude Code / Claude Desktop | CLAUDE.md hints + MCP wiring. |\n\n[629 more lines in file. Use offset=531 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1791368050418}}
{"type":"message","id":"82fabd17","parentId":"80a28f54","timestamp":"2026-10-07T10:14:10.419Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_306b50c449384abcb7c21976a232d03a|fc_055fb762f51dfcfc016ac61b71cad887d0ba8a9a572ad03c97","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"+</html>\n--- reviewed42a/extfn/docs/src/lib/components/DocsSiteSearch.svelte\n+++ preserved213/extfn/docs/src/lib/components/DocsSiteSearch.svelte\n@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@\n+<script lang=\"ts\">\n+  import Search from \"@site/docs-search\";\n+</script>\n+\n+<Search />\n--- reviewed42a/extfn/docs/src/routes/+layout.server.ts\n+++ preserved213/extfn/docs/src/routes/+layout.server.ts\n@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@\n+import { loadDocsSiteSource } from \"$lib/server/docs-site-source\";\n+import type { LayoutServerLoad } from \"./$types\";\n+\n+export const load: LayoutServerLoad = async () => {\n+  const source = await loadDocsSiteSource();\n+  // Keep the complete content manifest and search index on the server.\n+  return {\n+    source: {\n+      siteTitle: source.siteTitle,\n+      config: { site: source.config.site, navigation: source.config.navigation },\n+    },\n+  };\n+};\n--- reviewed42a/extfn/docs/src/routes/+layout.svelte\n+++ preserved213/extfn/docs/src/routes/+layout.svelte\n@@ -0,0 +1,86 @@\n+<script lang=\"ts\">\n+  import \"../app.css\";\n+  import DocsSiteSearch from \"$lib/components/DocsSiteSearch.svelte\";\n+  import TopBar from \"@docsfn/svelte/TopBar.svelte\";\n+  import { page } from \"$app/stores\";\n+  import { onMount, type Snippet } from \"svelte\";\n+  import { observeTopBar } from \"../../../../scripts/docs-site/layout\";\n+  import type { LayoutData } from \"./$types\";\n+\n+  interface Props {\n+    data: LayoutData;\n+    children: Snippet;\n+  }\n+\n+  let { data, children }: Props = $props();\n+  let siteRoot: HTMLDivElement;\n+  onMount(() => observeTopBar(siteRoot));\n+\n+</script>\n+\n+<div\n+  bind:this={siteRoot}\n+  class=\"docsfn-site-root\"\n+  class:docsfn-docs-chrome={$page.url.pathname.startsWith(\"/docs\")}\n+>\n+  <TopBar\n+    items={data.source.config.navigation?.topNav}\n+    searchTrigger={DocsSiteSearch}\n+  />\n+  <div class=\"docsfn-site-main\">\n+    {@render children()}\n+  </div>\n+  {#if data.source.config.site.showFooter !== false}\n+    <footer class=\"docsfn-site-footer\">\n+      <p>Built at <a href=\"https://21n.co\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">21n.co</a></p>\n+    </footer>\n+  {/if}\n+</div>\n+\n+<style>\n+  .docsfn-site-root {\n+    min-height: 100vh;\n+    width: 100%;\n+    max-width: none;\n+    display: flex;\n+    flex-direction: column;\n+  }\n+\n+  .docsfn-site-main {\n+    flex: 1;\n+    min-height: 0;\n+    display: flex;\n+    flex-direction: column;\n+  }\n+\n+  .docsfn-site-footer {\n+    flex-shrink: 0;\n+    align-self: stretch;\n+    width: 100%;\n+    max-width: none;\n+    box-sizing: border-box;\n+    position: relative;\n+    z-index: 2;\n+    border-top: 1px solid var(--docsfn-color-border);\n+    padding: 1rem 1.5rem;\n+    text-align: center;\n+    font-size: 0.875rem;\n+    color: var(--docsfn-color-muted);\n+    background: var(--docsfn-color-surface);\n+    transition: var(--docsfn-transition-theme);\n+  }\n+\n+  .docsfn-site-footer p {\n+    margin: 0;\n+  }\n+\n+  .docsfn-site-footer a {\n+    color: var(--docsfn-color-primary);\n+    text-decoration: none;\n+    font-weight: 500;\n+  }\n+\n+  .docsfn-site-footer a:hover {\n+    text-decoration: underline;\n+  }\n+</style>\n--- reviewed42a/extfn/docs/src/routes/+page.svelte\n+++ preserved213/extfn/docs/src/routes/+page.svelte\n@@ -0,0 +1,28 @@\n+<script lang=\"ts\">\n+  import LandingPage from \"../../../../scripts/docs-site/LandingPage.svelte\";\n+  import type { PageData } from \"./$types\";\n+\n+  interface Props {\n+    data: PageData;\n+  }\n+\n+  let { data }: Props = $props();\n+\n+  const tagline = \"Build browser extensions from one code-first config.\";\n+\n+  const features = [\n+    { title: \"Multi-target builds\", text: \"Build Chromium and Firefox MV3 outputs from one config.\" },\n+    { title: \"Runtime helpers\", text: \"Use Promise-first browser APIs, messaging, events, and ports.\" },\n+    { title: \"Content surfaces\", text: \"Mount multiple content scripts and Svelte components.\" },\n+    { title: \"Release workflow\", text: \"Scan built outputs and package store-uploadable archives.\" },\n+  ];\n+\n+  const quickLinks = [\n+    { label: \"Get started\", href: \"/docs/getting-started\", blurb: \"Create a config and build your first extension.\" },\n+    { label: \"Runtime\", href: \"/docs/runtime\", blurb: \"Use browser access, messaging, and capabilities.\" },\n+    { label: \"CLI workflow\", href: \"/docs/cli\", blurb: \"Develop, build, scan, and package targets.\" },\n+    { label: \"Reference\", href: \"/docs/reference\", blurb: \"Package map and source-aligned reference guides.\" },\n+  ];\n+</script>\n+\n+<LandingPage name=\"ExtFn\" siteTitle={data.source.siteTitle} description={data.source.config.site.description} {tagline} {features} {quickLinks} />\n--- reviewed42a/extfn/docs/src/routes/docs/[...slug]/+page.server.ts\n+++ preserved213/extfn/docs/src/routes/docs/[...slug]/+page.server.ts\n@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@\n+import { resolveMarkdownRelativeLinks } from \"@docsfn/core\";\n+import { getCompiledDocsPage, loadDocsSiteSource } from \"$lib/server/docs-site-source\";\n+import { loadDocsPage } from \"../../../../../../scripts/docs-site/page\";\n+import type { PageServerLoad } from \"./$types\";\n+\n+export const load: PageServerLoad = async ({ params }) => {\n+  const result = await loadDocsPage({\n\n[119 more lines in file. Use offset=1131 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1791368050419}}
