{"type":"message","id":"8349349b","parentId":"1b9a0aef","timestamp":"2026-10-07T10:31:50.097Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_7bcfaf57ece34a6d913405b6f154702e|fc_055fb762f51dfcfc016ac61f937ca087d09f844a2e1ec5749c","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Captured56 thread concerns, de-duplicated display only\n\nSame frozen collection. Only the explicitly AI-agent prompt details block is omitted; all comments and other visible body text remain, with resolved/outdated metadata. No new collection, classification or publication admission. Original full bodies remain authoritative.\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNmGb resolved=True outdated=True extfn/docs/src/lib/server/docs-site-source.ts\nComment PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM70-65r\n![kody code-review](https://img.shields.io/badge/kody-code--review-312B4B?labelColor=C9BBF2) ![Bug](https://img.shields.io/badge/Bug-B71C1C) ![medium](https://img.shields.io/badge/severity_level-medium-1A7BBE)\n\n\nparseFrontmatter only recognizes frontmatter when the file starts with exactly \"---\\n\" (LF, no BOM), and it scans for \"\\n---\" without allowing CRLF before the closing fence. a markdown file with CRLF line endings or a BOM has its frontmatter treated as page body, so the title/description leak visibly into rendered docs pages and llms.txt artifacts. match /^---\\r?\\n/ for the opening fence and /\\r?\\n---(\\r?\\n|$)/ for the closing fence.\n\n```typescript\nif (!/^---\\r?\\n/.test(source)) {\n    return { body: source, frontmatter: {} };\n  }\n\n  const closingIndex = source.search(/\\r?\\n---(\\r?\\n|$)/, );\n```\n\n\n\n<details>\n\n<summary>Prompt for LLM</summary>\n\n```\n\nFile extfn/docs/src/lib/server/docs-site-source.ts:\n\nLine 447 to 457:\n\nparseFrontmatter only recognizes frontmatter when the file starts with exactly \"---\\n\" (LF, no BOM), and it scans for \"\\n---\" without allowing CRLF before the closing fence. a markdown file with CRLF line endings or a BOM has its frontmatter treated as page body, so the title/description leak visibly into rendered docs pages and llms.txt artifacts. match /^---\\r?\\n/ for the opening fence and /\\r?\\n---(\\r?\\n|$)/ for the closing fence.\n\nSuggested Code:\n\nif (!/^---\\r?\\n/.test(source)) {\n    return { body: source, frontmatter: {} };\n  }\n\n  const closingIndex = source.search(/\\r?\\n---(\\r?\\n|$)/, );\n\n```\n\n</details>\n\n\n<sub>Talk to Kody by mentioning @kody</sub>\n\n\n<sub>Was this suggestion helpful? React with 👍 or 👎 to help Kody learn from this interaction.</sub>\n\n<!-- kody-codereview -->&#8203;\n&#8203;\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNmI6 resolved=True outdated=True extfn/docs/src/lib/server/docs-site-source.ts\nComment PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM70-69g\n![kody code-review](https://img.shields.io/badge/kody-code--review-312B4B?labelColor=C9BBF2) ![Bug](https://img.shields.io/badge/Bug-B71C1C) ![medium](https://img.shields.io/badge/severity_level-medium-1A7BBE)\n\n\nparseFrontmatter only recognizes frontmatter when the file starts with exactly `\"---\\n\"` and locates the closing delimiter with `indexOf(\"\\n---\", 4)`. any markdown file with CRLF line endings (e.g. authored on Windows) or a leading BOM silently fails frontmatter detection, so `title`/`description` render as literal body text and the page title falls back to the filename via deriveTitleFromPath. accept `---\\r\\n` (e.g. test with `/^---\\r?\\n/` or normalize line endings before parsing) and treat a BOM-prefixed source as frontmatter-bearing.\n\n\n\n\n\n<details>\n\n<summary>Prompt for LLM</summary>\n\n```\n\nFile extfn/docs/src/lib/server/docs-site-source.ts:\n\nLine 447 to 457:\n\nparseFrontmatter only recognizes frontmatter when the file starts with exactly `\"---\\n\"` and locates the closing delimiter with `indexOf(\"\\n---\", 4)`. any markdown file with CRLF line endings (e.g. authored on Windows) or a leading BOM silently fails frontmatter detection, so `title`/`description` render as literal body text and the page title falls back to the filename via deriveTitleFromPath. accept `---\\r\\n` (e.g. test with `/^---\\r?\\n/` or normalize line endings before parsing) and treat a BOM-prefixed source as frontmatter-bearing.\n\n```\n\n</details>\n\n\n<sub>Talk to Kody by mentioning @kody</sub>\n\n\n<sub>Was this suggestion helpful? React with 👍 or 👎 to help Kody learn from this interaction.</sub>\n\n<!-- kody-codereview -->&#8203;\n&#8203;\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNogZ resolved=True outdated=True extfn/docs/src/routes/+layout.server.ts\nComment PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM70--iu\n<!-- cubic:v=11e9947b-9a89-45cf-9ffd-2ceb123583ac -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=89d77ea6-21bc-5bb6-986a-2332a2024346 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":8} -->\nP2: The root layout returns the entire `DocsSiteSource` (manifest with every page's body, the full search artifact, and config) from a server load. SvelteKit serializes this into the client payload of every page and every client-side navigation, even though the client only reads `source.config.navigation.topNav`, `source.config.site.showFooter`/`description`, and `source.siteTitle` (+layout.svelte, +page.svelte). `manifest` and `searchArtifact` are consumed only server-side by `/docs/[...slug]/+page.server.ts` via `parent()` (search already has its own `/search.json` endpoint), so the whole corpus and search index are duplicated into every HTML response. Return only the config fields the chrome needs and let child server loads import the state directly.\n\n\n[Duplicated AI-agent prompt block omitted from this display; full original retained.]\n\n\n✅ Addressed in [`3dd6ff1`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/3dd6ff1a256c8289979ff29b10f4a59a31869d47)\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNoga resolved=True outdated=True extfn/docs/vite.config.ts\nComment PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM70--iw\n<!-- cubic:v=3f7dcd66-bd01-48b1-aaba-983ff346f98a -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=89d77ea6-21bc-5bb6-986a-2332a2024346 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":6} -->\nP2: Vite's string `find` aliases match by prefix, so these entries also intercept subpath imports. `searchfn/client/package.json` exports `@searchfn/client/constructors` and `@searchfn/client/in-memory-search`; if `@docsfn/core` or `@searchfn` source imports either, the import is rewritten to `searchfn/client/src/index.ts/constructors` (a non-existent path) instead of `src/constructors.ts`, breaking dev/build resolution. Anchor each alias with an anchored regex or a `$`-terminated find so only the bare specifier matches.\n\n\n[Duplicated AI-agent prompt block omitted from this display; full original retained.]\n\n\n✅ Addressed in [`fec011e`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/fec011e7c940d9ddc09b282f33007d9c3ec1aca9)\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNogd resolved=True outdated=True extfn/docs/tsconfig.json\nComment PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM70--iz\n<!-- cubic:v=16ae4880-db13-405a-9cb4-fe8c945a52f7 -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=89d77ea6-21bc-5bb6-986a-2332a2024346 -->\n\n[1198 more lines in file. Use offset=121 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1791369110097}}
{"type":"message","id":"8480f2c2","parentId":"8349349b","timestamp":"2026-10-07T10:31:50.097Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_0e883edd39534b8bad6d9117e8075b6b|fc_055fb762f51dfcfc016ac61f95e43887d097ea8084229144c1","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":7} -->\nP2: In tsconfig `extends`, the derived `include` replaces the `include` generated inside `.svelte-kit/tsconfig.json`, so `.svelte-kit/ambient.d.ts` and the generated types are left out of the TS program. Any `$env/*` import (or other kit-generated ambient type) will then fail with \"Cannot find module\" under svelte-check/editors while Vite build still passes. Note that `authfn/docs` and `filefn/docs` don't extend the kit config at all, and the repo's other SvelteKit apps (`filefn/examples/*/client/tsconfig.json`) extend it without overriding `include` — this file is the first to both extend and replace it. Add the `.svelte-kit` globs to `include` (or drop the block and let the generated config own the file list, keeping `vite.config.ts`/`svelte.config.js` covered).\n\n\n[Duplicated AI-agent prompt block omitted from this display; full original retained.]\n\n\n```suggestion\n  \"include\": [\n    \".svelte-kit/ambient.d.ts\",\n    \".svelte-kit/types/**/*.d.ts\",\n    \"src/**/*.ts\",\n    \"src/**/*.js\",\n    \"src/**/*.svelte\",\n    \"vite.config.ts\",\n    \"svelte.config.js\"\n  ]\n```\n\n✅ Addressed in [`fec011e`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/fec011e7c940d9ddc09b282f33007d9c3ec1aca9)\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNogf resolved=True outdated=True extfn/docs/content/docs/cli.md\nComment PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM70--i3\n<!-- cubic:v=64e72c79-8e66-41e2-9f31-c002e7780093 -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=89d77ea6-21bc-5bb6-986a-2332a2024346 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":9} -->\nP2: `package` is not conditional: `runPackageCommand` calls `buildExtension` on every invocation before scanning or archiving. Document that it always rebuilds, or add an output-existence check before promising reuse. This can incur full builds and fail on source/config changes even when valid artifacts already exist.\n\n\n[Duplicated AI-agent prompt block omitted from this display; full original retained.]\n\n\n✅ Addressed in [`fec011e`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/fec011e7c940d9ddc09b282f33007d9c3ec1aca9)\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNogg resolved=False outdated=True extfn/docs/content/docs/reference/consumer-host-abstraction.md\nComment PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM70--i4\n<!-- cubic:v=af5a2818-0cac-42a2-b3ea-497acfcbff8e -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=89d77ea6-21bc-5bb6-986a-2332a2024346 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":10} -->\nP2: `runtime.address.context` is a context kind, not the current URL path, so this adapter returns incorrect route state for shared navigation. Return `globalThis.location?.pathname ?? \"\"` and update the mirrored guide and generated LLM artifact.\n\n\n[Duplicated AI-agent prompt block omitted from this display; full original retained.]\n\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNogi resolved=False outdated=True extfn/docs/src/lib/server/docs-site-source.ts\nComment PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM70--i6\n<!-- cubic:v=2568cae0-99c9-4d90-89c3-db47ded3eb63 -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=89d77ea6-21bc-5bb6-986a-2332a2024346 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":9} -->\nP2: Normalize a leading BOM and CRLF line endings before detecting frontmatter; otherwise affected pages render their metadata as body text and fall back to filename-derived titles.\n\n\n[Duplicated AI-agent prompt block omitted from this display; full original retained.]\n\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNogk resolved=True outdated=True extfn/docs/content/docs/content-and-background.md\nComment PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM70--i8\n<!-- cubic:v=8aac9b42-10d9-470a-be39-5b7cb24bfc36 -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=89d77ea6-21bc-5bb6-986a-2332a2024346 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":6} -->\nP3: The sentence lists `mount mode` as a per-content-script property, but the config puts `mountMode` on each anchor (selector/selector-list/resolver), not on the script itself. Rephrase so the script owns ID/entry/match patterns/anchors/style isolation and each anchor carries its own mount mode.\n\n\n[Duplicated AI-agent prompt block omitted from this display; full original retained.]\n\n\n✅ Addressed in [`fec011e`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/fec011e7c940d9ddc09b282f33007d9c3ec1aca9)\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNogl resolved=True outdated=False extfn/docs/docsfn.config.ts\nComment PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM70--i9\n<!-- cubic:v=4a365efe-16f0-45db-94f9-4583319cbcfa -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=89d77ea6-21bc-5bb6-986a-2332a2024346 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":6} -->\nP3: This site block omits `showFooter: false`, so the layout renders the default \"Built at 21n.co\" footer, while the sibling DocsFn sites authfn/docs/docsfn.config.ts and filefn/docs/docsfn.config.ts both set `showFooter: false`. Existing sites appear to deliberately suppress it; add it here for consistency unless the footer is intended.\n\n\n[Duplicated AI-agent prompt block omitted from this display; full original retained.]\n\n\n```suggestion\n    basePath: \"/docs\",\n    showFooter: false,\n```\n\n✅ Addressed in [`8c1af41`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/8c1af4123a41b110375feb5aa98a4b68ad5f76b9)\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNogm resolved=True outdated=False extfn/docs/content/docs/configuration.md\nComment PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM70--i-\n<!-- cubic:v=cc50b0fc-d611-4e9d-9f60-0ff02d94acc3 -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=89d77ea6-21bc-5bb6-986a-2332a2024346 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":6} -->\nP3: The example code block uses `defineExtension` without importing it, so a reader copying the snippet gets an unresolved-identifier error. `content/docs/getting-started.md` introduces the same example with `import { defineExtension } from \"@extfn/core\";`; add the matching import here or reference the getting-started guide.\n\n\n[Duplicated AI-agent prompt block omitted from this display; full original retained.]\n\n\n```suggestion\nimport { defineExtension } from \"@extfn/core\";\n\nexport default defineExtension({\n```\n\n✅ Addressed in [`fec011e`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/fec011e7c940d9ddc09b282f33007d9c3ec1aca9)\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNogn resolved=False outdated=True extfn/docs/src/lib/server/docs-site-source.ts\nComment PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM70--jA\n<!-- cubic:v=004ae9b0-d32e-441b-9708-e35300429565 -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=89d77ea6-21bc-5bb6-986a-2332a2024346 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":8} -->\nP3: This site does not use the post compiler or the cache-summary/search-runtime helpers, so these exported paths are dead code in the consumer app. Remove the unused helpers and post cache, or add the routes/tests that consume them to avoid carrying an unreachable generalized scaffold.\n\n\n[Duplicated AI-agent prompt block omitted from this display; full original retained.]\n\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNogo resolved=True outdated=True extfn/docs/content/docs/runtime.md\nComment PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM70--jB\n<!-- cubic:v=92a5513f-0079-4b6a-befd-8db36bc53a43 -->\n\n[1078 more lines in file. Use offset=241 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1791369110097}}
