{"type":"message","id":"7b9f2193","parentId":"2725eca8","timestamp":"2026-10-07T10:32:02.889Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_2LIiv9EWF8wPcVbSeeOC0mSr|fc_055fb762f51dfcfc016ac61fa2adb087d095a627568b7ece69","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<!-- cubic:review-run=89d77ea6-21bc-5bb6-986a-2332a2024346 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":8} -->\nP3: The example's `globals: globalThis as never` is redundant and teaches a bad pattern: `createRuntime` already defaults `globals` to `globalThis` and derives `rawBrowser` from `globals.browser ?? globals.chrome ?? {}` (extfn/core/src/runtime/getRuntime.ts:58-64), so both options add nothing here while `as never` is a confusing cast for readers to copy. Omit `globals` and `rawBrowser` entirely and keep only the explicit target.\n\n\n[Duplicated AI-agent prompt block omitted from this display; full original retained.]\n\n\n```suggestion\n  target: \"chromium-mv3\",\n```\n\n✅ Addressed in [`fec011e`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/fec011e7c940d9ddc09b282f33007d9c3ec1aca9)\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNogq resolved=True outdated=True extfn/docs/content/docs/reference/scan.md\nComment PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM70--jE\n<!-- cubic:v=a9d6e688-119d-4687-a6a6-0d831dce355a -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=89d77ea6-21bc-5bb6-986a-2332a2024346 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":8} -->\nP3: The example for a custom report directory does not produce the report at the path shown. `resolveReportDir` in extfn/cli/src/commands/scan.ts resolves a relative `--report-dir` against `path.resolve(outDir, '..')` — the extension config directory — so running this command from the repo root writes the report to `extfn/examples/svelte-datafn-demo/extfn/examples/svelte-datafn-demo/dist/custom-scan/chromium-mv3.json` (the path is duplicated, since the example path already starts with `extfn/...`), not to `extfn/examples/svelte-datafn-demo/dist/custom-scan`. Use a path relative to the config directory instead, or note the base for relative `--report-dir` values.\n\n\n[Duplicated AI-agent prompt block omitted from this display; full original retained.]\n\n\n```suggestion\nnpm exec extfn scan -- --config extfn/examples/svelte-datafn-demo/extfn.config.ts --report-dir dist/custom-scan\n```\n\n✅ Addressed in [`fec011e`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/fec011e7c940d9ddc09b282f33007d9c3ec1aca9)\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNogr resolved=True outdated=False extfn/docs/tsconfig.json\nComment PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM70--jF\n<!-- cubic:v=7a2a8015-60df-4d71-81b5-0be4f103424f -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=89d77ea6-21bc-5bb6-986a-2332a2024346 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":5} -->\nP3: `types` restricts global type inclusion to `svelte` and `vite/client`, so `@types/node` (hoisted at the workspace root) is not loaded. With `checkJs: true` and `svelte.config.js` in `include`, `svelte-check`/`tsc`/editors will flag `process` in `svelte.config.js` (\"Cannot find name 'process'\"); `vite.config.ts`'s `node:path`/`node:url` imports also depend on `@types/node` being present. Either drop the `types` array so `@types/*` packages auto-load, or add `node` to the list.\n\n\n[Duplicated AI-agent prompt block omitted from this display; full original retained.]\n\n\n```suggestion\n    \"types\": [\n      \"svelte\",\n      \"vite/client\",\n      \"node\"\n    ]\n```\n\n✅ Addressed in [`fec011e`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/fec011e7c940d9ddc09b282f33007d9c3ec1aca9)\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNpbG resolved=True outdated=False extfn/docs/package.json\nComment PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM70-__F\n**Security issue**  \n🛑 Blocker — must fix before merge\n\n**Known vulnerabilities in svelte@5.0.0**\n\nOSV.dev reports 6 known vulnerabilities affecting `svelte@5.0.0`, introduced by this PR:\n\n- [GHSA-crpf-4hrx-3jrp](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-27125) **moderate**: Svelte SSR attribute spreading includes inherited properties from prototype chain — fixed in 5.51.5\n- [GHSA-f7gr-6p89-r883](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-27121) **moderate**: Svelte affected by cross-site scripting via spread attributes in Svelte SSR — fixed in 5.51.5\n- [GHSA-m56q-vw4c-c2cp](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-27122) **moderate**: Svelte SSR does not validate dynamic element tag names in `<svelte:element>` — fixed in 5.51.5\n\n…and 3 more — see the OSV links above.\n\nUpgrade to 5.51.5 or later.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn extfn/docs/package.json, upgrade the dependency svelte from 5.0.0 to a non-vulnerable version (5.51.5, 5.53.5, 5.55.7). Update any associated lockfile entries.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n> Not useful? Reply `@mira-rhombus reject` to dismiss this suggestion.\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNvgO resolved=True outdated=True extfn/docs/src/lib/components/DocsSiteSearch.svelte\nComment PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM70_J0X\nIn Cloudflare mode, the repo's docs Worker route matches only `/docs*`, so this absolute `/search.json` request bypasses the Worker that serves the new search endpoint. Search will fail on a docs host using the existing deployment pattern, even if the page under `/docs` loads.\n\n<details><summary>Technical details</summary>\n\n````markdown\n# Search endpoint outside Cloudflare route\n\n## Affected sites\n- `extfn/docs/src/lib/components/DocsSiteSearch.svelte:5` — fetches `/search.json`.\n- `extfn/docs/src/routes/search.json/+server.ts:5-8` — registers the handler at `/search.json`.\n- `scripts/cloudflare-docs/config.mjs:101-108` — Worker pattern is `${host}/docs*`.\n\n## Required outcome\n- Keep the search request and server endpoint within the configured Worker route, or explicitly route the root endpoint to the same Worker when ExtFn is deployed.\n````\n\n</details>\n\nComment PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM71COA6\nAddressed in fec011e by moving both the search fetch and endpoint under /docs/search.json.\n\n<!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ -->\n<sup><a href=\"https://pullfrog.com\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\"><img src=\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\" width=\"9px\" height=\"9px\" style=\"vertical-align: middle; \" alt=\"Pullfrog\"></picture></a>&nbsp;&nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/36233492935/job/108380936639) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)</sup>\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNvgQ resolved=True outdated=True extfn/docs/content/docs/reference/consumer-host-abstraction.md\nComment PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM70_J0b\nThe guide includes content mounts as consumers of this host, but content scripts cannot call `tabs.create` directly ([MDN](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Mozilla/Add-ons/WebExtensions/Content_scripts#webextension_apis)). A shared panel using this `goto()` from a content mount will reject with `E_CONTEXT_UNAVAILABLE` instead of navigating.\n\n<details><summary>Technical details</summary>\n\n````markdown\n# Navigation in content mounts\n\n## Affected sites\n- `extfn/docs/content/docs/reference/consumer-host-abstraction.md:16-20,90-94` — the example applies one adapter to pages and content mounts.\n- `extfn/core/src/runtime/browser.ts:31-42` — missing browser methods reject with `E_CONTEXT_UNAVAILABLE`.\n\n[958 more lines in file. Use offset=361 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1791369122889}}
{"type":"message","id":"c72a22e1","parentId":"7b9f2193","timestamp":"2026-10-07T10:32:02.889Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_J5ETtazcbUJBZkmyINP6AFCX|fc_055fb762f51dfcfc016ac61fa2adc887d09f13441e7e4e2a05","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"- `extfn/docs/consumer-host-abstraction.md:85-91` — the mirrored root guide has the same example.\n\n## Required outcome\n- Show a navigation adapter valid for the contexts the guide promises, or explicitly scope this adapter to extension pages and show content mounts relaying privileged tab creation through a background handler. Keep the mirrored guide aligned.\n````\n\n</details>\n\nComment PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM71CN6C\nAddressed in fec011e by routing content navigation through the host page and extension-page tab creation through the browser facade.\n\n<!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ -->\n<sup><a href=\"https://pullfrog.com\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\"><img src=\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\" width=\"9px\" height=\"9px\" style=\"vertical-align: middle; \" alt=\"Pullfrog\"></picture></a>&nbsp;&nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/36233492935/job/108380936639) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)</sup>\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNvgR resolved=True outdated=True extfn/docs/content/docs/reference/consumer-host-abstraction.md\nComment PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM70_J0d\n`runtime.address.context` is a context label such as `\"popup\"` or `\"content\"`, not the current URL pathname returned by the SvelteKit adapter above. Shared route-aware UI using the stated `currentPath()` contract will see the wrong location in extension surfaces.\n\n<details><summary>Technical details</summary>\n\n````markdown\n# Extension currentPath contract\n\n## Affected sites\n- `extfn/docs/content/docs/reference/consumer-host-abstraction.md:29-31,64-66,95-97` — interface and web adapter describe a pathname but extension adapter returns a context enum.\n- `extfn/core/src/runtime/context.ts:4-17` — `RuntimeAddress.context` is a context kind.\n- `extfn/docs/consumer-host-abstraction.md:90-92` — the mirrored root guide has the same mismatch.\n\n## Required outcome\n- Make `currentPath()` represent an actual pathname in both host adapters, or change the host contract and both implementations to explicitly model different navigation semantics. Keep the mirrored guide aligned.\n````\n\n</details>\n\nComment PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM71CN9N\nAddressed in fec011e by returning the document pathname in both mirrored guides.\n\n<!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ -->\n<sup><a href=\"https://pullfrog.com\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\"><img src=\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\" width=\"9px\" height=\"9px\" style=\"vertical-align: middle; \" alt=\"Pullfrog\"></picture></a>&nbsp;&nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/36233492935/job/108380936639) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)</sup>\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNzqx resolved=False outdated=False scripts/docs-site/runtime.ts\nComment PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM70_Qhn\n<!-- cubic:v=28db2e6a-2b9a-4df3-9915-24b920947e35 -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=062ac4fa-f9cd-5b7a-bd4b-d89f86693fc7 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":7} -->\nP1: This Node-only import breaks the documented Cloudflare opt-in unless every deployment enables `nodejs_compat`. Replace the path dependency with edge-safe POSIX path helpers, or make the Cloudflare configuration explicitly and verifiably enable the required compatibility flag.\n\n\n[Duplicated AI-agent prompt block omitted from this display; full original retained.]\n\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNzq1 resolved=True outdated=True extfn/docs/src/app.css\nComment PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM70_Qhu\n<!-- cubic:v=14c062be-3481-4a31-a39d-5f10b50ad1b2 -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=062ac4fa-f9cd-5b7a-bd4b-d89f86693fc7 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":5} -->\nP2: This rule wins only if the theme hides the mobile sidebar with `display: none` on the `.docsfn-sidebar-col` element itself; if the theme hides the drawer via visibility, transform, width/grid collapse, or a `--open` class on a wrapper element, `display: block` never re-shows it, and showing it inline in flow doesn't make it an overlay drawer. It also pins the site to theme internals and duplicates a 1023px magic breakpoint that can silently drift on a `@docsfn/svelte` upgrade. Verify the override against the installed theme.css (confirm the hide mechanism and where `--open` is toggled) and note the version + the theme rule this mirrors near this code so a future upgrade is caught; ideally drive open state through the theme's own drawer handling instead of a specificity patch.\n\n\n[Duplicated AI-agent prompt block omitted from this display; full original retained.]\n\n\n✅ Addressed in [`fec011e`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/fec011e7c940d9ddc09b282f33007d9c3ec1aca9)\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNzq4 resolved=True outdated=True extfn/docs/vite.config.ts\nComment PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM70_Qhz\n<!-- cubic:v=2151a600-133d-49d5-8309-4c7fc40830c0 -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=062ac4fa-f9cd-5b7a-bd4b-d89f86693fc7 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":8} -->\nP2: These aliases rely on synchronous `import.meta.resolve`, which only exists unflagged from Node 18.19.0/20.6.0, but the root `engines` floor is `>=18.17.0`. On Node 18.17-18.18 the config file throws during load, breaking `vite dev` and `vite build` for those versions. Use `createRequire(import.meta.url).resolve(...)` (Node 12.2+, sync, Windows-safe) instead of `import.meta.resolve`, matching the existing `dirname` pattern.\n\n\n[Duplicated AI-agent prompt block omitted from this display; full original retained.]\n\n\n✅ Addressed in [`fec011e`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/fec011e7c940d9ddc09b282f33007d9c3ec1aca9)\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNz7d resolved=False outdated=True extfn/docs/content/docs/reference/consumer-host-abstraction.md\nComment PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM70_Q56\n**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Return the actual pathname from the extension host**\n\nWhen shared components use `currentPath()` for routing or active-navigation state, this adapter returns an ExtFn context identifier such as `\"popup\"` or `\"content\"`, not the URL pathname returned by the SvelteKit implementation above. This makes the two implementations of `NavigationHost` observably incompatible; read the extension page's actual pathname (or explicitly redefine the interface around context identifiers) instead.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mN94Z resolved=True outdated=True extfn/docs/src/app.css\nComment PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM70_gm0\nThe override makes the mobile sidebar visible, but the pinned DocsFn drawer is fixed at `top: 0` with `z-index: 40`, while `TopBar` remains sticky at `z-index: 50`. The header therefore covers the beginning of the sidebar, including its first navigation entries, so mobile readers cannot reach them normally.\n\n<details><summary>Technical details</summary>\n\n````markdown\n# Mobile drawer hidden beneath header\n\n## Affected sites\n- `extfn/docs/src/app.css:75-77` — the new override reveals the drawer without accounting for its position beneath the top bar.\n- `@docsfn/svelte@0.0.3/src/DocsLayout.svelte` — mobile sidebar is fixed at top: 0 with z-index: 40, and backdrop uses z-index: 30.\n- `@docsfn/svelte@0.0.3/dist/theme-base.css` — sticky top bar uses z-index: 50.\n\n## Required outcome\n- Keep the opened sidebar's first links visible and clickable at mobile widths, whether by stacking the drawer above the header or offsetting the drawer below it.\n````\n\n</details>\n\nComment PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM71CODO\nAddressed in fec011e by offsetting the open drawer below the measured top bar and reducing its viewport height.\n\n<!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ -->\n<sup><a href=\"https://pullfrog.com\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\"><img src=\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\" width=\"9px\" height=\"9px\" style=\"vertical-align: middle; \" alt=\"Pullfrog\"></picture></a>&nbsp;&nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/36233492935/job/108380936639) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)</sup>\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mPpj0 resolved=False outdated=True extfn/docs/svelte.config.js\nComment PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM71CIqM\n<!-- cubic:v=9c522afc-2e6e-450e-96f8-453fb7748a37 -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=804fce71-3bb1-546d-b7cc-49349a868699 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":8} -->\nP3: This `@site/docs-search` alias duplicates the exact same mapping already defined in `extfn/docs/vite.config.ts` (`resolve.alias` with `find: \"@site/docs-search\"` → `path.resolve(dirname, \"../../scripts/docs-site/Search.svelte\")`). Both feed the same Vite resolve pipeline, so the `kit.alias` entry is redundant, and the two definitions already use different path forms (relative string vs `path.resolve`) that can drift. The sibling sites (`authfn/docs`, `filefn/docs`) keep all `@site/*` aliases solely in `vite.config.ts` and use no `kit.alias`. Keep exactly one definition.\n\n\n[Duplicated AI-agent prompt block omitted from this display; full original retained.]\n\n[838 more lines in file. Use offset=481 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1791369122889}}
{"type":"message","id":"d76d755c","parentId":"c72a22e1","timestamp":"2026-10-07T10:32:02.890Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_tI6y9SPl1A2srl7wXTDHKTeR|fc_055fb762f51dfcfc016ac61fa2add887d0a247c657c9527d04","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mPpj3 resolved=True outdated=True extfn/docs/README.md\nComment PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM71CIqQ\n<!-- cubic:v=ace3b9ec-0634-4982-8cca-e55e460eff94 -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=804fce71-3bb1-546d-b7cc-49349a868699 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":8} -->\nP3: The closing prose line is indented with two spaces, so it visually attaches to the preceding code fence and reads as a continuation of the shell block. Remove the leading indentation to restore it to a normal paragraph.\n\n\n[Duplicated AI-agent prompt block omitted from this display; full original retained.]\n\n\n```suggestion\nThe site defaults to port 6015. Set `site.canonicalUrl` in `docsfn.config.ts` after the public host is assigned.\n```\n\n✅ Addressed in [`dd11b96`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/dd11b96aea70743b7838ae7e5dd5e467c1ec2f64)\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mPpj- resolved=True outdated=True scripts/docs-site/layout.ts\nComment PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM71CIqa\n<!-- cubic:v=26e2d91d-2cd4-4e2d-a9de-da3646bb3536 -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=804fce71-3bb1-546d-b7cc-49349a868699 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":6} -->\nP3: `observeTopBar` silently returns a no-op when `.docsfn-topbar` isn't found, leaving the hardcoded `--docsfn-sticky-top-offset: 4rem` fallback in `extfn/docs/src/app.css` in effect — the same wrapped-mobile-links mismatch this helper exists to correct. TopBar is always rendered today, but this is shared runtime code that new site PRs copy (per `scripts/docs-site/README.md`), so a selector or theme-class drift would degrade the sticky drawer with no diagnosable signal. Log a warning from the no-op path so the fallback is observable.\n\n\n[Duplicated AI-agent prompt block omitted from this display; full original retained.]\n\n\n✅ Addressed in [`d10fbdb`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/d10fbdba0d2b61cc5beaff8741e914a24a72e215)\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mPpkC resolved=True outdated=False extfn/docs/src/app.css\nComment PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM71CIqg\n<!-- cubic:v=d98941ad-d77c-4487-9750-750d4c609faa -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=804fce71-3bb1-546d-b7cc-49349a868699 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":6} -->\nP3: `height: calc(100dvh - ...)` has no `vh` fallback. On engines without `dvh` support the declaration is dropped, so the open drawer keeps the theme's full-height sizing while gaining the new `top` offset, pushing its bottom edge past the viewport and making the last nav items unreachable. Add a `100vh` fallback line before the `dvh` one.\n\n\n[Duplicated AI-agent prompt block omitted from this display; full original retained.]\n\n\n```suggestion\n    height: calc(100vh - var(--docsfn-sticky-top-offset));\n    height: calc(100dvh - var(--docsfn-sticky-top-offset));\n```\n\n✅ Addressed in [`8c1af41`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/8c1af4123a41b110375feb5aa98a4b68ad5f76b9)\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mPrKM resolved=True outdated=False extfn/docs/package.json\nComment PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM71CK8M\n**Security issue**  \n🛑 Blocker — must fix before merge\n\n**Known vulnerabilities in vite@5.4.0**\n\nOSV.dev reports 15 known vulnerabilities affecting `vite@5.4.0`, introduced by this PR:\n\n- [GHSA-356w-63v5-8wf4](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-32395) **moderate**: Vite has an `server.fs.deny` bypass with an invalid `request-target` — fixed in 6.2.6, 6.1.5, 6.0.15, 5.4.18, 4.5.13\n- [GHSA-4r4m-qw57-chr8](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-31125) **moderate**: Vite has a `server.fs.deny` bypassed for `inline` and `raw` with `?import` query — fixed in 6.2.4, 6.1.3, 6.0.13, 5.4.16, 4.5.11\n- [GHSA-4w7w-66w2-5vf9](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-39365) **moderate**: Vite Vulnerable to Path Traversal in Optimized Deps `.map` Handling — fixed in 8.0.5, 7.3.2, 6.4.2\n\n…and 12 more — see the OSV links above.\n\nUpgrade to 6.2.6, 6.1.5, 6.0.15, 5.4.18, 4.5.13 or later.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn extfn/docs/package.json, upgrade the dependency vite from 5.4.0 to a non-vulnerable version (0.1.24, 2.14.1, 2.9.0, 3.2.11, 4.5.10, 4.5.11, 4.5.12, 4.5.13, 4.5.14, 4.5.4, 4.5.6, 5.2.14, 5.3.6, 5.4.12, 5.4.15, 5.4.16, 5.4.17, 5.4.18, 5.4.19, 5.4.20, 5.4.21, 5.4.6, 5.4.9, 6.0.12, 6.0.13, 6.0.14, 6.0.15, 6.0.9, 6.1.2, 6.1.3, 6.1.4, 6.1.5, 6.1.6, 6.2.3, 6.2.4, 6.2.5, 6.2.6, 6.2.7, 6.3.4, 6.3.6, 6.4.1, 6.4.2, 6.4.3, 7.0.7, 7.0.8, 7.1.11, 7.1.5, 7.3.2, 7.3.5, 8.0.16, 8.0.5). Update any associated lockfile entries.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n> Not useful? Reply `@mira-rhombus reject` to dismiss this suggestion.\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mPs38 resolved=False outdated=False scripts/docs-site/layout.ts\nComment PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM71CNfi\n## Superfluous trailing arguments\n\n<p>Superfluous argument passed to <a class=\"Link\" href=\"/21nCo/super-functions/blob/fec011e7c940d9ddc09b282f33007d9c3ec1aca9/scripts/verify-uifn-react-18-runtime.mjs#L49-L49\">default constructor of anonymous class</a>.</p>\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mP2_J resolved=True outdated=True scripts/docs-site/README.md\nComment PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM71CdEF\n<!-- cubic:v=20ac4afe-88a5-41e5-947e-3a8cc4aac7a3 -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=7c66403b-fcbb-598b-9cd0-5dfbd7ebe6ff -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":10} -->\nP2: This says all factory wrappers use the canonical runtime, but AuthFn and FileFn still define local `docs-site-source.ts` copies and do not import `scripts/docs-site/runtime`. Following this guidance will make shared runtime edits silently miss those sites; document the exceptions or migrate them first.\n\n\n[Duplicated AI-agent prompt block omitted from this display; full original retained.]\n\n\n```suggestion\nEach new-site PR includes this shared directory at the same repository path so it can land independently. Wrappers that import it use this canonical runtime; AuthFn and FileFn still retain local copies until their migrations land. After merge, edit it directly rather than duplicating provider logic in individual sites.\n```\n\n✅ Addressed in [`d10fbdb`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/d10fbdba0d2b61cc5beaff8741e914a24a72e215)\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mP2_K resolved=True outdated=True extfn/docs/src/lib/server/docs-site-source.ts\nComment PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM71CdEG\n<!-- cubic:v=ca7a4445-73b0-46e2-b116-b0263d12dfb5 -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=7c66403b-fcbb-598b-9cd0-5dfbd7ebe6ff -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":6} -->\nP3: This glob restrictively narrows the bundled static assets to .txt/.json/.md, but `createDocsSiteRuntime` treats every file under `static/` as an asset entry (extension-agnostic `createAssetEntry`), so any future non-listed asset (e.g. .svg, .png, .xml, .webmanifest) added to `extfn/docs/static` will silently disappear from the manifest's assets collection with no error. The change also diverges from the sibling sites `authfn/docs/src/lib/server/docs-site-source.ts:30` and `filefn/docs/src/lib/server/docs-site-source.ts:30`, which both use the unrestricted `static/**/*` glob. Keep the unrestricted glob (matching the other sites) or add a comment documenting why only these three types are intended.\n\n\n[Duplicated AI-agent prompt block omitted from this display; full original retained.]\n\n\n```suggestion\nconst assets = import.meta.glob(\"../../../static/**/*\", {\n```\n\n✅ Addressed in [`d10fbdb`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/d10fbdba0d2b61cc5beaff8741e914a24a72e215)\n\n\n[718 more lines in file. Use offset=601 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1791369122890}}
